{"parentUuid":"20958be3-dd9f-47f1-8d5b-66b50ab3b5f7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezwSb1zobQnH5Ti19BRp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011roGdDQxZwXvUDNAt9BR7W","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md","old_string":"- **Bloat.** List every canonical skill never invoked across all sessions\n  (`never_used` from the metrics; name them).\n- **Crutch test.** For each never-used and once-used skill, answer the `rot.md`\n  question — *would the current model do this fine without it?* Recommend\n  DELETE, KEEP (tacit knowledge the model cannot know), or SEASONAL. One line of\n  reasoning each.","new_string":"- **Bloat.** List every canonical skill never invoked in Claude Code transcripts\n  (`never_used` from the metrics; name them). Its scope is\n  `usage_scope=claude_code_transcripts_only`: Codex and Pi use is not counted.\n  If `usage_unreadable_transcripts` is above 0, say so — the list may be too long.\n- **Crutch test.** For each never-used and once-used skill, answer the `rot.md`\n  question — *would the current model do this fine without it?* Recommend\n  DELETE, KEEP (tacit knowledge the model cannot know), or SEASONAL. One line of\n  reasoning each. **Never recommend DELETE on `never_used` alone** — it is\n  Claude-only evidence. First check Codex:\n  `grep -rl \"<skill>/SKILL.md\" ~/.codex/sessions | wc -l`. A non-zero count means\n  the skill may be in use there; report the count. A match can also be a bulk\n  scan of the skills folder, so read one hit before calling it real use."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5347,"cache_read_input_tokens":91076,"output_tokens":3591,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":330},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests"