{"parentUuid":"1c79c031-446c-4fae-ad62-3bac00313415","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88b6ccb8-7105-4de5-afa1-ccbae8a94e54","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011roGdDQxZwXvUDNAt9BR7W","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"f3bca625-a7b6-48fb-8eb7-82402107062b","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:09:08.739Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md","oldString":"- **Bloat.** List every canonical skill never invoked across all sessions\n  (`never_used` from the metrics; name them).\n- **Crutch test.** For each never-used and once-used skill, answer the `rot.md`\n  question — *would the current model do this fine without it?* Recommend\n  DELETE, KEEP (tacit knowledge the model cannot know), or SEASONAL. One line of\n  reasoning each.","newString":"- **Bloat.** List every canonical skill never invoked in Claude Code transcripts\n  (`never_used` from the metrics; name them). Its scope is\n  `usage_scope=claude_code_transcripts_only`: Codex and Pi use is not counted.\n  If `usage_unreadable_transcripts` is above 0, say so — the list may be too long.\n- **Crutch test.** For each never-used and once-used skill, answer the `rot.md`\n  question — *would the current model do this fine without it?* Recommend\n  DELETE, KEEP (tacit knowledge the model cannot know), or SEASONAL. One line of\n  reasoning each. **Never recommend DELETE on `never_used` alone** — it is\n  Claude-only evidence. First check Codex:\n  `grep -rl \"<skill>/SKILL.md\" ~/.codex/sessions | wc -l`. A non-zero count means\n  the skill may be in use there; report the count. A match can also be a bulk\n  scan of the skills folder, so read one hit before calling it real use.","originalFile":"---\nname: aios-audit\ndescription: >-\n  Audit the whole AI operating system across decay tiers - skills, agents,\n  hooks, rules, memory, and cross-harness parity between Claude Code, Codex,\n  and Pi - then propose exactly two next builds. Use when the user says\n  \"/aios-audit\", \"audit my system\", \"audit my AI OS\", \"audit the bloat\",\n  \"is my setup rotting\", \"what should I cut\", \"are my skills portable\",\n  \"monthly skill audit\", or when rot.md shows a layer past its audit date.\n  Do not use for project data drift, routing, or index freshness - use\n  os-audit. Do not use for launchd, venv, or backup health - use\n  claude-stack-doctor. Do not use for SecondBrain note rot - use\n  improve-system or brain-audit.\nmetadata:\n  short-description: Decay-tier audit of the AI OS; delegates to the five layer-specific audit skills.\nargument-hint: \"[optional: a layer name from rot.md]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Agent\n---\n\n# AIOS Audit — is the harness itself still true?\n\nFive audit skills already exist, and each owns one layer. This skill owns the\nlayer none of them touch: **the harness** — skill roster, agents, hooks, rules,\nagent memory, and parity between Claude Code, Codex, and Pi. For every other\nlayer it **delegates**; it never re-implements another audit.\n\n| Delegate | Owns |\n|---|---|\n| `os-audit` (project) | project data: routing, index truth, freshness, duplication |\n| `brain-audit` | SecondBrain as a system — the four C's |\n| `improve-system` | note-level rot: stale seeds, duplicates, conflicts |\n| `claude-stack-doctor` | automation plumbing: launchd, venvs, memsearch, backup freshness |\n| `doctor-plus` | context-engineering posture of the workspace |\n\nIf `$ARGUMENTS` names one layer from `rot.md`, audit only that layer.\n\n## 1. Read-only\n\nThe only writes are the report file and the `Last audited` column of\n`~/.claude/rot.md`. **Never delete, archive, disable, or edit a skill during the\naudit.** Propose, then wait for approval. A deletion proposal that turns out wrong\nis cheap; a deletion is not.\n\n## 2. Step 0 — read `~/.claude/rot.md`\n\nFor each layer, compute days since `Last audited`. A layer that is **past due or\n`unknown`** is audited this run. A layer inside its window is reported green and\nskipped — that is what keeps a monthly run cheap. Read the delegation contract and\nthe layout invariants in `rot.md` before going further; they bind every step below.\n\n## 3. Step 1 — run the metrics\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py\n```\n\nCapture every `key=value` line. Any stack trace, or a value like `git_error`,\n`no_manifest` or `error_rc…`, is itself a RED finding — do not guess the number.\n\n## 4. Step 2 — assert the layout invariants\n\n| Key | Must be | If not |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical` | `0` | RED — a link was committed; Windows gets a dead file |\n| `pool_view_drift`, `codex_view_drift` | `0` | RED — someone edited a generated view instead of `~/.claude/skills/` |\n| `pool_dangling`, `codex_dangling` | `0` | RED — a deleted canonical skill left an abandoned link |\n| `portability_failures` | `0` | RED — see the parity check in Step 4 |\n\nInformation, never findings: `third_party_links_in_canonical` (changes with every\ninstall), `pool_third_party`, `codex_third_party` (deliberately preserved installs).\n\n## 5. Step 3 — delegate under the contract\n\nFor each due layer, invoke the owner named in `rot.md`, **read-only**:\n\n- Say it plainly in the invocation: *report findings only; apply nothing, write no\n  ledger, create no files.*\n- `improve-system` applies previously approved proposals in its own Step 0 —\n  suppress that explicitly. `brain-audit` appends to its own trend table — suppress\n  that too, or leave the Vault layer `unknown`.\n- Name the scope you need. Fold the delegate's findings under that layer's heading.\n- A receipt covers only what was checked. If the delegate covered less than its\n  row claims, write the date **with a scope note**, or leave the row `unknown`.\n  Never stamp a date because a delegate exited cleanly.\n\nThe Memory (agent) layer has no delegate — audit it directly: every `MEMORY.md`\nindex line resolves to a file; every memory file appears in its index;\n`~/.claude/global-memory/MEMORY.md` is under 2,500 chars; flag time-dimensioned\nfacts (counters, \"still open\", past-tense futures).\n\n## 6. Step 4 — the harness layer, audited directly\n\n- **Bloat.** List every canonical skill never invoked across all sessions\n  (`never_used` from the metrics; name them).\n- **Crutch test.** For each never-used and once-used skill, answer the `rot.md`\n  question — *would the current model do this fine without it?* Recommend\n  DELETE, KEEP (tacit knowledge the model cannot know), or SEASONAL. One line of\n  reasoning each.\n- **Overlap.** Skills whose descriptions claim the same trigger space. Recommend\n  a merge, or a sharper `Do not use … (use X)` clause on both.\n- **Parity.** Run `python3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skill-portability-check.py`;\n  every failure is a finding. Then check config-level parity, which the linter\n  cannot see: list canonical skills set `\"off\"` in `~/.claude/settings.json`\n  `skillOverrides`. Those are hidden in Claude Code but live in Codex and Pi.\n  Each one needs a decision: switch it back on, or retire it from canonical.\n- **Promotion.** Global skills used in fewer than 2 projects — demotion\n  candidates. Project skills used in 2+ projects — promotion candidates.\n- **Rules.** Diff `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` against the last 7 days of sessions.\n  Report rules contradicted by what actually happened, and corrections the user\n  repeated twice that are not yet rules.\n- **Hooks.** Compare `hooks_claude` with `hooks_codex`, then diff the two\n  directories by name. The copies must match (patch both, always).\n- **Agents.** If `agents=0`, report \"no agents defined\" and skip. Do not invent a finding.\n\n## 7. Step 5 — write the report\n\nWrite `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-audit-YYYY-MM-DD.md` with one section per\nlayer (green-skipped layers get one line). Update `Last audited` in\n`~/.claude/rot.md` **only for layers whose check actually ran and produced\noutput**, then `cp ~/.claude/rot.md ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/rot.md`.\n\nDo **not** write to `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` — `scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh` is\nits single writer. If the cron left an uncommitted trend row, commit it together\nwith this report.\n\n## 8. Step 6 — end with exactly two proposed next builds\n\nRanked. Each with the one command or sentence that starts it. Not ten. Two.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Monthly nudge**\n```\nUser: \"audit my AI OS\"\n→ reads rot.md: Skills and Rules past due, Hooks inside its window\n→ metrics: all invariants 0; never_used=19\n→ delegates nothing for Skills/Rules (owned here); skips Hooks green\n→ report with crutch-test verdicts, 2 parity decisions, 2 next builds\n```\n\n**One layer**\n```\nUser: \"/aios-audit Memory (agent)\"\n→ audits only the agent-memory stores directly\n→ stamps that one row in rot.md; every other row untouched\n```\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- **Linter green is not parity.** `skill-portability-check.py` reads frontmatter\n  only. A skill set `\"off\"` in `skillOverrides` passes it and still never fires in\n  Claude Code, while Codex (which ignores that file) loads it. Found 2026-09-12:\n  12 canonical skills off in Claude, live in Codex.\n- **Views are links into canonical.** Anything that writes into\n  `~/.agents/skills/<owned>/` by path writes canonical. `graphify install\n  --platform agents` does exactly that and overwrites the Claude variant — upgrade\n  graphify with `--platform claude` only.\n- **Concurrent sessions commit your work.** `closeout` in another session sweeps\n  every uncommitted change in the repos it visits. Commit the report as soon as it\n  is written, not at the end of a long session.\n- **Description length has a budget.** Claude Code caps the combined skill\n  description size; very long descriptions risk a skill silently dropping out of\n  the listing. When recommending a sharper `Do not use` clause, keep the whole\n  description near 650 characters.\n- **`dcg` blocks some shell shapes** (`rm -rf` inside heredocs, `$VAR` redirects,\n  `git` inside command substitution). Use Python `subprocess` or literal paths;\n  do not try to bypass the guard.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":90,"oldLines":12,"newStart":90,"newLines":18,"lines":[" "," ## 6. Step 4 — the harness layer, audited directly"," ","-- **Bloat.** List every canonical skill never invoked across all sessions","-  (`never_used` from the metrics; name them).","+- **Bloat.** List every canonical skill never invoked in Claude Code transcripts","+  (`never_used` from the metrics; name them). Its scope is","+  `usage_scope=claude_code_transcripts_only`: Codex and Pi use is not counted.","+  If `usage_unreadable_transcripts` is above 0, say so — the list may be too long."," - **Crutch test.** For each never-used and once-used skill, answer the `rot.md`","   question — *would the current model do this fine without it?* Recommend","   DELETE, KEEP (tacit knowledge the model cannot know), or SEASONAL. One line of","-  reasoning each.","+  reasoning each. **Never recommend DELETE on `never_used` alone** — it is","+  Claude-only evidence. First check Codex:","+  `grep -rl \"<skill>/SKILL.md\" ~/.codex/sessions | wc -l`. A non-zero count means","+  the skill may be in use there; report the count. A match can also be a bulk","+  scan of the skills folder, so read one hit before calling it real use."," - **Overlap.** Skills whose descriptions claim the same trigger space. Recommend","   a merge, or a sharper `Do not use … (use X)` clause on both."," - **Parity.** Run `python3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skill-portability-check.py`;"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1c79c031-446c-4fae-ad62-3bac00313415","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f3bca625-a7b6-48fb-8eb7-82402107062b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezwSb1zobQnH5Ti19BRp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XoV3yTdM16omDR6ZWVUcPv","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t7-failpaths.py","old_string":"def clear_lock():\n    if os.path.isdir(LOCK):\n        for n in os.listdir(LOCK):\n            os.remove(os.path.join(LOCK, n))\n        os.rmdir(LOCK)\n\ndef run():\n    return subprocess.run([CRON], capture_output=True, text=True).returncode","new_string":"RECOVER = LOCK + \".recover\"\n\ndef clear_dir(p):\n    if os.path.isdir(p):\n        for n in os.listdir(p):\n            os.remove(os.path.join(p, n))\n        os.rmdir(p)\n\ndef clear_lock():\n    clear_dir(LOCK)\n    clear_dir(RECOVER)\n\ndef run():\n    return subprocess.run([CRON], capture_output=True, text=True).returncode\n\ndef stale_lock():\n    clear_lock()\n    os.mkdir(LOCK)\n    open(f\"{LOCK}/pid\", \"w\").write(\"999999\")               # a pid that cannot exist"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5347,"cache_read_input_tokens":91076,"output_tokens":3591,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":330},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5347,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":3591,"cache_read_input_tokens":91076,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5347},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":6,"requestId":"req_011CezwSWXs7fsCn89ByLCwL","type":"assistant","uuid":"c91a1c66-9b1c-46d2-bdcc-61daa249702f","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:09:09.748Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c91a1c66-9b1c-46d2-bdcc-61daa249702f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88b6ccb8-7105-4de5-afa1-ccbae8a94e54","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XoV3yTdM16omDR6ZWVUcPv","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t7-failpaths.py has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"73af30a5-9543-4b6a-bd59-ef44b6bdf15f","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:09:11.050Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t7-failpaths.py","oldString":"def clear_lock():\n    if os.path.isdir(LOCK):\n        for n in os.listdir(LOCK):\n            os.remove(os.path.join(LOCK, n))\n        os.rmdir(LOCK)\n\ndef run():\n    return subprocess.run([CRON], capture_output=True, text=True).returncode","newString":"RECOVER = LOCK + \".recover\"\n\ndef clear_dir(p):\n    if os.path.isdir(p):\n        for n in os.listdir(p):\n            os.remove(os.path.join(p, n))\n        os.rmdir(p)\n\ndef clear_lock():\n    clear_dir(LOCK)\n    clear_dir(RECOVER)\n\ndef run():\n    return subprocess.run([CRON], capture_output=True, text=True).returncode\n\ndef stale_lock():\n    clear_lock()\n    os.mkdir(LOCK)\n    open(f\"{LOCK}/pid\", \"w\").write(\"999999\")               # a pid that cannot exist","originalFile":"\"\"\"Task 7 Step 3: prove the cron wrapper's failure paths (plan R9 / R2-06).\nSame three probes as the plan's shell block, done with os calls because dcg\nblocks `mv`/`rm -rf` on variable paths.\"\"\"\nimport os, subprocess, time\n\nK = \"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS\"\nCRON = f\"{K}/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh\"\nMET = f\"{K}/scripts/aios-metrics.py\"\nBAK = \"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t7-aios-metrics.bak\"\nTREND = f\"{K}/docs/audits/aios-trend.md\"\nLOG = \"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/scripts/logs/aios-audit.log\"\nLOCK = \"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/scripts/.aios-audit.lock\"\n\ndef rows():\n    return sum(1 for l in open(TREND) if l.startswith(\"| 20\"))\n\ndef log_tail_from(offset):\n    with open(LOG) as f:\n        f.seek(offset)\n        return f.read()\n\ndef clear_lock():\n    if os.path.isdir(LOCK):\n        for n in os.listdir(LOCK):\n            os.remove(os.path.join(LOCK, n))\n        os.rmdir(LOCK)\n\ndef run():\n    return subprocess.run([CRON], capture_output=True, text=True).returncode\n\nok_all = True\ndef report(label, good, detail):\n    global ok_all\n    ok_all &= good\n    print(f\"{'PASS' if good else 'FAIL'} {label}: {detail}\")\n\n# 1. Missing metrics script must fail the job and add no row.\nr0, off = rows(), os.path.getsize(LOG)\nos.rename(MET, BAK)\ntry:\n    rc = run()\nfinally:\n    os.rename(BAK, MET)\nt = log_tail_from(off)\nreport(\"missing metrics script\", rc == 1 and \"FAIL metrics script errored\" in t and rows() == r0,\n       f\"exit={rc} rows {r0}->{rows()} log_has_FAIL={'FAIL metrics script errored' in t}\")\n\n# 2. A LIVE lock must make the job stand down, no row.\nclear_lock()\nos.mkdir(LOCK)\nopen(f\"{LOCK}/pid\", \"w\").write(str(os.getpid()))          # this process is alive\nr0, off = rows(), os.path.getsize(LOG)\nrc = run()\nt = log_tail_from(off)\nreport(\"live lock\", rc == 0 and \"ABORT live run\" in t and rows() == r0,\n       f\"exit={rc} rows {r0}->{rows()} log_has_ABORT={'ABORT live run' in t}\")\n\n# 3. A STALE lock must be RECLAIMED and one row added.\nclear_lock()\nos.mkdir(LOCK)\nopen(f\"{LOCK}/pid\", \"w\").write(\"999999\")                   # a pid that cannot exist\nr0, off = rows(), os.path.getsize(LOG)\nrc = run()\nt = log_tail_from(off)\nreport(\"stale lock reclaimed\", rc == 0 and \"RECLAIM stale lock\" in t and rows() == r0 + 1,\n       f\"exit={rc} rows {r0}->{rows()} log_has_RECLAIM={'RECLAIM stale lock' in t}\")\nclear_lock()\nreport(\"lock released afterwards\", not os.path.exists(LOCK), f\"lock exists={os.path.exists(LOCK)}\")\nreport(\"metrics script restored\", os.path.isfile(MET) and os.access(MET, os.X_OK), MET)\nprint(\"ALL FAILURE PATHS PASS\" if ok_all else \"SOME FAILURE PATHS FAILED\")\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":19,"oldLines":15,"newStart":19,"newLines":26,"lines":["         f.seek(offset)","         return f.read()"," ","+RECOVER = LOCK + \".recover\"","+","+def clear_dir(p):","+    if os.path.isdir(p):","+        for n in os.listdir(p):","+            os.remove(os.path.join(p, n))","+        os.rmdir(p)","+"," def clear_lock():","-    if os.path.isdir(LOCK):","-        for n in os.listdir(LOCK):","-            os.remove(os.path.join(LOCK, n))","-        os.rmdir(LOCK)","+    clear_dir(LOCK)","+    clear_dir(RECOVER)"," "," def run():","     return subprocess.run([CRON], capture_output=True, text=True).returncode"," ","+def stale_lock():","+    clear_lock()","+    os.mkdir(LOCK)","+    open(f\"{LOCK}/pid\", \"w\").write(\"999999\")               # a pid that cannot exist","+"," ok_all = True"," def report(label, good, detail):","     global ok_all"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c91a1c66-9b1c-46d2-bdcc-61daa249702f","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"73af30a5-9543-4b6a-bd59-ef44b6bdf15f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezwSb1zobQnH5Ti19BRp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xkw5SGuinGZ8RSJK5bKxzo","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t7-failpaths.py","old_string":"clear_lock()\nreport(\"lock released afterwards\", not os.path.exists(LOCK), f\"lock exists={os.path.exists(LOCK)}\")","new_string":"report(\"lock released afterwards\", not os.path.exists(LOCK) and not os.path.exists(RECOVER),\n       f\"lock exists={os.path.exists(LOCK)} recover exists={os.path.exists(RECOVER)}\")\n\n# 4. Gate C C-02: TWO runs on the same stale lock -> exactly one row.\n# AIOS_LOCK_TEST_PAUSE holds the first reclaimer inside the recovery section,\n# so the second run is forced into the interleaving Codex described.\nfor trial, pause in ((\"paused\", \"3\"), (\"unpaused\", \"\")):\n    stale_lock()\n    r0, off = rows(), os.path.getsize(LOG)\n    env = dict(os.environ, AIOS_LOCK_TEST_PAUSE=pause)\n    a = subprocess.Popen([CRON], env=env)\n    time.sleep(0.3 if pause else 0)\n    b = subprocess.Popen([CRON], env=env)\n    rca, rcb = a.wait(), b.wait()\n    t = log_tail_from(off)\n    n_reclaim = t.count(\"RECLAIM stale lock (owner\")\n    leftovers = os.path.exists(LOCK) or os.path.exists(RECOVER)\n    report(f\"concurrent stale lock ({trial})\",\n           rca == 0 and rcb == 0 and rows() == r0 + 1 and n_reclaim == 1 and not leftovers,\n           f\"exit={rca},{rcb} rows {r0}->{rows()} reclaims={n_reclaim} leftovers={leftovers}\")\n\n# 5. A recovery lock older than 10 min is reclaimed; the run proceeds.\nstale_lock()\nos.mkdir(RECOVER)\nold = time.time() - 11 * 60\nos.utime(RECOVER, (old, old))\nr0, off = rows(), os.path.getsize(LOG)\nrc = run()\nt = log_tail_from(off)\nreport(\"stale recovery lock reclaimed\",\n       rc == 0 and \"RECLAIM stale recovery lock\" in t and 