{"parentUuid":"9d154977-efcd-4996-b504-419145bf00d8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88b6ccb8-7105-4de5-afa1-ccbae8a94e54","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CykKj8qqSBSpYWYKkbjeX4","type":"tool_result","content":"# Gate B round 2 dispositions\n\nTwo fresh Codex inspections with the round-1 dispositions as feedback.\nBoth REVISE. Round 2 is the last inspection the claudex-loop budget allows\n(MAX_INSPECTION_ROUNDS = 2), so the fixes below are host-verified but NOT\nindependently re-inspected. A third round needs Eric's go-ahead.\n\nIDs: S2-* = claude-skills inspection, K2-* = KeystoneOS inspection\n(Codex labelled both sets B2-*).\n\n| ID | Sev | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| S2-01 | high | ACCEPTED | Both twins refuse (exit 2, before any mutation, dry runs included) when a view's manifest is a link or not a regular file. The manifest write now goes to a new regular file (bash `mktemp`; PowerShell GUID name), removes the old entry (which deletes a link, never its target), and moves the new file into place. Commit `7459560`. |\n| K2-01 | medium | ACCEPTED | Checker validates the supported YAML subset line by line, nested and list-item lines included: quoted scalars need valid escapes and a closing quote on the same line; only `[a, b]` flow sequences of plain scalars are allowed; flow mappings, anchors, aliases, tags, tab indentation and malformed block headers are rejected. Found and fixed during testing: any empty-valued key (`metadata:`) made every nested line skip validation (`\"\" in \"|>\"` is True), and a list item's sibling key was misread as a continuation. |\n| K2-03 | medium | ACCEPTED | Evidence failures exit 2: settings file present but unreadable or malformed, `skillOverrides` not an object, git probe failing in a repo. Absent settings still mean \"no overrides\". The staged `aios-metrics.py` reports `error_rc<N>` unless the checker exits 0 or 1. |\n| S2-02 / K2-02 | medium | OPEN — Eric's decision | 7 owned skills are `\"off\"` in Claude Code and published to Codex and Pi. The checker fails them. Resolving needs a roster choice (re-enable, or retire from canonical). |\n\n## Executed verification\n\n- Sync, bash 3.2, 13 scratch-HOME cases: all 9 round-1 cases still pass; pool manifest linked to\n  canonical `SKILL.md` → exit 2; codex manifest linked, `DRY_RUN=1` → exit 2; manifest is a\n  directory → exit 2; second normal run → manifests regular files, no temp files left.\n  Canonical `SKILL.md` intact in all 13.\n- PowerShell twin: 0 parse errors; preflight logic refuses a linked manifest; the write logic run\n  against a real symlink leaves the canonical file untouched, leaves a regular manifest with the\n  right content, and no temp file. Windows PowerShell 5.1 not exercised.\n- Real layout: sync exit 0; both manifests regular files, 43 lines, 0 temp files; drift 0/0,\n  dangling 0/0, tracked links 0.\n- Checker: 16/16 fixtures as expected; syntax check agrees with PyYAML on all 42 real skills;\n  real roster 7 failing, all override-only; fail-closed 4/4 exit 2; control exit 0; older\n  fixtures unchanged.\n=== CONTEXT ===\n# Gate C context (host-authored)\n\nScope per the plan's Review Gates section: `scripts/aios-metrics.py`,\n`scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh`, the launchd plist, and the `aios-audit` SKILL.md body.\n\n- The plist is outside this repo: `/Users/kristinarash/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.aiosaudit.plist`\n  (byte-identical to the plan's Task 7 Step 4 block; `plutil -lint` OK; loaded; one run via\n  `launchctl start` exited 0 with an empty stderr file and wrote a trend row).\n- `~/.claude/rot.md` is outside the repo; `docs/rot.md` is its committed copy.\n- Deviations from the plan text, all deliberate:\n  1. `aios-metrics.py` reports `portability_failures=error_rc<N>` unless the checker exits 0 or 1\n     (Gate B round 2, K2-03: evidence failures must not read as a pass).\n  2. The `aios-audit` SKILL.md adds a Parity check of `skillOverrides`, a Hooks name diff, Examples\n     and Gotchas sections beyond the plan's 8 required body parts; the plan's frontmatter is verbatim.\n- Known open item, not a Gate C defect: `portability_failures=7` is the unresolved roster decision\n  (7 owned skills off in Claude Code but published to Codex and Pi), carried from Gate B.\n\nExecuted host verification: metrics script exit 0, key=value only, invariants 0; cron Step 2 run\nexit 0 with a full row and `=== done ok ===`; every wrapper key is emitted by the metrics script;\nfailure paths (missing metrics script exit 1 no row; live lock exit 0 no row; stale lock reclaimed,\nexit 0, one row); launchd-started run exit 0; headless `claude -p \"audit my AI OS\"` in this repo\nlisted and fired `aios-audit`.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c08f55f2-38ea-4673-bc92-8b1ce8abb35a","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:10:22.994Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Gate B round 2 dispositions\n\nTwo fresh Codex inspections with the round-1 dispositions as feedback.\nBoth REVISE. Round 2 is the last inspection the claudex-loop budget allows\n(MAX_INSPECTION_ROUNDS = 2), so the fixes below are host-verified but NOT\nindependently re-inspected. A third round needs Eric's go-ahead.\n\nIDs: S2-* = claude-skills inspection, K2-* = KeystoneOS inspection\n(Codex labelled both sets B2-*).\n\n| ID | Sev | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| S2-01 | high | ACCEPTED | Both twins refuse (exit 2, before any mutation, dry runs included) when a view's manifest is a link or not a regular file. The manifest write now goes to a new regular file (bash `mktemp`; PowerShell GUID name), removes the old entry (which deletes a link, never its target), and moves the new file into place. Commit `7459560`. |\n| K2-01 | medium | ACCEPTED | Checker validates the supported YAML subset line by line, nested and list-item lines included: quoted scalars need valid escapes and a closing quote on the same line; only `[a, b]` flow sequences of plain scalars are allowed; flow mappings, anchors, aliases, tags, tab indentation and malformed block headers are rejected. Found and fixed during testing: any empty-valued key (`metadata:`) made every nested line skip validation (`\"\" in \"|>\"` is True), and a list item's sibling key was misread as a continuation. |\n| K2-03 | medium | ACCEPTED | Evidence failures exit 2: settings file present but unreadable or malformed, `skillOverrides` not an object, git probe failing in a repo. Absent settings still mean \"no overrides\". The staged `aios-metrics.py` reports `error_rc<N>` unless the checker exits 0 or 1. |\n| S2-02 / K2-02 | medium | OPEN — Eric's decision | 7 owned skills are `\"off\"` in Claude Code and published to Codex and Pi. The checker fails them. Resolving needs a roster choice (re-enable, or retire from canonical). |\n\n## Executed verification\n\n- Sync, bash 3.2, 13 scratch-HOME cases: all 9 round-1 cases still pass; pool manifest linked to\n  canonical `SKILL.md` → exit 2; codex manifest linked, `DRY_RUN=1` → exit 2; manifest is a\n  directory → exit 2; second normal run → manifests regular files, no temp files left.\n  Canonical `SKILL.md` intact in all 13.\n- PowerShell twin: 0 parse errors; preflight logic refuses a linked manifest; the write logic run\n  against a real symlink leaves the canonical file untouched, leaves a regular manifest with the\n  right content, and no temp file. Windows PowerShell 5.1 not exercised.\n- Real layout: sync exit 0; both manifests regular files, 43 lines, 0 temp files; drift 0/0,\n  dangling 0/0, tracked links 0.\n- Checker: 16/16 fixtures as expected; syntax check agrees with PyYAML on all 42 real skills;\n  real roster 7 failing, all override-only; fail-closed 4/4 exit 2; control exit 0; older\n  fixtures unchanged.\n=== CONTEXT ===\n# Gate C context (host-authored)\n\nScope per the plan's Review Gates section: `scripts/aios-metrics.py`,\n`scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh`, the launchd plist, and the `aios-audit` SKILL.md body.\n\n- The plist is outside this repo: `/Users/kristinarash/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.aiosaudit.plist`\n  (byte-identical to the plan's Task 7 Step 4 block; `plutil -lint` OK; loaded; one run via\n  `launchctl start` exited 0 with an empty stderr file and wrote a trend row).\n- `~/.claude/rot.md` is outside the repo; `docs/rot.md` is its committed copy.\n- Deviations from the plan text, all deliberate:\n  1. `aios-metrics.py` reports `portability_failures=error_rc<N>` unless the checker exits 0 or 1\n     (Gate B round 2, K2-03: evidence failures must not read as a pass).\n  2. The `aios-audit` SKILL.md adds a Parity check of `skillOverrides`, a Hooks name diff, Examples\n     and Gotchas sections beyond the plan's 8 required body parts; the plan's frontmatter is verbatim.\n- Known open item, not a Gate C defect: `portability_failures=7` is the unresolved roster decision\n  (7 owned skills off in Claude Code but published to Codex and Pi), carried from Gate B.\n\nExecuted host verification: metrics script exit 0, key=value only, invariants 0; cron Step 2 run\nexit 0 with a full row and `=== done ok ===`; every wrapper key is emitted by the metrics script;\nfailure paths (missing metrics script exit 1 no row; live lock exit 0 no row; stale lock reclaimed,\nexit 0, one row); launchd-started run exit 0; headless `claude -p \"audit my AI OS\"` in this repo\nlisted and fired `aios-audit`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9d154977-efcd-4996-b504-419145bf00d8","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"432c574c-e7ae-4624-a97a-9cf92eeb1456","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88b6ccb8-7105-4de5-afa1-ccbae8a94e54","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T6L6JBN1Dnnr1HdRXDyneX","type":"tool_result","content":"      49 /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t8-pi-trial.md\n     226 /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md\n     275 total\n1:# Gate A — plan approval record — 2026-09-12\n13:## Review history\n31:## Pre-flight state at approval (read-only, verified)\n43:## Execution so far\n61:## Task 4 — premise correction found before execution\n80:### Full triage (read-only, content-compared, `__pycache__`/`.pyc`/`.DS_Store` ignored)\n99:### Backup taken before any publish\n107:### Task 4 Step 1 — done\n118:### Task 4 Step 2 — decisions\n147:### Task 4 Steps 3–7 — evidence\n160:## Task 5 — evidence\n192:## Gate B — round 1\n212:## Gate B — round 2 (inspection budget now used up)\n\nany repo it sweeps. Long plan executions should commit at each verified step,\nnot batch the commit to the end of a task.\n\n| 7 | Daily backup reloaded: skills tree clean first; plist has no `RunAtLoad` (09:00 only); `launchctl list` shows `com.keystone.dailybackup`. |\n\n## Gate B — round 1\n\nTwo fresh Codex inspections (`runner.py inspect --host claude --builder claude`),\none per repo: claude-skills from `3ab4467`, KeystoneOS from `8c4c028`.\n\n| Repo | Verdict | Findings |\n|---|---|---|\n| claude-skills | REVISE | R13-01 high (a view root aliasing canonical makes the publish loop delete the canonical skill), R13-02 medium (git records `harvest/`; `name: Harvest` breaks a fresh checkout), R13-03 medium (checker accepts unloadable YAML) |\n| KeystoneOS | REVISE | B-01 medium (= R13-03), B-02 medium (`skillOverrides` parity gap not enforced) |\n\nAll accepted. Fixed in `8c6bb7a` (claude-skills) and `e47e3af` (KeystoneOS):\n\n- **R13-01:** both twins resolve all three roots through every link in the path and its ancestors and refuse (exit 2, no changes) on same-or-nested roots. Bash: 9 scratch-HOME cases pass, canonical intact in all. PowerShell: parses; resolver tested on real symlinks under pwsh 7 (7 cases pass); Windows PowerShell 5.1 not exercised.\n- **R13-02:** `name: harvest` restored; local folder case fixed; real sync retired the `Harvest` view links (archived) and published `harvest`. Metrics after: drift 0/0, dangling 0/0, tracked links 0.\n- **R13-03 / B-01:** plain scalars with `: ` or ` #` fail. 6 new fixtures behave as expected; PyYAML cross-check over 48 files: 0 disagreements.\n- **B-02, in part:** owned skills `\"off\"` in Claude Code but published now fail the checker — **7 today**. Choosing the enabled roster is left to Eric (the overrides were set on purpose in the 2026-09-12 skill audit).\n- Not a finding: three descriptions trimmed under 650 chars.\n\nConsequence for the numbers: `portability_failures` is now **7**, not 0, until the roster decision is made.\n\n## Gate B — round 2 (inspection budget now used up)\n\nFresh Codex inspections again, with the round-1 dispositions as feedback. Both REVISE.\n\n| Repo | Findings |\n|---|---|\n| claude-skills | S2-01 high: a view manifest that is a link makes the sync overwrite its target (e.g. a canonical `SKILL.md`). S2-02: roster parity still open. |\n| KeystoneOS | K2-01 medium: quoted escapes and flow collections not validated. K2-02: roster parity still open. K2-03 medium: unreadable settings or a failed git probe read as \"no problems\". |\n\nFixed and host-verified, **not re-inspected** (claudex-loop allows 2 inspection rounds):\n\n- **S2-01** (`7459560`): both twins refuse a linked or non-regular manifest before any change, and write the manifest as a new file moved into place. 13 bash cases pass with canonical intact; PowerShell write path tested on a real symlink; real sync clean (drift 0/0).\n- **K2-01 / K2-03** (`602f3a8`): line-by-line subset validation including nested lines; evidence failures exit 2; the staged metrics script honours the exit code. 16/16 fixtures; 0 disagreements with PyYAML over 42 real skills; 4/4 fail-closed cases.\n- Two checker bugs were found by these tests and fixed before commit: empty-valued keys skipped all nested validation, and list-item sibling keys were misread as continuations.\n- **S2-02 / K2-02 open:** the 7-skill roster decision. Details: `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/gateB-dispositions-r2.md`.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3e743200-29b3-44a4-a514-1963b6352382","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:10:24.568Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"      49 /Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t8-pi-trial.md\n     226 /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md\n     275 total\n1:# Gate A — plan approval record — 2026-09-12\n13:## Review history\n31:## Pre-flight state at approval (read-only, verified)\n43:## Execution so far\n61:## Task 4 — premise correction found before execution\n80:### Full triage (read-only, content-compared, `__pycache__`/`.pyc`/`.DS_Store` ignored)\n99:### Backup taken before any publish\n107:### Task 4 Step 1 — done\n118:### Task 4 Step 2 — decisions\n147:### Task 4 Steps 3–7 — evidence\n160:## Task 5 — evidence\n192:## Gate B — round 1\n212:## Gate B — round 2 (inspection budget now used up)\n\nany repo it sweeps. Long plan executions should commit at each verified step,\nnot batch the commit to the end of a task.\n\n| 7 | Daily backup reloaded: skills tree clean first; plist has no `RunAtLoad` (09:00 only); `launchctl list` shows `com.keystone.dailybackup`. |\n\n## Gate B — round 1\n\nTwo fresh Codex inspections (`runner.py inspect --host claude --builder claude`),\none per repo: claude-skills from `3ab4467`, KeystoneOS from `8c4c028`.\n\n| Repo | Verdict | Findings |\n|---|---|---|\n| claude-skills | REVISE | R13-01 high (a view root aliasing canonical makes the publish loop delete the canonical skill), R13-02 medium (git records `harvest/`; `name: Harvest` breaks a fresh checkout), R13-03 medium (checker accepts unloadable YAML) |\n| KeystoneOS | REVISE | B-01 medium (= R13-03), B-02 medium (`skillOverrides` parity gap not enforced) |\n\nAll accepted. Fixed in `8c6bb7a` (claude-skills) and `e47e3af` (KeystoneOS):\n\n- **R13-01:** both twins resolve all three roots through every link in the path and its ancestors and refuse (exit 2, no changes) on same-or-nested roots. Bash: 9 scratch-HOME cases pass, canonical intact in all. PowerShell: parses; resolver tested on real symlinks under pwsh 7 (7 cases pass); Windows PowerShell 5.1 not exercised.\n- **R13-02:** `name: harvest` restored; local folder case fixed; real sync retired the `Harvest` view links (archived) and published `harvest`. Metrics after: drift 0/0, dangling 0/0, tracked links 0.\n- **R13-03 / B-01:** plain scalars with `: ` or ` #` fail. 6 new fixtures behave as expected; PyYAML cross-check over 48 files: 0 disagreements.\n- **B-02, in part:** owned skills `\"off\"` in Claude Code but published now fail the checker — **7 today**. Choosing the enabled roster is left to Eric (the overrides were set on purpose in the 2026-09-12 skill audit).\n- Not a finding: three descriptions trimmed under 650 chars.\n\nConsequence for the numbers: `portability_failures` is now **7**, not 0, until the roster decision is made.\n\n## Gate B — round 2 (inspection budget now used up)\n\nFresh Codex inspections again, with the round-1 dispositions as feedback. Both REVISE.\n\n| Repo | Findings |\n|---|---|\n| claude-skills | S2-01 high: a view manifest that is a link makes the sync overwrite its target (e.g. a canonical `SKILL.md`). S2-02: roster parity still open. |\n| KeystoneOS | K2-01 medium: quoted escapes and flow collections not validated. K2-02: roster parity still open. K2-03 medium: unreadable settings or a failed git probe read as \"no problems\". |\n\nFixed and host-verified, **not re-inspected** (claudex-loop allows 2 inspection rounds):\n\n- **S2-01** (`7459560`): both tw