{"parentUuid":"4ea5c117-13b1-402c-b62d-8abdf43de7bf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezwZwideQ6kgCFtuCfQc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EftuaJTZds6eiHxReELKnw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/9823c1f0/tmp/gateC-dispositions.md","content":"# Gate C dispositions (host-authored, 2026-09-13)\n\nCodex Gate C verdict on KeystoneOS (base `767b3de`): REVISE, three medium findings.\nAll accepted and fixed. Host-verified below; this inspection is the independent check.\n\n| ID | Sev | Disposition | What changed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| C-01 | medium | ACCEPTED | Commit `77d9ecc`: `scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh`, `scripts/aios-metrics.py`, `scripts/skill-portability-check.py` recorded as mode 100755 via `git update-index --chmod=+x` (repo has `core.fileMode=false`). `git ls-files -s` shows 100755 for all three. |\n| C-02 | medium | ACCEPTED | Commit `dae7aeb`: stale-lock reclaim serialised by a second atomic lock `$LOCK.recover` (mkdir; stale when older than 10 min). Only a holder of `.recover` deletes `$LOCK`. While holding it the run re-tries `mkdir $LOCK`, re-reads the owner, aborts on a live owner or a young ownerless lock, and releases `.recover` on every path. EXIT trap removes `$LOCK` only if `$LOCK/pid` equals `$$`. Log strings `ABORT live run` / `RECLAIM stale lock` unchanged. A test-only `AIOS_LOCK_TEST_PAUSE` sleep sits just before the reclaim, unset under launchd. Accepted residual risk (commented in the script): a crash inside the millisecond recovery section, followed more than 10 minutes later by two runs starting together. |\n| C-03 | medium | ACCEPTED | Commit `dae7aeb`: `usage()` counts transcripts that raise on read instead of swallowing them. New keys `usage_scope=claude_code_transcripts_only` and `usage_unreadable_transcripts=N`; no existing key renamed (the cron wrapper's keys are untouched). `aios-audit` SKILL.md §6: Bloat now says \"never invoked in Claude Code transcripts\", notes the scope and unreadable count; Crutch test forbids DELETE on `never_used` alone and gives `grep -rl \"<skill>/SKILL.md\" ~/.codex/sessions \\| wc -l`, with a warning that bulk scans also match. |\n\n## Executed verification\n\n- `bash -n` on the wrapper; `py_compile` on metrics and the test script: OK.\n- C-03 probe (`~/.claude/jobs/9823c1f0/tmp/c03-probe.py`): baseline `usage_scope=claude_code_transcripts_only`, `usage_unreadable_transcripts=0`; with one mode-000 `.jsonl` placed under `~/.claude/projects/` the count became 1; probe file removed. PASS.\n- Failure paths (`~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t7-failpaths.py`), all against the real wrapper and real metrics:\n  - missing metrics script: exit 1, no row, `FAIL metrics script errored` — PASS\n  - live lock: exit 0, no row, `ABORT live run` — PASS\n  - stale lock reclaimed: exit 0, one row, `RECLAIM stale lock` — PASS\n  - lock and `.recover` released afterwards — PASS\n  - two concurrent runs on one stale lock, first held 3 s inside the recovery section: exit 0,0; exactly one row; one RECLAIM; no leftover lock or `.recover` — PASS\n  - same, no pause (started together): exit 0,0; one row; one RECLAIM; no leftovers — PASS\n  - `.recover` aged 11 min: reclaimed, run proceeds, one row, nothing left — PASS\n  - fresh `.recover`: exit 0, no row, `ABORT another run is recovering` — PASS\n  - metrics script restored and executable — PASS\n- Test side effects undone: `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` and `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log` restored byte-for-byte from pre-test copies. `git status` clean apart from the three committed source files.\n\n## Still open, not a Gate C defect\n\n- `portability_failures=7`: the 7-skill roster decision carried from Gate B (S2-02 / K2-02). Eric's call.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":488