{"parentUuid":"62c93598-df4f-4db3-bad6-ee11c061f727","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88b6ccb8-7105-4de5-afa1-ccbae8a94e54","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TFjNyszPe7rZG6bB6CdjH3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Pi trial - 2026-09-12\n2\t\n3\tBoundary: separate macOS user `piuser`, no read access to the operator home.\n4\t`cd` into a directory is NOT a boundary and was not treated as one (R5).\n5\t\n6\t**Verdict: BLOCKED at Step 1.** Creating `piuser` needs `sudo`, and this plan ran as a\n7\tnon-interactive background session: `sudo -n true` → \"a password is required\". The plan's\n8\tstop condition applies (\"If the user cannot be created ... stop and write up what failed\").\n9\tNothing was installed and no Pi process was run. Eric's own `/opt/homebrew/bin/pi` was left\n10\tuntouched on purpose: it auto-discovers Eric's real pool, so it is not the trial binary.\n11\t\n12\t| Question | Answer |\n13\t|---|---|\n14\t| pi version | not reached (Step 1) — the trial installs its own copy under `/Users/piuser/.npm-global` |\n15\t| piuser blocked from ~/DEV and ~/SecondBrain? | not reached (Step 1). Pre-check: `ls -ld ~` = `drwxr-x---+ kristinarash staff`, so a `piuser` in group `staff` WOULD read `~` through the group bits — the plan's own-group step (GID 4242, confirmed unused) is required, not optional |\n16\t| skills auto-discovered | not reached (Step 1). Expected value to compare against: `pool_skills=210` (Task 4 Step 6) |\n17\t| skills needing edits to fire in Pi | not reached (Step 1) |\n18\t| extension contract matched the research note? | not reached (Step 1). Guard staged byte-for-byte from the plan (factory + `pi.on('tool_call')` + `event.input`) |\n19\t| minutes to port the dcg guard | not reached (Step 1) |\n20\t| hooks still to port | not reached (Step 1); inventory today: 61 in `~/.claude/hooks`, 59 in `~/.codex/hooks` (the two copies differ by 2) |\n21\t| verdict | BLOCKED |\n22\t\n23\t## What the guard proved\n24\t\n25\tNothing yet — the guard needs the boundary user first. Probes A/B/C in plan Step 6 are unchanged.\n26\t\n27\t## To unblock (Eric, in a terminal — about 2 minutes)\n28\t\n29\tRun plan Task 8 Step 1 exactly. It prompts for your password:\n30\t\n31\t```bash\n32\tsudo sysadminctl -addUser piuser -fullName \"Pi Trial\" -password - -home /Users/piuser\n33\tsudo dscl . -create /Groups/pitrial\n34\tsudo dscl . -create /Groups/pitrial PrimaryGroupID 4242\n35\tsudo dscl . -create /Users/piuser PrimaryGroupID 4242\n36\tid piuser\n37\tdseditgroup -o checkmember -m piuser staff\n38\tsudo -u piuser ls ~/DEV          2>&1 | tail -2\n39\tsudo -u piuser ls ~/SecondBrain  2>&1 | tail -2\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\tBoth `ls` lines must print **Permission denied**; `id piuser` must not list `staff(20)`.\n43\tThen a session can run Steps 2-8 (Steps 2, 3, 6 and 8 also use `sudo`, so they need an\n44\tinteractive session or a sudo-capable one).\n45\t\n46\t## What a real adoption would still need\n47\t\n48\tNot in scope here. At minimum: a boundary design that is not a second user\n49\taccount, an approval-prompt layer, and a port of the remaining hooks.\n50\t"}]},"uuid":"05379335-64b3-4e76-aa9b-40682ff6ca8e","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:11:04.628Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t8-pi-trial.md","content":"# Pi trial - 2026-09-12\n\nBoundary: separate macOS user `piuser`, no read access to the operator home.\n`cd` into a directory is NOT a boundary and was not treated as one (R5).\n\n**Verdict: BLOCKED at Step 1.** Creating `piuser` needs `sudo`, and this plan ran as a\nnon-interactive background session: `sudo -n true` → \"a password is required\". The plan's\nstop condition applies (\"If the user cannot be created ... stop and write up what failed\").\nNothing was installed and no Pi process was run. Eric's own `/opt/homebrew/bin/pi` was left\nuntouched on purpose: it auto-discovers Eric's real pool, so it is not the t