{"parentUuid":"d4340c62-51a0-45fc-bb35-5c24a49c435f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88b6ccb8-7105-4de5-afa1-ccbae8a94e54","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FSAPA6sEXpGGxv8Nyxt6M5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# STATUS\n2\t\n3\tRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n4\t\n5\t<!-- Filled 2026-09-12 by dev-sync on Windows, reconstructed from git history and the\n6\t     AIOS plan. It was an empty migration stub before this. Verify before relying on it. -->\n7\t\n8\t## Current state\n9\t- The dominant thread is the **harness-agnostic AIOS plan**:\n10\t  `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`. Goal is that every skill\n11\t  Eric owns loads identically in Claude Code, Codex and Pi from one versioned canonical\n12\t  folder, plus a recurring audit that keeps the AIOS from rotting.\n13\t- Architecture: `~/.claude/skills/` (repo `erash11/claude-skills`) is canonical and holds\n14\t  real directories only. `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are generated views\n15\t  rebuilt per machine by `sync-to-codex.sh` / `.ps1` - symlinks on Mac, copies on Windows.\n16\t- Codex approved the plan on round 6 (findings 10 -> 9 -> 7 -> 4 -> 1 -> 0), then a\n17\t  round-7 pass (R7-01..R7-05) folded in one declared vendor inventory everywhere.\n18\t- **2026-09-12 afternoon, Mac: Task 1 (snapshot and freeze, plus AMEND-01) and Task 2\n19\t  (prune the stale pool mirror, 306 -> 208) are complete.** Task 2 archived 98 skills\n20\t  that were still live in `~/.agents/skills`. Reversible. Audit records are in\n21\t  `docs/audits/2026-09-12-*.txt`.\n22\t- The approval was a static, read-only review. It is an approved plan, not proven\n23\t  behaviour. Gates B, C and D still apply.\n24\t- Also landed recently: daily-backup schedule aligned with launchd (00:30 -> 09:00), a\n25\t  stale Windows duplicate of `reMarkale_extract` dropped, and a corrupt\n26\t  `memsearch-sync.ps1.from-mac` removed.\n27\t\n28\t## Next\n29\t- **Task 3: harden the sync writers before anything moves** (`sync-to-codex.sh` and the\n30\t  `.ps1` twin). Then Task 4 (invert the outward symlinks, publish the views) and Task 5\n31\t  (portable frontmatter).\n32\t- Gate B is a `codex-review` after Task 5. Gate C comes after Task 7, Gate D before\n33\t  declaring done.\n34\t- Plan checkboxes are not being ticked (Task 1 still shows unchecked). Commit messages\n35\t  are the reliable progress record.\n36\t\n37\t## Open questions\n38\t- None recorded in the plan. Round 6 closed with no material unresolved defects in scope.\n39\t\n40\t## Gotchas\n41\t- Never commit a symlink into `~/.claude/skills/`. Windows pulls that repo and an absolute\n42\t  Mac symlink arrives unusable.\n43\t- Hooks and sync scripts exist in two copies (`~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/`; `.sh`\n44\t  and `.ps1`). Any change patches both.\n45\t- Global `MEMORY.md` is at 2,489 of 2,500 chars. Consolidate before adding to it.\n46\t- Never point Pi at `~/DEV` - it ships no sandbox and no approval prompts, by design.\n47\t- Never let any harness near `DexaProject` (identifiable athlete health data, on Google\n48\t  Drive, not in `~/DEV`).\n49\t- Plugin skills (`superpowers`, `mattpocock-skills`) are vendored and out of scope.\n50\t- **Windows:** four vendored skills (`claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`,\n51\t  `codex-review`) are committed to `claude-skills` as symlinks. On Windows they arrive\n52\t  pointing at a path that does not exist. AMEND-01 in Task 4 untracks them.\n53\t- On the Mac: `timeout` is not installed, `dcg` blocks `find ... -delete`, and Python is\n54\t  PEP 668-managed (stdlib `python3` or `uv`, never global `pip install`).\n55\t- No success claim without pasted command output.\n56\t"}]},"uuid":"9e6f173a-12bd-42f7-b5e9-7f187451dd3a","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:11:05.237Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md","content":"# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n<!-- Filled 2026-09-12 by dev-sync on Windows, reconstructed from git history and the\n     AIOS plan. It was an empty migration stub before this. Verify before relying on it. -->\n\n## Current state\n- The dominant thread is the **harness-agnostic AIOS plan**:\n  `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`. Goal is that every skill\n  Eric owns loads identically in Claude Code, Codex and Pi from one versioned canonical\n  folder, plus a recurring audit that keeps the AIOS from rotting.\n- Architecture: `~/.claude/skills/` (repo `erash11/claude-skills`) is canonical and holds\n  real directories only. `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are generated views\n  rebuilt per machine by `sync-to-codex.sh` / `.ps1` - symlinks on Mac, copies on Windows.\n- Codex approved the plan on round 6 (findings 10 -> 9 -> 7 -> 4 -> 1 -> 0), then a\n  round-7 pass (R7-01..R7-05) folded in one declared vendor inventory everywhere.\n- **2026-09-12 afternoon, Mac: Task 1 (snapshot and freeze, plus AMEND-01) and Task 2\n  (prune the stale pool mirror, 306 -> 208) are complete.** Task 2 archived 98 skills\n  that were still live in `~/.agents/skills`. Reversible. Audit records are in\n  `docs/audits/2026-09-12-*.txt`.\n- The approval was a static, read-only review. It is an approved plan, not proven\n  behaviour. Gates B, C and D still apply.\n- Also landed recently: daily-backup schedule aligned with launchd (00:30 -> 09:00), a\n  stale Windows duplicate of `reMarkale_extract` dropped, and a corrupt\n  `memsearch-sync.ps1.from-mac` removed.\n\n## Next\n- **Task 3: harden the sync writers before anything moves** (`sync-to-codex.sh` and the\n  `.ps1` twin). Then Task 4 (invert the outward symlinks, publish the views) and Task 5\n  (portable frontmatter).\n- Gate B is a `codex-review` after Task 5. Gate C comes after Task 7, Gate D before\n  declaring done.\n- Plan checkboxes are not being ticked (Task 1 still shows unchecked). Commit messages\n  are the reliable progress record.\n\n## Open questions\n- None recorded in the plan. Round 6 closed with no material unresolved defects in scope.\n\n## Gotchas\n- Never commit a symlink into `~/.claude/skills/`. Windows pulls that repo and an absolute\n  Mac symlink arrives unusable.\n- Hooks and sync scripts exist in two copies (`~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/`; `.sh`\n  and `.ps1`). Any change patches both.\n- Global `MEMORY.md` is at 2,489 of 2,500 chars. Consolidate before adding to it.\n- Never point Pi at `~/DEV` - it ships no sandbox and no approval prompts, by design.\n- Never let any harness near `DexaProject` (identifiable athlete health data, on Google\n  Drive, not in `~/DEV`).\n- Plugin skills (`superpowers`, `mattpocock-skills`) are vendored and out of scope.\n- **Windows:** four vendored skills (`claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`,\n  `codex-review`) are committed to `claude-skills` as symlinks. On Windows they arrive\n  pointing at a path that does not exist. AMEND-01 in Task 4 untracks them.\n- On the Mac: `timeout` is not installed, `dcg` blocks `find ... -delete`, and Python is\n  PEP 668-managed (stdlib `python3` or `uv`, never global `pip install`).\n- No success claim without pasted command output.\n","numLines":56,"startLine":1,"totalLines":56}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d4340c62-51a0-45fc-bb35-5c24a49c435f","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
