{"parentUuid":"e7f226fc-b4ad-4fb3-a308-65369ace7c88","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88b6ccb8-7105-4de5-afa1-ccbae8a94e54","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BUunNX4nQrq2jEd4pubLat","type":"tool_result","content":"40\t| Current `sync-to-codex.ps1` | 13 lines, `Remove-Item -Recurse` + `Copy-Item` — matches the plan's baseline |\n41\t| `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` | absent — correct; created only at the end of Task 4 Step 2 |\n42\t\n43\t## Execution so far\n44\t\n45\t- Task 1 — done (`d2e4a3b`)\n46\t- Task 2 — done (`f54c8d9`)\n47\t- **Task 3 — done.** Every step verified on the real, installed files:\n48\t\n49\t| Step | Evidence |\n50\t|---|---|\n51\t| 0 | `com.keystone.dailybackup` unloaded (`launchctl list` no longer shows it) |\n52\t| 2–3 | Both scripts installed byte-for-byte from the approved plan (sha256 of each installed file == the staged extract); original mode `0644` kept; `bash -n` OK |\n53\t| 3b | Installed twin parses under `pwsh`: 205 lines, 0 `Write-Error` calls, 6 `Stop-Fatal`, first-run gate and `.git/info/exclude` present |\n54\t| 4 / 4b | Against the **installed** script on `/bin/bash` 3.2: CASE 1 exit 0 (link skipped, canary intact, `theirs` ignored, `mine` tracked); CASE 2 exit 2 (owned-became-link FATAL); CASE 3+4 exit 0 (2 links removed from the index, only `owned/SKILL.md` left, `D old-link`); CASE 5 dry exit 0 / real exit 2 with gate message; CASE 5b `DRY_RUN=true` exit 2, pool copy untouched; deletion workflow exits 0 twice, 0 dangling, archived under `agents` + `codex`, manifest cleaned |\n55\t| 5 | **Real layout**, `DRY_RUN=1`: exit 0, `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`, 86 `would sync` lines (43 × 2 views). Fingerprints of index, `info/exclude`, pool listing and codex listing **identical before and after**; `memory-write`/`meeting-sync` still real dirs; no manifest, no marker. Nothing written. |\n56\t| 5b | Hook installed after confirming none existed and `core.hooksPath` unset; executable; sha matches plan. Installed hook T1 untrack exit 0, T2 new link exit 1 (reason printed), T3 normal exit 0, T4 file→link exit 1 |\n57\t| 5c | `daily-backup.ps1` patched (plan's OLD block matched the real file exactly once); parses under `pwsh`. Harness on the **real patched file + installed hook**: `COMMIT FAILED` with hook reason recorded, then normal change `committed` + `pushed`, `ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED`, exit 0. Committed to dotclaude **by name only** as `d3e0955` and pushed (11 live session logs left unstaged) |\n58\t| 6 | `git status` in the skills repo showed exactly `M sync-to-codex.ps1` and `M sync-to-codex.sh` |\n59\t| 7 | Committed `8193bb9` and pushed. **The new pre-commit hook allowed it** — first live confirmation that it does not block normal commits |\n60\t\n61\t## Task 4 — premise correction found before execution\n62\t\n63\tTask 4 Step 2 expected \"at least\" `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` to be\n64\tDIVERGED. The scan found **22** owned skills whose pool copy is a real\n65\tdirectory that differs from canonical. The two named in the plan were read in\n66\tfull, and in both the pool copy is an **older version**, not unique work:\n67\t\n68\t- `memory-write` — pool `SKILL.md` dated 2026-08-07, canonical 2026-09-02. The pool copy lacks the `name:`-slug rule and the retrieval-ladder section that canonical has.\n69\t- `meeting-sync` — pool dated 2026-08-07, canonical 2026-08-15. The pool copy carries the pre-migration path `/Users/kristinarash/Desktop/SecondBrain/...`.\n70\t\n71\tThe scan also had a gap the plan did not cover: it considered only\n72\tdirectories with a `SKILL.md`. The publish also replaces the pool's `_shared`\n73\tsupport directory and any real directories in `~/.codex/skills` for managed\n74\tnames. Both are now included in the triage and the backup.\n75\t\n76\tThe plan's step logic already handles any number of DIVERGED names, so this is\n77\trecorded here rather than edited into the approved plan, which keeps its hash\n78\tvalid.\n79\t\n80\t### Full triage (read-only, content-compared, `__pycache__`/`.pyc`/`.DS_Store` ignored)\n81\t\n82\t- **Pool:** 23 entries differ — 22 owned skills plus `_shared`.\n83\t  - **22 are \"canonical newer — safe\":** no file exists only in the pool, and no differing file is newer in the pool. They are stale copies.\n84\t  - **1 needs review: `graphify`**, detailed below.\n85\t- **Codex view:** 0 real directories differ from canonical.\n86\t\n87\t**`graphify`.** Two files differ, `SKILL.md` and `references/hooks.md`. The pool\n88\t`SKILL.md` is dated 2026-08-29 14:34, **one minute after** canonical's 14:33. The\n89\tdiff is not independent work. It is graphify's installer writing a\n90\t**per-harness variant**:\n91\t\n92\t| | Canonical (Claude Code) | Pool (Codex / agents) |\n93\t|---|---|---|\n94\t| Subagent dispatch | \"Call the **Agent** tool … `subagent_type=\"general-purpose\"`\" | \"Uses the **`Task`** tool … `Task(description=…)`\" |\n95\t| Integration section | \"native **CLAUDE.md** integration\" | \"native **AGENTS.md** integration\" |\n96\t\n97\tThe 4,795 files that exist only in canonical are `graphify/.venv` (its runtime).\n98\t\n99\t### Backup taken before any publish\n100\t\n101\tAll 23 diverged pool copies were copied to\n102\t`~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/`, including `graphify` (29 files)\n103\tand `_shared`. File counts matched on every copy, and none were skipped. The codex\n104\tbackup root `pre-sync-2026-09-12-codex/` is empty because nothing there diverged.\n105\tThe VIEWS tarball from Task 1 remains a second, independent copy.\n106\t\n107\t### Task 4 Step 1 — done\n108\t\n109\tRun through Python `subprocess`: `dcg` blocks `git` inside shell command\n110\tsubstitution, so the plan's shell form could not be used. Results:\n111\t\n112\t- 19 tracked mode-120000 entries; every one is a symlink on disk.\n113\t- `git rm --cached --pathspec-from-file` exited 0.\n114\t- **19** staged deletions; all 19 still on disk as links; **0** tracked links left in the index.\n115\t- The 19 now show as `??` until Step 3 writes `.git/info/exclude`.\n116\t- No `git add -A` may run before Step 3. The daily backup is still unloaded.\n117\t\n118\t### Task 4 Step 2 — decisions\n119\t\n120\t**All 22 stale copies: canonical wins.** Nothing is copied into canonical.\n121\t\n122\t**The plan's premise did not hold.** R2-01 and R9-01 assumed the pool held\n123\tedits that exist nowhere else. The reconcile tested that and found none: every\n124\tpool copy is older, and one still carries the pre-migration\n125\t`Desktop/SecondBrain` path. The reconcile did its job by proving that nothing\n126\tneeds to move.\n127\t\n128\t**`graphify`: canonical wins; the Codex variant stays archived** in\n129\t`pre-sync-2026-09-12/graphify`. No name-list exception was added, because a\n130\tlist would bring back the R7-01 regression. Two known costs:\n131\t\n132\t1. **Codex and Pi get the Claude-flavoured body.** They will read \"call the\n133\t   Agent tool\" and \"CLAUDE.md\". Task 5 fixes frontmatter only, not skill\n134\t   bodies, so this stays open (out of scope for this plan).\n135\t2. **Write-through, verified in graphify's installer source.**\n136\t   `graphify install --platform agents` calls `_copy_skill_file(\"agents\")`.\n137\t   That function writes `~/.agents/skills/graphify/SKILL.md` with a temp file\n138\t   plus `os.replace`, and replaces `references/` with `rmtree` plus\n139\t   `os.replace`. After Step 3 that path is a link to canonical, so the command\n140\t   writes the Codex variant **into canonical**. The next daily backup would\n141\t   then commit it. **Do not run `--platform agents` any more**; running\n142\t   `--platform claude` alone is now enough. This is the first `aios-audit`\n143\t   finding and a `rot.md` line for Task 6.\n144\t\n145\tMarker `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` created after these decisions.\n146\t\n147\t### Task 4 Steps 3–7 — evidence\n148\t\n149\tA fingerprint was saved before Step 3 and compared after it.\n150\t\n151\t| Step | Evidence |\n152\t|---|---|\n153\t| 3 | Real run exit 0: `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`; exclude block holds all 19 names, leading slash, no trailing slash; `/.claude/RESUME.md` kept; `.gitignore` unchanged. `check-ignore` yes for 19 of 19. `git status` went from 19 `D` + 19 `??` to 19 `D` only. The index was not changed by the sync. |\n154\t| 3 (views) | **Pool** 209 → 215 entries: 36 real dirs → links, 5 new links, manifest added. **Codex** 33 → 56: 4 real dirs → links, 22 new links, manifest added. **0** changes to any non-owned name in either view (third-party entries and the codex `session-handoff` dir untouched). All 43 owned entries link to canonical in both views. |\n155\t| 4 | `git add -A`: **0** mode-120000 entries staged; `19 files changed, 19 deletions(-)`; no `.gitignore` change |\n156\t| 5 | 42 owned, 19 links, 61 resolvable `SKILL.md`, 0 dangling, `_shared OK`, meeting-sync resolves `_shared`: True |\n157\t| 6 | Idempotent dry run exit 0; manifest 43 in both views; nothing missing; no wrong targets. **Pool skill count = 210** (Task 8 baseline) |\n158\t| 7 | `/reload-skills` needs an interactive session, so this background job could not run it. Disk-level substitute: 61 resolvable `SKILL.md` (Step 5). **Eric to confirm `/skills` shows 61 in a live session.** Committed `5f80203` (erash11/claude-skills) and pushed; HEAD == upstream; tree clean. The pre-commit hook allowed the deletions. |\n159\t\n160\t## Task 5 — evidence\n161\t\n162\t| Step | Evidence |\n163\t|---|---|\n164\t| 1 | Checker extracted byte-for-byte from plan lines 1583–1732 (150 lines); compiles; `chmod +x`. |\n165\t| 2 | Baseline `checked 42 skills, 33 failing, 9 portable`, exit 1. Empty inventory: `FATAL no SKILL.md found`, exit 2. Bad fixtures: all four FAIL for the stated reason (negonly: no standalone positive; dupekey: duplicate key; badquote: unbalanced quote; fragments: both clauses missing), exit 1. `dcg` blocks `rm -rf` inside a heredoc, so fixtures were built in fresh folders under the job tmp dir instead. |\n166\t| 3 | 33 descriptions rewritten from a hand-written file, in plan priority order, five per batch, checker after each batch (every batch: 0 still failing). Only the description block changed (plus `Harvest` `name:` → `Harvest`). Word-diff vs HEAD: only connector words removed (`Triggers on`, `Trigger phrases`, `whenever`, `instead.`, `automatically`). A real YAML loader (`uv run --with pyyaml`) parses all 42; **`new-project` was invalid YAML before** (unquoted `: `). Bodies byte-identical to HEAD: a first pass normalised CRLF in `html-to-pdf` and `pp-espn`; reverted to the original bytes. `library-advisor` got one extra `Do not use` sentence. |\n167\t| 4 | `checked 42 skills, 0 failing, 42 portable`, exit 0. |\n168\t| 5 | Headless runs, not interactive sessions (background job). `claude -p` with Bash/Write/Edit denied and a 3-turn cap; `codex exec -s read-only`. `memory-write`, `pp-zotero-research-library`, `meeting-prep`: loaded in **both** harnesses. `library-review`: loaded in Codex; **not listed in Claude Code at all**. |\n169\t\n170\t**Finding from Step 5, verified:** `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides`\n171\tsets 12 canonical skills `\"off\"`: 7 owned (`ArXiv`, `ISA`, `Science`,\n172\t`capture-insight`, `library-review`, `pp-espn`, `session-miner`) and 5\n173\tthird-party (`grilling`, `handoff`, `prototype`, `teach`, `watch`). Claude Code\n174\tomits them from its skill list. Codex does not read that file, so it loads\n175\tthem. This predates Task 5 (three of the seven were never edited). Two\n176\tconsequences:\n177\t\n178\t- Harness parity is broken by config, not by frontmatter. This is an `aios-audit` finding.\n179\t- Task 4 Step 7's \"`/skills` shows 61\" can never hold: Claude Code exposes 49 of the 61 (35 of 42 owned). The count was already this before the migration.\n180\t\n181\tA side-effect check after the `memory-write` runs found no memory file written\n182\tin either harness.\n183\t\n184\t| 6 | Report `docs/audits/2026-09-12-portability.md` generated from the real result files (0 `FILL IN`). **The skills-repo commit was made by another session, not this one:** at 17:43 an interactive Claude Code session ran `closeout`, which swept the uncommitted frontmatter edits into `cfcc291` (\"docs: reformat skill descriptions as block scalars, add disambiguation notes\") and pushed it. Verified against this job's final state: 34 files (the 33 rewrites plus `library-advisor`), every body byte-identical to `5f80203`, checker 0 failing, and parsed name+description identical to the state verified here. Its message wrongly calls the work \"pre-existing\"; pushed history was not rewritten. The KeystoneOS half is committed below. |\n185\t\n186\t**Risk recorded:** a concurrent `closeout` commits whatever is uncommitted in\n187\tany repo it sweeps. Long plan executions should commit at each verified step,\n188\tnot batch the commit to the end of a task.\n189\t"}]},"uuid":"c1ae7578-52d7-4e12-a697-983356b0d998","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:11:06.291Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md","content":"| Current `sync-to-codex.ps1` | 13 lines, `Remove-Item -Recurse` + `Copy-Item` — matches the plan's baseline |\n| `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` | absent — correct; created only at the end of Task 4 Step 2 |\n\n## Execution so far\n\n- Task 1 — done (`d2e4a3b`)\n- Task 2 — done (`f54c8d9`)\n- **Task 3 — done.** Every step verified on the real, installed files:\n\n| Step | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| 0 | `com.keystone.dailybackup` unloaded (`launchctl list` no longer shows it) |\n| 2–3 | Both scripts installed byte-for-byte from the approved plan (sha256 of each installed file == the staged extract); original mode `0644` kept; `bash -n` OK |\n| 3b | Installed twin parses under `pwsh`: 205 lines, 0 `Write-Error` calls, 6 `Stop-Fatal`, first-run gate and `.git/info/exclude` present |\n| 4 / 4b | Against the **installed** script on `/bin/bash` 3.2: CASE 1 exit 0 (link skipped, canary intact, `theirs` ignored, `mine` tracked); CASE 2 exit 2 (owned-became-link FATAL); CASE 3+4 exit 0 (2 links removed from the index, only `owned/SKILL.md` left, `D old-link`); CASE 5 dry exit 0 / real exit 2 with gate message; CASE 5b `DRY_RUN=true` exit 2, pool copy untouched; deletion workflow exits 0 twice, 0 dangling, archived under `agents` + `codex`, manifest cleaned |\n| 5 | **Real layout**, `DRY_RUN=1`: exit 0, `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`, 86 `would sync` lines (43 × 2 views). Fingerprints of index, `info/exclude`, pool listing and codex listing **identical before and after**; `memory-write`/`meeting-sync` still real dirs; no manifest, no marker. Nothing written. |\n| 5b | Hook installed after confirming none existed and `core.hooksPath` unset; executable; sha matches plan. Installed hook T1 untrack exit 0, T2 new link exit 1 (reason printed), T3 normal exit 0, T4 file→link exit 1 |\n| 5c | `daily-backup.ps1` patched (plan's OLD block matched the real file exactly once); parses under `pwsh`. Harness on the **real patched file + installed hook**: `COMMIT FAILED` with hook reason recorded, then normal change `committed` + `pushed`, `ALL BACKUP-COMMIT CHECKS PASSED`, exit 0. Committed to dotclaude **by name only** as `d3e0955` and pushed (11 live session logs left unstaged) |\n| 6 | `git status` in the skills repo showed exactly `M sync-to-codex.ps1` and `M sync-to-codex.sh` |\n| 7 | Committed `8193bb9` and pushed. **The new pre-commit hook allowed it** — first live confirmation that it does not block normal commits |\n\n## Task 4 — premise correction found before execution\n\nTask 4 Step 2 expected \"at least\" `memory-write` and `meeting-sync` to be\nDIVERGED. The scan found **22** owned skills whose pool copy is a real\ndirectory that differs from canonical. The two named in the plan were read in\nfull, and in both the pool copy is an **older version**, not unique work:\n\n- `memory-write` — pool `SKILL.md` dated 2026-08-07, canonical 2026-09-02. The pool copy lacks the `name:`-slug rule and the retrieval-ladder section that canonical has.\n- `meeting-sync` — pool dated 2026-08-07, canonical 2026-08-15. The pool copy carries the pre-migration path `/Users/kristinarash/Desktop/SecondBrain/...`.\n\nThe scan also had a gap the plan did not cover: it considered only\ndirectories with a `SKILL.md`. The publish also replaces the pool's `_shared`\nsupport directory and any real directories in `~/.codex/skills` for managed\nnames. Both are now included in the triage and the backup.\n\nThe plan's step logic already handles any number of DIVERGED names, so this is\nrecorded here rather than edited into the approved plan, which keeps its hash\nvalid.\n\n### Full triage (read-only, content-compared, `__pycache__`/`.pyc`/`.DS_Store` ignored)\n\n- **Pool:** 23 entries differ — 22 owned skills plus `_shared`.\n  - **22 are \"canonical newer — safe\":** no file exists only in the pool, and no differing file is newer in the pool. They are stale copies.\n  - **1 needs review: `graphify`**, detailed below.\n- **Codex view:** 0 real directories differ from canonical.\n\n**`graphify`.** Two files differ, `SKILL.md` and `references/hooks.md`. The pool\n`SKILL.md` is dated 2026-08-29 14:34, **one minute after** canonical's 14:33. The\ndiff is not independent work. It is graphify's installer writing a\n**per-harness variant**:\n\n| | Canonical (Claude Code) | Pool (Codex / agents) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Subagent dispatch | \"Call the **Agent** tool … `subagent_type=\"general-purpose\"`\" | \"Uses the **`Task`** tool … `Task(description=…)`\" |\n| Integration section | \"native **CLAUDE.md** integration\" | \"native **AGENTS.md** integration\" |\n\nThe 4,795 files that exist only in canonical are `graphify/.venv` (its runtime).\n\n### Backup taken before any publish\n\nAll 23 diverged pool copies were copied to\n`~/.agents/skills-archive/pre-sync-2026-09-12/`, including `graphify` (29 files)\nand `_shared`. File counts matched on every copy, and none were skipped. The codex\nbackup root `pre-sync-2026-09-12-codex/` is empty because nothing there diverged.\nThe VIEWS tarball from Task 1 remains a second, independent copy.\n\n### Task 4 Step 1 — done\n\nRun through Python `subprocess`: `dcg` blocks `git` inside shell command\nsubstitution, so the plan's shell form could not be used. Results:\n\n- 19 tracked mode-120000 entries; every one is a symlink on disk.\n- `git rm --cached --pathspec-from-file` exited 0.\n- **19** staged deletions; all 19 still on disk as links; **0** tracked links left in the index.\n- The 19 now show as `??` until Step 3 writes `.git/info/exclude`.\n- No `git add -A` may run before Step 3. The daily backup is still unloaded.\n\n### Task 4 Step 2 — decisions\n\n**All 22 stale copies: canonical wins.** Nothing is copied into canonical.\n\n**The plan's premise did not hold.** R2-01 and R9-01 assumed the pool held\nedits that exist nowhere else. The reconcile tested that and found none: every\npool copy is older, and one still carries the pre-migration\n`Desktop/SecondBrain` path. The reconcile did its job by proving that nothing\nneeds to move.\n\n**`graphify`: canonical wins; the Codex variant stays archived** in\n`pre-sync-2026-09-12/graphify`. No name-list exception was added, because a\nlist would bring back the R7-01 regression. Two known costs:\n\n1. **Codex and Pi get the Claude-flavoured body.** They will read \"call the\n   Agent tool\" and \"CLAUDE.md\". Task 5 fixes frontmatter only, not skill\n   bodies, so this stays open (out of scope for this plan).\n2. **Write-through, verified in graphify's installer source.**\n   `graphify install --platform agents` calls `_copy_skill_file(\"agents\")`.\n   That function writes `~/.agents/skills/graphify/SKILL.md` with a temp file\n   plus `os.replace`, and replaces `references/` with `rmtree` plus\n   `os.replace`. After Step 3 that path is a link to canonical, so the command\n   writes the Codex variant **into canonical**. The next daily backup would\n   then commit it. **Do not run `--platform agents` any more**; running\n   `--platform claude` alone is now enough. This is the first `aios-audit`\n   finding and a `rot.md` line for Task 6.\n\nMarker `~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready` created after these decisions.\n\n### Task 4 Steps 3–7 — evidence\n\nA fingerprint was saved before Step 3 and compared after it.\n\n| Step | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| 3 | Real run exit 0: `canonical manifest: 43 entries; third-party links: 19`; exclude block holds all 19 names, leading slash, no trailing slash; `/.claude/RESUME.md` kept; `.gitignore` unchanged. `check-ignore` yes for 19 of 19. `git status` went from 19 `D` + 19 `??` to 19 `D` only. The index was not changed by the sync. |\n| 3 (views) | **Pool** 209 → 215 entries: 36 real dirs → links, 5 new links, manifest added. **Codex** 33 → 56: 4 real dirs → links, 22 new links, manifest added. **0** changes to any non-owned name in either view (third-party entries and the codex `session-handoff` dir untouched). All 43 owned entries link to canonical in both views. |\n| 4 | `git add -A`: **0** mode-120000 entries staged; `19 files changed, 19 deletions(-)`; no `.gitignore` change |\n| 5 | 42 owned, 19 links, 61 resolvable `SKILL.md`, 0 dangling, `_shared OK`, meeting-sync resolves `_shared`: True |\n| 6 | Idempotent dry run exit 0; manifest 43 in both views; nothing missing; no wrong targets. **Pool skill count = 210** (Task 8 baseline) |\n| 7 | `/reload-skills` needs an interactive session, so this background job could not run it. Disk-level substitute: 61 resolvable `SKILL.md` (Step 5). **Eric to confirm `/skills` shows 61 in a live session.** Committed `5f80203` (erash11/claude-skills) and pushed; HEAD == upstream; tree clean. The pre-commit hook allowed the deletions. |\n\n## Task 5 — evidence\n\n| Step | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Checker extracted byte-for-byte from plan lines 1583–1732 (150 lines); compiles; `chmod +x`. |\n| 2 | Baseline `checked 42 skills, 33 failing, 9 portable`, exit 1. Empty inventory: `FATAL no SKILL.md found`, exit 2. Bad fixtures: all four FAIL for the stated reason (negonly: no standalone positive; dupekey: duplicate key; badquote: unbalanced quote; fragments: both clauses missing), exit 1. `dcg` blocks `rm -rf` inside a heredoc, so fixtures were built in fresh folders under the job tmp dir instead. |\n| 3 | 33 descriptions rewritten from a hand-written file, in plan priority order, five per batch, checker after each batch (every batch: 0 still failing). Only the description block changed (plus `Harvest` `name:` → `Harvest`). Word-diff vs HEAD: only connector words removed (`Triggers on`, `Trigger phrases`, `whenever`, `instead.`, `automatically`). A real YAML loader (`uv run --with pyyaml`) parses all 42; **`new-project` was invalid YAML before** (unquoted `: `). Bodies byte-identical to HEAD: a first pass normalised CRLF in `html-to-pdf` and `pp-espn`; reverted to the original bytes. `library-advisor` got one extra `Do not use` sentence. |\n| 4 | `checked 42 skills, 0 failing, 42 portable`, exit 0. |\n| 5 | Headless runs, not interactive sessions (background job). `claude -p` with Bash/Write/Edit denied and a 3-turn cap; `codex exec -s read-only`. `memory-write`, `pp-zotero-research-library`, `meeting-prep`: loaded in **both** harnesses. `library-review`: loaded in Codex; **not listed in Claude Code at all**. |\n\n**Finding from Step 5, verified:** `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides`\nsets 12 canonical skills `\"off\"`: 7 owned (`ArXiv`, `ISA`, `Science`,\n`capture-insight`, `library-review`, `pp-espn`, `session-miner`) and 5\nthird-party (`grilling`, `handoff`, `prototype`, `teach`, `watch`). Claude Code\nomits them from its skill list. Codex does not read that file, so it loads\nthem. This predates Task 5 (three of the seven were never edited). Two\nconsequences:\n\n- Harness parity is broken by config, not by frontmatter. This is an `aios-audit` finding.\n- Task 4 Step 7's \"`/skills` shows 61\" can never hold: Claude Code exposes 49 of the 61 (35 of 42 owned). The count was already this before the migration.\n\nA side-effect check after the `memory-write` runs found no memory file written\nin either harness.\n\n| 6 | Report `docs/audits/2026-09-12-portability.md` generated from the real result files (0 `FILL IN`). **The skills-repo commit was made by another session, not this one:** at 17:43 an interactive Claude Code session ran `closeout`, which swept the uncommitted frontmatter edits into `cfcc291` (\"docs: reformat skill descriptions as block scalars, add disambiguation notes\") and pushed it. Verified against this job's final state: 34 files (the 33 rewrites plus `library-advisor`), every body byte-identical to `5f80203`, checker 0 failing, and parsed name+description identical to the state verified here. Its message wrongly calls the work \"pre-existing\"; pushed history was not rewritten. The KeystoneOS half is committed below. |\n\n**Risk recorded:** a concurrent `closeout` commits whatever is uncommitted in\nany repo it sweeps. Long plan executions should commit at each verified step,\nnot batch the commit to the end of a task.\n","numLines":150,"startLine":40,"totalLines":227}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e7f226fc-b4ad-4fb3-a308-65369ace7c88","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
