{"parentUuid":"0c527960-9e39-41d2-9af2-f5f3976c495b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88b6ccb8-7105-4de5-afa1-ccbae8a94e54","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VQNEzhy66JuZZj3SrkQxtf","type":"tool_result","content":"- [ ] **Step 2: Run it by hand and verify the trend row**\n\n```bash\n~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\ncat ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-trend.md\ntail -25 ~/.claude/scripts/logs/aios-audit.log\ngit -C ~/DEV/KeystoneOS status --short\n```\n\nExpected: `exit=0`; a header plus one row with **no `MISSING` cells**; the log ends `=== done ok ===`; `git status` shows `aios-trend.md` as **modified but uncommitted** — that is correct, the human commits it.\n\n**A `MISSING` cell means a `get` key does not match a metrics key.** Confirm the two agree before loading launchd — this is how a rename silently kills the job (R7-04):\n\n```bash\ndiff <(python3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py | cut -d= -f1 | sort) \\\n     <(grep -o '\\$(get [a-z_]*)' ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh \\\n       | sed 's/\\$(get //;s/)//' | sort -u) \\\n  | grep '^>' && echo \"ABOVE: keys the wrapper wants that metrics does not emit\" \\\n  || echo \"every wrapper key is emitted by the metrics script\"\n```\n\nExpected: `every wrapper key is emitted by the metrics script`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Prove the failure paths (R9's masked-failure point)**\n\n```bash\n# A bad metrics script must fail the job, not write a row.\nmv ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py /tmp/aios-metrics.bak\n~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh; echo \"exit=$? (expect 1)\"\nmv /tmp/aios-metrics.bak ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py\n\n# A LIVE lock must make the job stand down.\nL=~/.claude/scripts/.aios-audit.lock\nrm -rf \"$L\"; mkdir -p \"$L\"; echo $$ > \"$L/pid\"     # this shell is alive\n~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh; echo \"exit=$? (expect 0, ABORT live run)\"\nrows_before=$(grep -c '^| 20' ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-trend.md)\n\n# A STALE lock must be RECLAIMED, not wedge the job forever (R2-06).\nrm -rf \"$L\"; mkdir -p \"$L\"; echo 999999 > \"$L/pid\"  # a pid that cannot exist\n~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh; echo \"exit=$? (expect 0, RECLAIM then run)\"\nrows_after=$(grep -c '^| 20' ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-trend.md)\necho \"rows before=$rows_before after=$rows_after (expect after = before + 1)\"\nrm -rf \"$L\"\ntail -20 ~/.claude/scripts/logs/aios-audit.log\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n- missing metrics script: `exit=1`, log says `FAIL metrics script errored`, **no** row added\n- live lock: `exit=0`, log says `ABORT live run (pid ...)`, **no** row added\n- stale lock: `exit=0`, log says `RECLAIM stale lock`, **and one row IS added** — `rows_after = rows_before + 1`\n\nThat last line is the whole point of the fix. Round 2 caught that the earlier test removed the lock by hand, which proved nothing about recovery. If a stale lock does not get reclaimed, one crashed run silences the job permanently — fix before loading launchd.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Write the launchd plist**\n\nCreate `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.aiosaudit.plist`. Day 1 at 14:00 — well clear of the 09:00 backup's possible 240-minute window, and the lock covers the rest:\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC \"-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN\"\n  \"http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd\">\n<plist version=\"1.0\">\n<dict>\n  <key>Label</key><string>com.keystone.aiosaudit</string>\n  <key>ProgramArguments</key>\n  <array>\n    <string>/bin/bash</string>\n    <string>-lc</string>\n    <string>$HOME/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh</string>\n  </array>\n  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>\n  <dict>\n    <key>Day</key><integer>1</integer>\n    <key>Hour</key><integer>14</integer>\n    <key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer>\n  </dict>\n  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>\n  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/tmp/com.keystone.aiosaudit.out</string>\n  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/tmp/com.keystone.aiosaudit.err</string>\n</dict>\n</plist>\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Load it and verify launchd accepted it**\n\n```bash\nlaunchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.aiosaudit.plist 2>/dev/null\nlaunchctl load  ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.aiosaudit.plist\nlaunchctl list | grep aiosaudit\n```\n\nExpected: one line ending `com.keystone.aiosaudit`. A non-zero middle column means the last run failed — read `/tmp/com.keystone.aiosaudit.err`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Force a run through launchd, not just bash**\n\n```bash\nlaunchctl start com.keystone.aiosaudit\ncat /tmp/com.keystone.aiosaudit.err\ntail -5 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-trend.md\n```\n\nExpected: `.err` empty, a second row appended. launchd has a different PATH than an interactive shell — this step catches that. If `python3` is not found, put an absolute interpreter in `aios-metrics.py`'s shebang.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: De-duplicate test rows, note the cadence, commit**\n\n```bash\ncd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np = \"docs/audits/aios-trend.md\"\nlines = open(p).read().splitlines()\nseen, out = set(), []\nfor l in lines:\n    if l.startswith(\"| 20\"):\n        if l in seen:\n            continue\n        seen.add(l)\n    out.append(l)\nopen(p, \"w\").write(\"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\")\nEOF\ncat docs/audits/aios-trend.md\ncat >> ~/.claude/rot.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Cadence\n\nMonthly metrics: launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit`, day 1 at 14:00.\nIt writes a trend row and a nudge. It does not commit and does not push.\nThe agentic audit is run by hand: \"audit my AI OS\" in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`.\nEOF\ncp ~/.claude/rot.md docs/rot.md\ngit add scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh docs/audits/aios-trend.md docs/rot.md\ngit commit -m \"feat: monthly AIOS metrics on launchd, no unattended commits\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n```\n\n---","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"90ae4bcb-ab22-48e4-aec9-43f10b46f9cd","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:11:34.466Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- [ ] **Step 2: Run it by hand and verify the trend row**\n\n```bash\n~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\ncat ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-trend.md\ntail -25 ~/.claude/scripts/logs/aios-audit.log\ngit -C ~/DEV/KeystoneOS status --short\n```\n\nExpected: `exit=0`; a header plus one row with **no `MISSING` cells**; the log ends `=== done ok ===`; `git status` shows `aios-trend.md` as **modified but uncommitted** — that is correct, the human commits it.\n\n**A `MISSING` cell means a `get` key does not match a metrics key.** Confirm the two agree before loading launchd — this is how a rename silently kills the job (R7-04):\n\n```bash\ndiff <(python3 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py | cut -d= -f1 | sort) \\\n     <(grep -o '\\$(get [a-z_]*)' ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh \\\n       | sed 's/\\$(get //;s/)//' | sort -u) \\\n  | grep '^>' && echo \"ABOVE: keys the wrapper wants that metrics does not emit\" \\\n  || echo \"every wrapper key is emitted by the metrics script\"\n```\n\nExpected: `every wrapper key is emitted by the metrics script`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Prove the failure paths (R9's masked-failure point)**\n\n```bash\n# A bad metrics script must fail the job, not write a row.\nmv ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py /tmp/aios-metrics.bak\n~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh; echo \"exit=$? (expect 1)\"\nmv /tmp/aios-metrics.bak ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py\n\n# A LIVE lock must make the job stand down.\nL=~/.claude/scripts/.aios-audit.lock\nrm -rf \"$L\"; mkdir -p \"$L\"; echo $$ > \"$L/pid\"     # this shell is alive\n~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh; echo \"exit=$? (expect 0, ABORT live run)\"\nrows_before=$(grep -c '^| 20' ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-trend.md)\n\n# A STALE lock must be RECLAIMED, not wedge the job forever (R2-06).\nrm -rf \"$L\"; mkdir -p \"$L\"; echo 999999 > \"$L/pid\"  # a pid that cannot exist\n~/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh; echo \"exit=$? (expect 0, RECLAIM then run)\"\nrows_after=$(grep -c '^| 20' ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-trend.md)\necho \"rows before=$rows_before after=$rows_after (expect after = before + 1)\"\nrm -rf \"$L\"\ntail -20 ~/.claude/scripts/logs/aios-audit.log\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n- missing metrics script: `exit=1`, log says `FAIL metrics script errored`, **no** row added\n- live lock: `exit=0`, log says `ABORT live run (pid ...)`, **no** row added\n- stale lock: `exit=0`, log says `RECLAIM stale lock`, **and one row IS added** — `rows_after = rows_before + 1`\n\nThat last line is the whole point of the fix. Round 2 caught that the earlier test removed the lock by hand, which proved nothing about recovery. If a stale lock does not get reclaimed, one crashed run silences the job permanently — fix before loading launchd.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Write the launchd plist**\n\nCreate `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.aiosaudit.plist`. Day 1 at 14:00 — well clear of the 09:00 backup's possible 240-minute window, and the lock covers the rest:\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC \"-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN\"\n  \"http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd\">\n<plist version=\"1.0\">\n<dict>\n  <key>Label</key><string>com.keystone.aiosaudit</string>\n  <key>ProgramArguments</key>\n  <array>\n    <string>/bin/bash</string>\n    <string>-lc</string>\n    <string>$HOME/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh</string>\n  </array>\n  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>\n  <dict>\n    <key>Day</key><integer>1</integer>\n    <key>Hour</key><integer>14</integer>\n    <key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer>\n  </dict>\n  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>\n  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/tmp/com.keystone.aiosaudit.out</string>\n  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/tmp/com.keystone.aiosaudit.err</string>\n</dict>\n</plist>\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Load it and verify launchd accepted it**\n\n```bash\nlaunchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.aiosaudit.plist 2>/dev/null\nlaunchctl load  ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.aiosaudit.plist\nlaunchctl list | grep aiosaudit\n```\n\nExpected: one line ending `com.keystone.aiosaudit`. A non-zero middle column means the last run failed — read `/tmp/com.keystone.aiosaudit.err`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Force a run through launchd, not just bash**\n\n```bash\nlaunchctl start com.keystone.aiosaudit\ncat /tmp/com.keystone.aiosaudit.err\ntail -5 ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-trend.md\n```\n\nExpected: `.err` empty, a second row appended. launchd has a different PATH than an interactive shell — this step catches that. If `python3` is not found, put an absolute interpreter in `aios-metrics.py`'s shebang.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: De-duplicate test rows, note the cadence, commit**\n\n```bash\ncd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np = \"docs/audits/aios-trend.md\"\nlines = open(p).read().splitlines()\nseen, out = set(), []\nfor l in lines:\n    if l.startswith(\"| 20\"):\n        if l in seen:\n            continue\n        seen.add(l)\n    out.append(l)\nopen(p, \"w\").write(\"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\")\nEOF\ncat docs/audits/aios-trend.md\ncat >> ~/.claude/rot.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Cadence\n\nMonthly metrics: launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit`, day 1 at 14:00.\nIt writes a trend row and a nudge. It does not commit and does not push.\nThe agentic audit is run by hand: \"audit my AI OS\" in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`.\nEOF\ncp ~/.claude/rot.md docs/rot.md\ngit add scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh docs/audits/aios-trend.md docs/rot.md\ngit commit -m \"feat: monthly AIOS metrics on launchd, no unattended commits\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n```\n\n---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0c527960-9e39-41d2-9af2-f5f3976c495b","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"ext