nstalls the audit reports but never touches (R2-02) |\n| `pool_dangling` / `codex_dangling` | `0` | abandoned links from a deleted canonical skill — invisible to every other check (R5-01) |\n| `project_skills` | `2` | `os-audit` + `aios-audit` |\n| `portability_failures` | `0` | Task 5 passed |\n\nA non-zero `*_drift` means someone edited a generated view instead of the canonical source — fix before continuing. A large `*_third_party` is expected and correct; it is a number to watch, not a failure. `no_manifest` in either drift field means `sync-to-codex.sh` has not run since Task 3.\n\n-----\n- [ ] **Step 5: Cross-reference `os-audit` so the two do not fight**\n\nAdd near the top of `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md`:\n\n```markdown\n> Scope note: this skill audits **project data** — routing, indexes, freshness,\n> duplication. The harness layer (skills, agents, hooks, rules, cross-harness\n> parity) belongs to `aios-audit`, which calls this skill for the data layer.\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Smoke-test end to end**\n\nIn a Claude Code session with cwd `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`, run `/reload-skills`, then type \"audit my AI OS\". Expected: `aios-audit` fires, reads `rot.md`, runs the metrics script, produces a report, and ends with exactly two proposals.\n\n```bash\nls -l ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-audit-*.md\ngrep -c 'unknown' ~/.claude/rot.md\n```\n\nExpected: a report file exists. The `unknown` count should have **dropped** by exactly the number of layers whose checks ran — not to zero.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Commit**\n\n```bash\ncd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS\ncp ~/.claude/rot.md docs/rot.md\ngit add .claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md .claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md \\\n        scripts/aios-metrics.py docs/rot.md docs/audits/\ngit commit -m \"feat: aios-audit compound skill + rot.md decay tiers\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\n```\n\n---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceTo