{"parentUuid":"00080bf8-31de-43b7-88b1-ded82849e37b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88b6ccb8-7105-4de5-afa1-ccbae8a94e54","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"BLOCKED by dcg\n\nTip: dcg explain \"cd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS; echo \\\"launchd:\\\"; launchctl list | grep -E 'aiosaudit|dailybackup'; plutil -lint ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.aiosaudit.plist; echo \\\"err file bytes:\\\"; wc -c /tmp/com.keystone.aiosaudit.err 2>&1; echo \\\"wrapper keys missing from metrics:\\\"; python3 scripts/aios-metrics.py | cut -d= -f1 | sort > ~/.claude/jobs/9823c1f0/tmp/mkeys.txt 2>/dev/null; grep -o '\\$(get [a-z_]*)' scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh | sed 's/\\$(get //;s/)//' | sort -u | comm -13 ~/.claude/jobs/9823c1f0/tmp/mkeys.txt - ; echo \\\"(end)\\\"; echo \\\"rot cadence:\\\"; grep -n \\\"Cadence\\|aiosaudit\\\" ~/.claude/rot.md docs/rot.md; cmp ~/.claude/rot.md docs/rot.md && echo \\\"rot copies identical\\\"; echo \\\"os-audit xref:\\\"; grep -n \\\"aios-audit\\\" .claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md\"\n\nReason: shell truncating redirect (including arbitrary numeric, named, and PowerShell all-stream forms) to a sensitive system or home path destroys the previous file contents. EXTREMELY DANGEROUS.\n\nExplanation: `> /etc/passwd` (or `: > /etc/passwd`, `echo > /etc/passwd`, etc.) opens the target file with O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_TRUNC — the contents are destroyed before any write happens. This applies equally to `>|` (force-overwrite), `&>` / `>&` (stdout+stderr to file), and numbered FD forms (`1>`, `2>`, `1>|`, `2>|`). All of these are silent, immediate, irrecoverable.\n             \n             There is NO recovery without backups.\n             \n             Safer alternatives:\n             - Use append (`>>`) to preserve existing content: `echo line >> <file>`.\n             - Make a backup: `cp <file> <file>.bak && echo data > <file>`.\n             - For temp scratch: `> /tmp/<subdir>/scratch` is allowed.\n             - Read redirects (`< <file>`) are not affected — they don't truncate.\n\nRule: core.filesystem:redirect-truncate-root-home\n\nIf this operation is truly needed, ask the user for explicit permission and have them run the command manually.","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TLdjDSiyTJtYtrM2VAeAqA"}]},"uuid":"0b221da4-c0d1-4e40-beb3-7b9076120768","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:11:50.418Z","toolUseResult":"Error: BLOCKED by dcg\n\nTip: dcg explain \"cd ~/DEV/KeystoneOS; echo \\\"launchd:\\\"; launchctl list | grep -E 'aiosaudit|dailybackup'; plutil -lint ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.aiosaudit.plist; echo \\\"err file bytes:\\\"; wc -c /tmp/com.keystone.aiosaudit.err 2>&1; echo \\\"wrapper keys missing from metrics:\\\"; python3 scripts/aios-metrics.py | cut -d= -f1 | sort > ~/.claude/jobs/9823c1f0/tmp/mkeys.txt 2>/dev/null; grep -o '\\$(get [a-z_]*)' scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh | sed 's/\\$(get //;s/)//' | sort -u | comm -13 ~/.claude/jobs/9823c1f0/tmp/mkeys.txt - ; echo \\\"(end)\\\"; echo \\\"rot cadence:\\\"; grep -n \\\"Cadence\\|aiosaudit\\\" ~/.claude/rot.md docs/rot.md; cmp ~/.claude/rot.md docs/rot.md && echo \\\"rot copies identical\\\"; echo \\\"os-audit xref:\\\"; grep -n \\\"aios-audit\\\" .claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md\"\n\nReason: shell truncating redirect (including arbitrary numeric, named, and PowerShell all-stream forms) to a sensitive system or home path destroys the previous file contents. EXTREMELY DANGEROUS.\n\nExplanation: `> /etc/passwd` (or `: > /etc/passwd`, `echo > /etc/passwd`, etc.) opens the target file with O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_TRUNC — the contents are destroyed before any write happens. This applies equally to `>|` (force-overwrite), `&>` / `>&` (stdout+stderr to file), and numbered FD forms (`1>`, `2>`, `1>|`, `2>|`). All of these are silent, immediate, irrecoverable.\n             \n             There is NO recovery without backups.\n             \n             Safer alternatives:\n             - Use append (`>>`) to preserve existing content: `echo line >> <file>`.\n             - Make a backup: `cp <file> <file>.bak && echo data > <file>`.\n             - For temp scratch: `> /tmp/<subdir>/scratch` is allowed.\n             - Read redirects (`< <file>`) are not affected — they don't truncate.\n\nRule: core.filesystem:redirect-truncate-root-home\n\nIf this operation is truly needed, ask the user for explicit permission and have them run the command manually.","toolDenialKind":"permission-rule","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"00080bf8-31de-43b7-88b1-ded82849e37b","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
