{"parentUuid":"8902b4d6-42dc-4ec8-b0a8-4a39215ac317","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cezwh391cXSJ1DUTTNgHV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All Task 6–7 checks pass again — launchd jobs loaded, plist valid, keys aligned, cadence documented — though no audit report exists yet and rot.md still shows 12 unknown rows. Now writing the Tasks 6–7/Gate C log entry and copying the Pi trial report into the repo.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_read_input_tokens":134440,"output_tokens":4362,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":825},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1001,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":4362,"cache_read_input_tokens":134440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1001},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CezwgyQXTjr1mE5h9cp2x","type":"assistant","uuid":"8ffa3962-b35f-419c-a808-4e0dfc8a789d","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:12:14.181Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8ffa3962-b35f-419c-a808-4e0dfc8a789d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cezwh391cXSJ1DUTTNgHV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lks8S3zfp696Lm1Ej9cUmc","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md","old_string":"- **S2-02 / K2-02 open:** the 7-skill roster decision. Details: `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/gateB-dispositions-r2.md`.","new_string":"- **S2-02 / K2-02 open:** the 7-skill roster decision. Details: `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/gateB-dispositions-r2.md`.\n\n## Task 6 — evidence (`8773ff2`)\n\n| Step | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | `~/.claude/rot.md` written; `docs/rot.md` is its committed copy (`cmp` identical, re-checked 2026-09-13). |\n| 2–3 | `aios-metrics.py` prints `key=value` only, exit 0. `canonical_skills=42`, `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical=0`, `third_party_links_in_canonical=19`, drift 0/0, dangling 0/0, `project_skills=2`. **Deviation:** `portability_failures=7`, not the plan's `0` — the open roster decision from Gate B. Also reports `error_rc<N>` unless the checker exits 0 or 1 (K2-03). |\n| 4 | `.claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md` written. Beyond the plan's required parts it adds a `skillOverrides` parity check, a hooks name diff, Examples and Gotchas. Frontmatter verbatim. |\n| 5 | `os-audit` SKILL.md carries the scope note pointing the harness layer at `aios-audit` (line 11). |\n| 6 | **Partly verified only.** A background job cannot run `/reload-skills` or an interactive session. Substitute: headless `claude -p \"audit my AI OS\"` in this repo, 3-turn cap, `--disallowedTools Bash`. It listed and fired `aios-audit`, read `rot.md`, and ran the metrics — through the context-mode MCP shell, which `--disallowedTools Bash` does not block. It wrote nothing: no `docs/audits/aios-audit-*.md` exists and `rot.md` still has 12 `unknown`. **The plan's expectation (a report, two proposals, fewer `unknown`) is unverified. Eric runs \"audit my AI OS\" interactively in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`.** |\n| 7 | Committed `8773ff2`. |\n\n## Task 7 — evidence (`08bf6e8`)\n\n| Step | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | `scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh` written. |\n| 2 | Hand run exit 0; full row, no `MISSING`; log ends `=== done ok ===`. Key check: every `$(get …)` key is emitted by the metrics script (re-checked 2026-09-13: none missing). |\n| 3 | Failure paths via `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t7-failpaths.py` (os calls, because `dcg` blocks `mv`/`rm -rf` on variable paths): missing metrics exit 1 no row; live lock exit 0 `ABORT live run` no row; stale lock exit 0 `RECLAIM stale lock` one row. |\n| 4 | `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.aiosaudit.plist` byte-identical to the plan block; `plutil -lint` OK. |\n| 5 | Loaded. `launchctl list` shows `-  0  com.keystone.aiosaudit`. |\n| 6 | `launchctl start` run: exit 0, `/tmp/com.keystone.aiosaudit.err` empty (0 bytes), row written. |\n| 7 | Test rows de-duplicated to one (`2026-09-12`); cadence appended to `rot.md` and copied; committed `08bf6e8`. Daily backup `com.keystone.dailybackup` reloaded, last exit 0. |\n\n## Gate C — round 1 (`767b3de`..`08bf6e8`)\n\nCodex inspection: **REVISE**, three medium. All accepted.\n\n| ID | Finding | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| C-01 | Scripts recorded as 100644; the plist executes the wrapper directly, so a fresh clone fails | `77d9ecc`: all three scripts 100755 in the index (`core.fileMode=false` had hidden it) |\n| C-02 | Stale-lock reclaim not atomic: two runs can both reclaim, both write rows, and one trap frees the other's lock | `dae7aeb`: a second atomic lock `$LOCK.recover` (stale after 10 min) serialises reclaim; owner re-read while holding it; EXIT trap frees only a lock whose pid is `$$` |\n| C-03 | `never_used` counts Claude transcripts only, swallows read errors, yet the audit read it as \"never invoked across all sessions\" | `dae7aeb`: new keys `usage_scope=claude_code_transcripts_only`, `usage_unreadable_transcripts=N`; the skill forbids DELETE on `never_used` alone and gives the `~/.codex/sessions` grep |\n\nHost verification, 2026-09-13: C-03 probe (one mode-000 transcript → count 0 → 1, probe removed). `t7-failpaths.py` extended to 9 probes, **all PASS**: the original three; lock and `.recover` released; two concurrent runs on one stale lock, with and without a 3 s pause inside the recovery section → exit 0/0, exactly one row, one RECLAIM, nothing left behind; an 11-minute-old `.recover` reclaimed; a fresh `.recover` respected (no row). Test rows and the nudge were undone by restoring `aios-trend.md` and `.errors.log` from pre-test copies.\n\nRound 2 (independent re-inspection of `767b3de`..HEAD by Codex): result recorded below when it returns.\n\n## Task 8 — BLOCKED at Step 1\n\n`id piuser` → `no such user` (2026-09-13). Creating it needs `sudo`; background sessions cannot. Report: `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pi-trial.md`. Eric's `/opt/homebrew/bin/pi` was not used."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_read_input_tokens":134440,"output_tokens":4362,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":825},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1001,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":4362,"cache_read_input_tokens":134440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1001},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CezwgyQXTjr1mE5h9cp2x","type":"assistant","uuid":"c632a2bf-2db4-4bbe-b1a2-f8fee7ad3a7d","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:12:36.854Z","advisorModel":"cla