lock` one row. |","+| 4 | `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.aiosaudit.plist` byte-identical to the plan block; `plutil -lint` OK. |","+| 5 | Loaded. `launchctl list` shows `-  0  com.keystone.aiosaudit`. |","+| 6 | `launchctl start` run: exit 0, `/tmp/com.keystone.aiosaudit.err` empty (0 bytes), row written. |","+| 7 | Test rows de-duplicated to one (`2026-09-12`); cadence appended to `rot.md` and copied; committed `08bf6e8`. Daily backup `com.keystone.dailybackup` reloaded, last exit 0. |","+","+## Gate C — round 1 (`767b3de`..`08bf6e8`)","+","+Codex inspection: **REVISE**, three medium. All accepted.","+","+| ID | Finding | Fix |","+|---|---|---|","+| C-01 | Scripts recorded as 100644; the plist executes the wrapper directly, so a fresh clone fails | `77d9ecc`: all three scripts 100755 in the index (`core.fileMode=false` had hidden it) |","+| C-02 | Stale-lock reclaim not atomic: two runs can both reclaim, both write rows, and one trap frees the other's lock | `dae7aeb`: a second atomic lock `$LOCK.recover` (stale after 10 min) serialises reclaim; owner re-read while holding it; EXIT trap frees only a lock whose pid is `$$` |","+| C-03 | `never_used` counts Claude transcripts only, swallows read errors, yet the audit read it as \"never invoked across all sessions\" | `dae7aeb`: new keys `usage_scope=claude_code_transcripts_only`, `usage_unreadable_transcripts=N`; the skill forbids DELETE on `never_used` alone and gives the `~/.codex/sessions` grep |","+","+Host verification, 2026-09-13: C-03 probe (one mode-000 transcript → count 0 → 1, probe removed). `t7-failpaths.py` extended to 9 probes, **all PASS**: the original three; lock and `.recover` released; two concurrent runs on one stale lock, with and without a 3 s pause inside the recovery section → exit 0/0, exactly one row, one RECLAIM, nothing left behind; an 11-minute-old `.recover` reclaimed; a fresh `.recover` respected (no row). Test rows and the nudge were undone by restoring `aios-trend.md` and `.errors.log` from pre-test copies.","+","+Round 2 (independent re-inspection of `767b3de`..HEAD by Codex): result recorded below when it returns.","+","+## Task 8 — BLOCKED at Step 1","+","+`id piuser` → `no such user` (2026-09-13). Creating it needs `sudo`; background sessions cannot. Report: `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pi-trial.md`. Eric's `/opt/homebrew/bin/pi` was not used."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c632a2bf-2db4-4bbe-b1a2-f8fee7ad3a7d","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"84278f7b-5719-442b-84ba-bc5c347f3653","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cezwh391cXSJ1DUTTNgHV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HQfNj2ikAUhrtPhuciiP1q","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-pi-trial.md","content":"# Pi trial - 2026-09-12\n\nBoundary: separate macOS user `piuser`, no read access to the operator home.\n`cd` into a directory is NOT a boundary and was not treated as one (R5).\n\n**Verdict: BLOCKED at Step 1.** Creating `piuser` needs `sudo`, and this plan ran as a\nnon-interactive background session: `sudo -n true` → \"a password is required\". The plan's\nstop condition applies (\"If the user cannot be created ... stop and write up what failed\").\nNothing was installed and no Pi process was run. Eric's own `/opt/homebrew/bin/pi` was left\nuntouched on purpose: it auto-discovers Eric's real pool, so it is not the trial binary.\nRe-checked 2026-09-13: `id piuser` → `no such user`. Still blocked.\n\n| Question | Answer |\n|---|---|\n| pi version | not reached (Step 1) — the trial installs its own copy under `/Users/piuser/.npm-global` |\n| piuser blocked from ~/DEV and ~/SecondBrain? | not reached (Step 1). Pre-check: `ls -ld ~` = `drwxr-x---+ kristinarash staff`, so a `piuser` in group `staff` WOULD read `~` through the group bits — the plan's own-group step (GID 4242, confirmed unused) is required, not optional |\n| skills auto-discovered | not reached (Step 1). Expected value to compare against: `pool_skills=210` (Task 4 Step 6) |\n| skills needing edits to fire in Pi | not reached (Step 1) |\n| extension contract matched the research note? | not reached (Step 1). Guard staged byte-for-byte from the plan (factory + `pi.on('tool_call')` + `event.input`) |\n| minutes to port the dcg guard | not reached (Step 1) |\n| hooks still to port | not reached (Step 1); inventory today: 61 in `~/.claude/hooks`, 59 in `~/.codex/hooks` (the two copies differ by 2) |\n| verdict | BLOCKED |\n\n## What the guard proved\n\nNothing yet — the guard needs the boundary user first. Probes A/B/C in plan Step 6 are unchanged.\n\n## To unblock (Eric, in a terminal — about 2 minutes)\n\nRun plan Task 8 Step 1 exactly. It prompts for your password:\n\n```bash\nsudo sysadminctl -addUser piuser -fullName \"Pi Trial\" -password - -home /Users/piuser\nsudo dscl . -create /Groups/pitrial\nsudo dscl . -create /Groups/pitrial PrimaryGroupID 4242\nsudo dscl . -create /Users/piuser PrimaryGroupID 4242\nid piuser\ndseditgroup -o checkmember -m piuser staff\nsudo -u piuser ls ~/DEV          2>&1 | tail -2\nsudo -u piuser ls ~/SecondBrain  2>&1 | tail -2\n```\n\nBoth `ls` lines must print **Permission denied**; `id piuser` must not list `staff(20)`.\nThen a session can run Steps 2-8 (Steps 2, 3, 6 and 8 also use `sudo`, so they need an\ninteractive session or a sudo-capable one).\n\n## What a real adoption would still need\n\nNot in scope here. At minimum: a boundary design that is not a second user\naccount, an approval-prompt layer, and a port of the remaining hooks.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_read_input_tokens":134440,"output_tokens":4362,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":825},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1001,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":4362,"cache_read_input_tokens":134440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1001},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CezwgyQX