{"parentUuid":"c3b20b28-6f27-4ee3-bb26-4df39c8c2ddf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88b6ccb8-7105-4de5-afa1-ccbae8a94e54","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HYyFakfgXt8WgkTszEE348","type":"tool_result","content":"f58187c docs(audit): log Tasks 6-7, Gate C round 1; Task 8 blocked at Step 1\n        \"evidence\": \"The carried-forward roster defect remains unresolved: ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review, pp-espn, and session-miner are disabled through Claude's skillOverrides while published to the other views. The settings and recorded trend corroborate the seven failures. This contradicts the plan's identical-loading goal and zero-failure gate, even though it is not a newly introduced Gate C defect.\",\n        \"fix\": \"Resolve the seven roster choices: re-enable retained skills in Claude or retire them from canonical and regenerate the views. Alternatively, explicitly revise the parity requirement and approval scope to permit these intentional differences.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"coverage\": [\n      \"Read all eight changed files, the supplied plan and diff, and host dispositions; confirmed the on-disk plan SHA-256 matches the requested hash.\",\n      \"Inspected cron locking, metric consumption, trend and nudge writes, and the installed launchd plist.\",\n      \"Traced shared error-log interactions through daily-backup.ps1, the session-start snapshot hook, and keystone-reconcile.ps1.\",\n      \"Inspected sync manifest publication references, Claude override settings, checker-to-metrics error propagation, and tracked executable modes.\"\n    ],\n    \"limitations\": [\n      \"Static inspection only; no files edited, tests run, or work delegated. Host-reported test results were not independently reproduced.\",\n      \"Windows filesystem behavior, Pi isolation, and live harness discovery were not exercised.\",\n      \"The recovery-lock timeout retains the concurrency risk explicitly accepted in the host dispositions.\",\n      \"The external skills repository received targeted inspection, not a complete implementation review.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"input_tokens\": 508633,\n    \"cached_input_tokens\": 391552,\n    \"cache_write_input_tokens\": 0,\n    \"output_tokens\": 1257,\n    \"reasoning_output_tokens\": 61\n  },\n  \"observed_models\": [],\n  \"elapsed_seconds\": 61.21\n}\n\n\n[exited with code 0]\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/9823c1f0/tmp/gateC2-keystone/claudex-b75aanbe/result.json\n{\n \"verdict\": \"REVISE\",\n \"summary\": \"The executable-mode fix and ordinary stale-lock recovery are present. Roster parity remains unresolved, and the portability checker still accepts non-string descriptions.\",\n \"findings\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"IR-01\",\n   \"severity\": \"medium\",\n   \"path\": \"scripts/skill-portability-check.py:181\",\n   \"evidence\": \"A skill with a matching name and `description: [Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.]` passes the check by static inspection: scalar() treats the sequence as text, clause_problems() finds both clauses, and _flow_sequence() accepts it. The YAML value is a list, violating the required description-string contract. The checker can therefore report portable for an unloadable skill.\",\n   \"fix\": \"Validate the types of required fields before checking their content. Reject sequences and mappings for name and description; extract their actual scalar values rather than interpreting raw YAML text as a string.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"IR-02\",\n   \"severity\": \"medium\",\n   \"path\": \"docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md:224\",\n   \"evidence\": \"The carried-forward roster defect remains unresolved: ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review, pp-espn, and session-miner are disabled through Claude's skillOverrides while published to the other views. The settings and recorded trend corroborate the seven failures. This contradicts the plan's identical-loading goal and zero-failure gate, even though it is not a newly introduced Gate C defect.\",\n   \"fix\": \"Resolve the seven roster choices: re-enable retained skills in Claude or retire them from canonical and regenerate the views. Alternatively, explicitly revise the parity requirement and approval scope to permit these intentional differences.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"coverage\": [\n  \"Read all eight changed files, the supplied plan and diff, and host dispositions; confirmed the on-disk plan SHA-256 matches the requested hash.\",\n  \"Inspected cron locking, metric consumption, trend and nudge writes, and the installed launchd plist.\",\n  \"Traced shared error-log interactions through daily-backup.ps1, the session-start snapshot hook, and keystone-reconcile.ps1.\",\n  \"Inspected sync manifest publication references, Claude override settings, checker-to-metrics error propagation, and tracked executable modes.\"\n ],\n \"limitations\": [\n  \"Static inspection only; no files edited, tests run, or work delegated. Host-reported test results were not independently reproduced.\",\n  \"Windows filesystem behavior, Pi isolation, and live harness discovery were not exercised.\",\n  \"The recovery-lock timeout retains the concurrency risk explicitly accepted in the host dispositions.\",\n  \"The external skills repository received targeted inspection, not a complete implementation review.\"\n ]\n}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"86c14585-f467-4d43-8d4d-e82ba2f77c7d","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:12:57.476Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"f58187c docs(audit): log Tasks 6-7, Gate C round 1; Task 8 blocked at Step 1\n        \"evidence\": \"The carried-forward roster defect remains unresolved: ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review, pp-espn, and session-miner are disabled through Claude's skillOverrides while published to the other views. The settings and recorded trend corroborate the seven failures. This contradicts the plan's identical-loading goal and zero-failure gate, even though it is not a n