{"parentUuid":"9fa849bc-2e05-4df8-8a1a-20e319b68cfb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezwuMjni7xKzqzyW23J3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U3MGojKgaixXSxALtaPU4D","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md","old_string":"Round 2 (independent re-inspection of `767b3de`..HEAD by Codex): result recorded below when it returns.","new_string":"## Gate C — round 2 (2026-09-13)\n\nFresh Codex inspections, one per repo, with the Gate B r2 and Gate C dispositions as feedback.\n\n| Repo (base) | Verdict | Findings |\n|---|---|---|\n| KeystoneOS (`767b3de`) | REVISE | **IR-01 medium:** the checker accepted `description: [Use when … Do not use …]` — a list, not a string. **IR-02:** roster parity still open. No finding against C-01, C-02 or C-03; the recovery-lock residual risk is noted as accepted. |\n| claude-skills (`8c6bb7a`, covers `7459560`) | REVISE | **S3-01:** roster parity still open. The S2-01 linked-manifest fix was confirmed for both twins. No new code defect. |\n\n**IR-01 fixed** (commit after `f58187c`): `value_kind()` reads the YAML node type of `name` and `description` before any content check; a sequence or mapping (flow or block, any indent) is reported once and not content-checked. Host-verified with `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t5f-checker-test.py`: 24/24 fixtures (16 carried from t5e, 6 new wrong-type cases, 2 string controls); value kinds and syntax verdicts agree with PyYAML on all 42 real skills; real roster still exactly the 7 override failures; fail-closed 4/4 exit 2, control exit 0; older fixture homes unchanged. **Not independently re-inspected.**\n\n**Only open item from Gate C: the 7-skill roster decision (IR-02 = S3-01 = S2-02 = K2-02).** It is a choice, not a code defect."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_detai