nspected.**\n\n**Only open item from Gate C: the 7-skill roster decision (IR-02 = S3-01 = S2-02 = K2-02).** It is a choice, not a code defect.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":260,"oldLines":8,"newStart":260,"newLines":19,"lines":[" "," Host verification, 2026-09-13: C-03 probe (one mode-000 transcript → count 0 → 1, probe removed). `t7-failpaths.py` extended to 9 probes, **all PASS**: the original three; lock and `.recover` released; two concurrent runs on one stale lock, with and without a 3 s pause inside the recovery section → exit 0/0, exactly one row, one RECLAIM, nothing left behind; an 11-minute-old `.recover` reclaimed; a fresh `.recover` respected (no row). Test rows and the nudge were undone by restoring `aios-trend.md` and `.errors.log` from pre-test copies."," ","-Round 2 (independent re-inspection of `767b3de`..HEAD by Codex): result recorded below when it returns.","+## Gate C — round 2 (2026-09-13)"," ","+Fresh Codex inspections, one per repo, with the Gate B r2 and Gate C dispositions as feedback.","+","+| Repo (base) | Verdict | Findings |","+|---|---|---|","+| KeystoneOS (`767b3de`) | REVISE | **IR-01 medium:** the checker accepted `description: [Use when … Do not use …]` — a list, not a string. **IR-02:** roster parity still open. No finding against C-01, C-02 or C-03; the recovery-lock residual risk is noted as accepted. |","+| claude-skills (`8c6bb7a`, covers `7459560`) | REVISE | **S3-01:** roster parity still open. The S2-01 linked-manifest fix was confirmed for both twins. No new code defect. |","+","+**IR-01 fixed** (commit after `f58187c`): `value_kind()` reads the YAML node type of `name` and `description` before any content check; a sequence or mapping (flow or block, any indent) is reported once and not content-checked. Host-verified with `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t5f-checker-test.py`: 24/24 fixtures (16 carried from t5e, 6 new wrong-type cases, 2 string controls); value kinds and syntax verdicts agree with PyYAML on all 42 real skills; real roster still exactly the 7 override failures; fail-closed 4/4 exit 2, control exit 0; older fixture homes unchanged. **Not independently re-inspected.**","+","+**Only open item from Gate C: the 7-skill roster decision (IR-02 = S3-01 = S2-02 = K2-02).** It is a choice, not a code defect.","+"," ## Task 8 — BLOCKED at Step 1"," "," `id piuser` → `no such user` (2026-09-13). Creating it needs `sudo`; background sessions cannot. Report: `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pi-trial.md`. Eric's `/opt/homebrew/bin/pi` was not used."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d84596a-62a4-43c0-a13f-4de60d85b2f8","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"9c0ef665-db41-4bbb-a472-06f2e319d0cb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezwuMjni7xKzqzyW23J3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RwUUy9VC23NnjdeYkm5pUU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md","content":"# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\nLast updated 2026-09-13 (Mac, background session). Evidence for every claim below is in\n`docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md`.\n\n## Current state\n- The dominant thread is the **harness-agnostic AIOS plan**:\n  `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md` (approved; do not edit —\n  its SHA-256 `71b5242e…` binds the approval). Goal: every skill Eric owns loads\n  identically in Claude Code, Codex and Pi from one versioned canonical folder, plus a\n  recurring audit that keeps the AIOS from rotting.\n- Architecture: `~/.claude/skills/` (repo `erash11/claude-skills`) is canonical and holds\n  real directories only. `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are generated views\n  rebuilt per machine by `sync-to-codex.sh` / `.ps1` — symlinks on Mac, copies on Windows.\n- **Tasks 1–7 done.** Task 8 (Pi trial) **BLOCKED** at Step 1: it needs `sudo` to create\n  `piuser`. Report: `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pi-trial.md`.\n- **Gate B** (2 rounds) and **Gate C** (2 rounds) run. Every code finding is fixed:\n  C-01 exec bits, C-02 atomic stale-lock reclaim, C-03 usage metrics scoped to Claude\n  transcripts, IR-01 checker rejects list/map descriptions. IR-01 is host-tested but\n  not re-inspected by Codex.\n- Monthly metrics run on launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit` (day 1, 14:00). It writes a row\n  to `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` and a nudge; it never commits.\n- `portability_failures=7`: the open roster decision below. Every other invariant is 0.\n\n## Next\n- **Eric decides the roster** (see Open questions). Then re-run\n  `python3 scripts/skill-portability-check.py` — it should reach 0 failing.\n- **Eric runs \"audit my AI OS\"** interactively in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`. The Task 6 smoke\n  test was headless and wrote no report, so the full audit flow is unverified.\n- **Task 8:** run plan Task 8 Step 1 in a terminal (commands in the Pi trial report),\n  then a sudo-capable session runs Steps 2–8. Or accept BLOCKED.\n- Gate D (verification before completion) after those.\n\n## Open questions\n- **Roster:** 7 owned skills are `\"off\"` in `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides` but\n  published to Codex and Pi: ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review,\n  pp-espn, session-miner. Re-enable them in Claude Code, or retire them from canonical.\n  Flagged by Codex in every review round since Gate B.\n\n## Gotchas\n- Never commit a symlink into `~/.claude/skills/`. Windows pulls that repo and an absolute\n  Mac symlink arrives unusable. A pre-commit hook refuses it.\n- Hooks and sync scripts exist in two copies (`~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/`; `.sh`\n  and `.ps1`). Any change patches both.\n- Never run `graphify install --platform agents`: the views link into canonical, so it\n  overwrites the Claude variant. Use `--platform claude` only.\n- `never_used` in the metrics is **Claude Code evidence only**. Check `~/.codex/sessions`\n  before recommending any deletion.\n- `claude -p --disallowedTools Bash` does not block the context-mode MCP shell tools.\n- A concurrent `closeout` commits whatever is uncommitted. Commit at each verified step.\n- `dcg` blocks: `rm -rf` in heredocs, `mv` and `>` redirects on home paths, `git` inside\n  command substitution. Use the Write tool plus a Python file that does the I/O.\n- Never point Pi at `~/DEV` — it ships no sandbox and no approval prompts, by design.\n- Never let any harness near `DexaProject` (identifiable athlete health data, on Google\n  Drive, not in `~/DEV`).\n- Plugin skills (`superpowers`, `mattpocock-skills`) are vendored and out of scope.\n- On the Mac: `timeout` is not installed and Python is PEP 668-managed (stdlib `python3`\n  or `uv`, never global `pip install`).\n- No success claim without pasted command output.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2585,"cache_read_input_tokens":163711,"output_tokens":3730,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":907},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2585,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":3730,"cache_read_input_tokens":163711,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2585,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2585},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CezwuKiF56mc5JHJMFQWy","type":"assistant","uuid":"92a78c18-3b89-48de-bce7-cd8c7701a10b","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:15:31.925Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
