ipts/skill-portability-check.py` — it should reach 0 failing.","+- **Eric runs \"audit my AI OS\"** interactively in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`. The Task 6 smoke","+  test was headless and wrote no report, so the full audit flow is unverified.","+- **Task 8:** run plan Task 8 Step 1 in a terminal (commands in the Pi trial report),","+  then a sudo-capable session runs Steps 2–8. Or accept BLOCKED.","+- Gate D (verification before completion) after those."," "," ## Open questions","-- None recorded in the plan. Round 6 closed with no material unresolved defects in scope.","+- **Roster:** 7 owned skills are `\"off\"` in `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides` but","+  published to Codex and Pi: ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review,","+  pp-espn, session-miner. Re-enable them in Claude Code, or retire them from canonical.","+  Flagged by Codex in every review round since Gate B."," "," ## Gotchas"," - Never commit a symlink into `~/.claude/skills/`. Windows pulls that repo and an absolute","-  Mac symlink arrives unusable.","+  Mac symlink arrives unusable. A pre-commit hook refuses it."," - Hooks and sync scripts exist in two copies (`~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/`; `.sh`","   and `.ps1`). Any change patches both.","-- Global `MEMORY.md` is at 2,489 of 2,500 chars. Consolidate before adding to it.","-- Never point Pi at `~/DEV` - it ships no sandbox and no approval prompts, by design.","+- Never run `graphify install --platform agents`: the views link into canonical, so it","+  overwrites the Claude variant. Use `--platform claude` only.","+- `never_used` in the metrics is **Claude Code evidence only**. Check `~/.codex/sessions`","+  before recommending any deletion.","+- `claude -p --disallowedTools Bash` does not block the context-mode MCP shell tools.","+- A concurrent `closeout` commits whatever is uncommitted. Commit at each verified step.","+- `dcg` blocks: `rm -rf` in heredocs, `mv` and `>` redirects on home paths, `git` inside","+  command substitution. Use the Write tool plus a Python file that does the I/O.","+- Never point Pi at `~/DEV` — it ships no sandbox and no approval prompts, by design."," - Never let any harness near `DexaProject` (identifiable athlete health data, on Google","   Drive, not in `~/DEV`)."," - Plugin skills (`superpowers`, `mattpocock-skills`) are vendored and out of scope.","-- **Windows:** four vendored skills (`claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`,","-  `codex-review`) are committed to `claude-skills` as symlinks. On Windows they arrive","-  pointing at a path that does not exist. AMEND-01 in Task 4 untracks them.","-- On the Mac: `timeout` is not installed, `dcg` blocks `find ... -delete`, and Python is","-  PEP 668-managed (stdlib `python3` or `uv`, never global `pip install`).","+- On the Mac: `timeout` is not installed and Python is PEP 668-managed (stdlib `python3`","+  or `uv`, never global `pip install`)."," - No success claim without pasted command output."]}],"originalFile":"# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n<!-- Filled 2026-09-12 by dev-sync on Windows, reconstructed from git history and the\n     AIOS plan. It was an empty migration stub before this. Verify before relying on it. -->\n\n## Current state\n- The dominant thread is the **harness-agnostic AIOS plan**:\n  `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`. Goal is that every skill\n  Eric owns loads identically in Claude Code, Codex and Pi from one versioned canonical\n  folder, plus a recurring audit that keeps the AIOS from rotting.\n- Architecture: `~/.claude/skills/` (repo `erash11/claude-skills`) is canonical and holds\n  real directories only. `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are generated views\n  rebuilt per machine by `sync-to-codex.sh` / `.ps1` - symlinks on Mac, copies on Windows.\n- Codex approved the plan on round 6 (findings 10 -> 9 -> 7 -> 4 -> 1 -> 0), then a\n  round-7 pass (R7-01..R7-05) folded in one declared vendor inventory everywhere.\n- **2026-09-12 afternoon, Mac: Task 1 (snapshot and freeze, plus AMEND-01) and Task 2\n  (prune the stale pool mirror, 306 -> 208) are complete.** Task 2 archived 98 skills\n  that were still live in `~/.agents/skills`. Reversible. Audit records are in\n  `docs/audits/2026-09-12-*.txt`.\n- The approval was a static, read-only review. It is an approved plan, not proven\n  behaviour. Gates B, C and D still apply.\n- Also landed recently: daily-backup schedule aligned with launchd (00:30 -> 09:00), a\n  stale Windows duplicate of `reMarkale_extract` dropped, and a corrupt\n  `memsearch-sync.ps1.from-mac` removed.\n\n## Next\n- **Task 3: harden the sync writers before anything moves** (`sync-to-codex.sh` and the\n  `.ps1` twin). Then Task 4 (invert the outward symlinks, publish the views) and Task 5\n  (portable frontmatter).\n- Gate B is a `codex-review` after Task 5. Gate C comes after Task 7, Gate D before\n  declaring done.\n- Plan checkboxes are not being ticked (Task 1 still shows unchecked). Commit messages\n  are the reliable progress record.\n\n## Open questions\n- None recorded in the plan. Round 6 closed with no material unresolved defects in scope.\n\n## Gotchas\n- Never commit a symlink into `~/.claude/skills/`. Windows pulls that repo and an absolute\n  Mac symlink arrives unusable.\n- Hooks and sync scripts exist in two copies (`~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/`; `.sh`\n  and `.ps1`). Any change patches both.\n- Global `MEMORY.md` is at 2,489 of 2,500 chars. Consolidate before adding to it.\n- Never point Pi at `~/DEV` - it ships no sandbox and no approval prompts, by design.\n- Never let any harness near `DexaProject` (identifiable athlete health data, on Google\n  Drive, not in `~/DEV`).\n- Plugin skills (`superpowers`, `mattpocock-skills`) are vendored and out of scope.\n- **Windows:** four vendored skills (`claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`,\n  `codex-review`) are committed to `claude-skills` as symlinks. On Windows they arrive\n  pointing at a path that does not exist. AMEND-01 in Task 4 untracks them.\n- On the Mac: `timeout` is not installed, `dcg` blocks `find ... -delete`, and Python is\n  PEP 668-managed (stdlib `python3` or `uv`, never global `pip install`).\n- No success claim without pasted command output.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"92a78c18-3b89-48de-bce7-cd8c7701a10b","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
