{"parentUuid":"e8e0e332-d540-48a2-8c3e-a518b6d0fcaa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cezx2PRgXsRg67K2zVvJE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MhgYSeUvmP6ckwQhkE5RnH","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_dcg-guard-blocks.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_read_input_tokens":175349,"output_tokens":95,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":95,"cache_read_input_tokens":175349,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cezx2N744SHtDQoM4Skkt","attributionSkill":"memory-write","type":"assistant","uuid":"d1ee6540-ef35-4506-95a0-9acd90b83de3","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:16:25.121Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d1ee6540-ef35-4506-95a0-9acd90b83de3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88b6ccb8-7105-4de5-afa1-ccbae8a94e54","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MhgYSeUvmP6ckwQhkE5RnH","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>This memory is 5 days old. Memories are point-in-time observations, not live state — claims about code behavior or file:line citations may be outdated. Verify against current code before asserting as fact.</system-reminder>\n1\t---\n2\tname: dcg-guard-blocks\n3\tdescription: \"The dcg command guard blocks whole compound commands — which shapes trip it, and the rewrite that gets the work done\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 80892ff4-3719-4a85-aa22-4eaf3500081d\n8\t  modified: 2026-09-08T02:19:00.806Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tThe `dcg` guard sits in front of Bash and rejects a command **before any of it runs**.\n12\tIt blocks the *whole* invocation, not the offending line — so a `set -e` script with\n13\tfour good steps and one blocked step accomplishes nothing, silently.\n14\t\n15\t**Shapes confirmed to block (2026-09-07):**\n16\t\n17\t- `mv` where either side mentions `~`, `$HOME`, `/etc`, `/usr`, `/var`, `/home`.\n18\t  Rule `core.filesystem:mv-sensitive-source-root-home`. It is guarding the\n19\t  \"relocate then delete\" bypass (`mv /etc /tmp/x && rm -rf /tmp/x`), so it fires\n20\t  on shape alone — an ordinary `mv ~/foo ~/DEV/foo` is caught.\n21\t  **Fix: write both paths absolute** — `mv /Users/kristinarash/foo /Users/kristinarash/DEV/foo`\n22\t  passes. Verified on four real moves.\n23\t- `git branch -d` / `-D` / `-M` / `-C`. Rule `core.git:branch-force-delete`.\n24\t  No rewrite gets past this one — deleting a merged branch needs the user to run it.\n25\t  **Do not bundle it with a push**: a `git push … ; git branch -d …` one-liner is\n26\t  rejected as a unit and the push never happens.\n27\t\n28\t**The habit that follows:** when a multi-step shell job touches home paths or refs,\n29\trun the steps as separate calls, or at minimum keep any guard-prone step out of the\n30\tsame invocation as work you need to land. Then verify — a blocked command produces\n31\tan error, but a *partially* useful compound produces nothing at all.\n32\t\n33\t`dcg explain \"<command>\"` prints the rule and suggested alternatives.\n34\t\n35\tRelated: [[zsh-shell-traps]], [[keystoneos-verification-habits]]\n36\t"}]},"uuid":"c4fb0bd7-f6a3-4ef3-889b-2cf67d755549","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:16:25.330Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_dcg-guard-blocks.md","content":"---\nname: dcg-guard-blocks\ndescription: \"The dcg command guard blocks whole compound commands — which shapes trip it, and the rewrite that gets the work done\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 80892ff4-3719-4a85-aa22-4eaf3500081d\n  modified: 2026-09-08T02:19:00.806Z\n---\n\nThe `dcg` guard sits in front of Bash and rejects a command **before any of it runs**.\nIt blocks the *whole* invocation, not the offending line — so a `set -e` script with\nfour good steps and one blocked step accomplishes nothing, silently.\n\n**Shapes confirmed to block (2026-09-07):**\n\n- `mv` where either side mentions `~`, `$HOME`, `/etc`, `/usr`, `/var`, `/home`.\n  Rule `core.filesystem:mv-sensitive-source-root-home`. It is guarding the\n  \"relocate then delete\" bypass (`mv /etc /tmp/x && rm -rf /tmp/x`), so it fires\n  on shape alone — an ordinary `mv ~/foo ~/DEV/foo` is caught.\n  **Fix: write both paths absolute** — `mv /Users/kristinarash/foo /Users/kristinarash/DEV/foo`\n  passes. Verified on four real moves.\n- `git branch -d` / `-D` / `-M` / `-C`. Rule `core.git:branch-force-delete`.\n  No rewrite gets past this one — deleting a merged branch needs the user to run it.\n  **Do not bundle it with a push**: a `git push … ; git branch -d …` one-liner is\n  rejected as a unit and the push never happens.\n\n**The habit that follows:** when a multi-step shell job touches home paths or refs,\nrun the steps as separate calls, or at minimum keep any guard-prone step out of the\nsame invocation as work you need to land. Then verify — a blocked command produces\nan error, but a *partially* useful compound produces nothing at all.\n\n`dcg explain \"<command>\"` prints the rule and suggested alternatives.\n\nRelated: [[zsh-shell-traps]], [[keystoneos-verification-habits]]\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d1ee6540-ef35-4506-95a0-9acd90b83de3","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
