{"parentUuid":"1ab93f84-f778-4957-a1e9-734b142136e5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88b6ccb8-7105-4de5-afa1-ccbae8a94e54","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LmSu1as5Y3Vu5sfyTjPFdA","type":"tool_result","content":"c03-probe.py\ngateC-dispositions.md\nir01-redgreen.py\nt5f-checker-test.py\nt7-failpaths.py","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"06c93e61-c28e-4c7e-8e22-5da89e34d451","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:18:27.529Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"c03-probe.py\ngateC-dispositions.md\nir01-redgreen.py\nt5f-checker-test.py\nt7-failpaths.py","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/c03-probe.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":26,"lines":["+\"\"\"Gate C C-03 probe: an unreadable Claude transcript must be counted.\"\"\"","+import os, subprocess","+","+MET = \"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/aios-metrics.py\"","+PROBE = \"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/zz-c03-probe.jsonl\"","+","+def metrics():","+    out = subprocess.run([\"python3\", MET], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout","+    return dict(l.split(\"=\", 1) for l in out.splitlines() if \"=\" in l)","+","+base = metrics()","+print(\"baseline:\", {k: base.get(k) for k in (\"usage_scope\", \"usage_unreadable_transcripts\", \"never_used\", \"portability_failures\")})","+","+open(PROBE, \"w\").write(\"{}\\n\")","+os.chmod(PROBE, 0)","+try:","+    probed = metrics()","+finally:","+    os.chmod(PROBE, 0o600)","+    os.remove(PROBE)","+","+before = int(base[\"usage_unreadable_transcripts\"])","+after = int(probed[\"usage_unreadable_transcripts\"])","+ok = base[\"usage_scope\"] == \"claude_code_transcripts_only\" and after == before + 1 and not os.path.exists(PROBE)","+print(f\"unreadable {before} -> {after}; probe removed={not os.path.exists(PROBE)}\")","+print(\"C-03 PROBE PASS\" if ok else \"C-03 PROBE FAIL\")"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/gateC-dispositions.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":30,"lines":["+# Gate C dispositions (host-authored, 2026-09-13)","+","+Codex Gate C verdict on KeystoneOS (base `767b3de`): REVISE, three medium findings.","+All accepted and fixed. Host-verified below; this inspection is the independent check.","+","+| ID | Sev | Disposition | What changed |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| C-01 | medium | ACCEPTED | Commit `77d9ecc`: `scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh`, `scripts/aios-metrics.py`, `scripts/skill-portability-check.py` recorded as mode 100755 via `git update-index --chmod=+x` (repo has `core.fileMode=false`). `git ls-files -s` shows 100755 for all three. |","+| C-02 | medium | ACCEPTED | Commit `dae7aeb`: stale-lock reclaim serialised by a second atomic lock `$LOCK.recover` (mkdir; stale when older than 10 min). Only a holder of `.recover` deletes `$LOCK`. While holding it the run re-tries `mkdir $LOCK`, re-reads the owner, aborts on a live owner or a young ownerless lock, and releases `.recover` on every path. EXIT trap removes `$LOCK` only if `$LOCK/pid` equals `$$`. Log strings `ABORT live run` / `RECLAIM stale lock` unchanged. A test-only `AIOS_LOCK_TEST_PAUSE` sleep sits just before the reclaim, unset under launchd. Accepted residual risk (commented in the script): a crash inside the millisecond recovery section, followed more than 10 minutes later by two runs starting together. |","+| C-03 | medium | ACCEPTED | Commit `dae7aeb`: `usage()` counts transcripts that raise on read instead of swallowing them. New keys `usage_scope=claude_code_transcripts_only` and `usage_unreadable_transcripts=N`; no existing key renamed (the cron wrapper's keys are untouched). `aios-audit` SKILL.md §6: Bloat now says \"never invoked in Claude Code transcripts\", notes the scope and unreadable count; Crutch test forbids DELETE on `never_used` alone and gives `grep -rl \"<skill>/SKILL.md\" ~/.codex/sessions \\| wc -l`, with a warning that bulk scans also match. |","+","+## Executed verification","+","+- `bash -n` on the wrapper; `py_compile` on metrics and the test script: OK.","+- C-03 probe (`~/.claude/jobs/9823c1f0/tmp/c03-probe.py`): baseline `usage_scope=claude_code_transcripts_only`, `usage_unreadable_transcripts=0`; with one mode-000 `.jsonl` placed under `~/.claude/projects/` the count became 1; probe file removed. PASS.","+- Failure paths (`~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t7-failpaths.py`), all against the real wrapper and real metrics:","+  - missing metrics script: exit 1, no row, `FAIL metrics script errored` — PASS","+  - live lock: exit 0, no row, `ABORT live run` — PASS","+  - stale lock reclaimed: exit 0, one row, `RECLAIM stale lock` — PASS","+  - lock and `.recover` released afterwards — PASS","+  - two concurrent runs on one stale lock, first held 3 s inside the recovery section: exit 0,0; exactly one row; one RECLAIM; no leftover lock or `.recover` — PASS","+  - same, no pause (started together): exit 0,0; one row; one RECLAIM; no leftovers — PASS","+  - `.recover` aged 11 min: reclaimed, run proceeds, one row, nothing left — PASS","+  - fresh `.recover`: exit 0, no row, `ABORT another run is recovering` — PASS","+  - metrics script restored and executable — PASS","+- Test side effects undone: `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` and `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log` restored byte-for-byte from pre-test copies. `git status` clean apart from the three committed source files.","+","+## Still open, not a Gate C defect","+","+- `portability_failures=7`: the 7-skill roster decision carried from Gate B (S2-02 / K2-02). Eric's call."]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/ir01-redgreen.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":20,"lines":["+\"\"\"Red-green for IR-01: the pre-fix checker must PASS the wrong-type fixtures","+(the bug), the current checker must FLAG them.\"\"\"","+import subprocess, types","+","+K = \"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS\"","+FX = \"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t5f-fx/.claude/skills\"","+CASES = [\"desc-flow-seq\", \"desc-block-seq\", \"desc-block-seq0\", \"desc-block-map\", \"desc-plain-multi\"]","+","+def load(src, label):","+    m = types.ModuleType(label)","+    exec(compile(src, label, \"exec\"), m.__dict__)","+    return m","+","+old_src = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", K, \"show\", \"2bcdda2~1:scripts/skill-portability-check.py\"],","+                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout","+new_src = open(f\"{K}/scripts/skill-portability-check.py\").read()","+old, new = load(old_src, \"old\"), load(new_src, \"new\")","+for c in CASES:","+    p = f\"{FX}/{c}/SKILL.md\"","+    print(f\"{c:18} old_flagged={bool(old.check(p)[1])!s:5} new_flagged={bool(new.check(p)[1])!s:5}\")"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/t5f-checker-test.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":140,"lines":["+\"\"\"Gate C r2 IR-01 checker tests: name/description must be strings, not lists or maps.","+Re-runs every t5e fixture expectation in fresh folders (old fixture dirs cannot be deleted).","+Run with: uv run --no-project --with pyyaml python t5f-checker-test.py\"\"\"","+import os, subprocess, glob, importlib.util, yaml, stat","+","+T = \"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp\"","+CHK = \"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/scripts/skill-portability-check.py\"","+GOOD_DESC = \"Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\"","+","+def run(home=None):","+    env = dict(os.environ)","+    if home:","+        env[\"HOME\"] = home","+    return subprocess.run([\"python3\", CHK], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env)","+","+def skill(root, name, fm_lines):","+    os.makedirs(f\"{root}/.claude/skills/{name}\")","+    open(f\"{root}/.claude/skills/{name}/SKILL.md\", \"w\").write(\"---\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(fm_lines) + \"\\n---\\nbody\\n\")","+","+spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"chk\", CHK)","+chk = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)","+spec.loader.exec_module(chk)","+","+# name -> (frontmatter lines, expect_flagged, loader_should_accept)","+FX = {","+    # --- carried from t5e (K2-01) ---","+    \"dq-bad-escape\":    ([\"name: dq-bad-escape\", 'description: \"Use when testing. Do not use otherwise. \\\\q\"'], True, False),","+    \"dq-good-escapes\":  ([\"name: dq-good-escapes\", 'description: \"Use when \\\\\"x\\\\\" \\\\x41 \\\\u00e9. Do not use otherwise.\"'], False, True),","+    \"dq-unclosed\":      ([\"name: dq-unclosed\", 'description: \"Use when testing.', '  Do not use otherwise.\"'], True, None),","+    \"dq-trailing-text\": ([\"name: dq-trailing-text\", 'description: \"Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\" extra'], True, False),","+    \"sq-good-doubled\":  ([\"name: sq-good-doubled\", \"description: 'Use when it''s testing. Do not use otherwise.'\"], False, True),","+    \"sq-unclosed\":      ([\"name: sq-unclosed\", \"description: 'Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\"], True, False),","+    \"flow-map\":         ([\"name: flow-map\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\", \"metadata: {a: b}\"], True, None),","+    \"flow-seq-good\":    ([\"name: flow-seq-good\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\", \"metadata:\", \"  bins: [one, two-cli]\"], False, True),","+    \"flow-seq-nested\":  ([\"name: flow-seq-nested\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\", \"metadata:\", \"  bins: [[one], two]\"], True, None),","+    \"tag\":              ([\"name: tag\", f\"description: !!str {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, None),","+    \"anchor\":           ([\"name: anchor\", f\"description: &d {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, None),","+    \"tab-indent\":       ([\"name: tab-indent\", \"description: >-\", f\"\\t{GOOD_DESC}\"], True, False),","+    \"nested-colon\":     ([\"name: nested-colon\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\", \"metadata:\", \"  short-description: bad: value\"], True, False),","+    \"block-good\":       ([\"name: block-good\", \"description: >-\", \"  Use when testing: a # b. Do not use otherwise.\"], False, True),","+    \"list-items-good\":  ([\"name: list-items-good\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\", \"metadata:\", \"  install:\", \"    - kind: go\", \"      module: github.com/x/y\"], False, True),","+    \"top-junk\":         ([\"name: top-junk\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\", \"just words\"], True, False),","+    # --- new for IR-01: wrong node type for name/description ---","+    \"desc-flow-seq\":    ([\"name: desc-flow-seq\", f\"description: [{GOOD_DESC}]\"], True, True),","+    \"desc-block-seq\":   ([\"name: desc-block-seq\", \"description:\", f\"  - {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),","+    \"desc-block-seq0\":  ([\"name: desc-block-seq0\", \"description:\", f\"- {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),","+    \"desc-block-map\":   ([\"name: desc-block-map\", \"description:\", f\"  when: {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),","+    \"desc-flow-map\":    ([\"name: desc-flow-map\", \"description: {when: yes}\"], True, True),","+    \"name-flow-seq\":    ([\"name: [name-flow-seq]\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),","+    # --- controls: strings in every supported shape must still pass ---","+    \"desc-plain-multi\": ([\"name: desc-plain-multi\", \"description:\", \"  Use when testing.\", \"  Do not use otherwise.\"], False, True),","+    \"desc-folded-then-key\": ([\"name: desc-folded-then-key\", \"description: >-\", f\"  {GOOD_DESC}\", \"metadata:\", \"  a: b\"], False, True),","+}","+","+H = f\"{T}/t5f-fx\"","+for n, (lines, _, _) in FX.items():","+    skill(H, n, lines)","+r = run(H)","+print(\"FIXTURES exit\", r.returncode, \"|\", r.stdout.strip().splitlines()[-1])","+failing, reasons, cur = set(), {}, None","+for l in r.stdout.splitlines():","+    if l.startswith(\"FAIL \"):","+        cur = l[5:]; failing.add(cur); reasons[cur] = []","+    elif cur and l.strip().startswith(\"- \"):","+        reasons[cur].append(l.strip()[2:])","+bad = []","+for n, (lines, expect_flag, loader_ok) in FX.items():","+    flagged = n in failing","+    try:","+        doc = yaml.safe_load(\"\\n\".join(lines))","+        loads = True","+    except yaml.YAMLError:","+        doc, loads = None, False","+    note = \"\"","+    if loader_ok is not None and loads != loader_ok:","+        note = f\" (loader assumption wrong: loads={loads})\"","+    # Type agreement: whenever the loader succeeds, value_kind must match its type.","+    if loads and isinstance(doc, dict):","+        fm = \"\\n\".join(lines)","+        for k in (\"name\", \"description\"):","+            v = doc.get(k)","+            want = \"sequence\" if isinstance(v, list) else \"mapping\" if isinstance(v, dict) else \"scalar\"","+            got = chk.value_kind(fm, k)","+            if got != want:","+                note += f\" (value_kind {k}={got}, loader says {want})\"","+    status = \"PASS\" if flagged == expect_flag and not note else \"FAIL\"","+    if status == \"FAIL\":","+        bad.append(n)","+    first = (reasons.get(n) or [\"\"])[0][:70]","+    print(f\"  {status} {n}: flagged={flagged} expect={expect_flag} loads={loads}{note} | {first}\")","+","+# Real roster: syntax check AND value kinds must agree with a YAML loader.","+dis, kind_dis = [], []","+real = [p for p in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.expanduser(\"~/.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md\")))","+        if not os.path.islink(os.path.dirname(p))]","+for p in real:","+    fm = chk.frontmatter(open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\").read())","+    flagged = bool(chk.syntax_problems(fm))","+    try:","+        doc = yaml.safe_load(fm); loads = True","+    except yaml.YAMLError:","+        doc, loads = None, False","+    if flagged == loads:","+        dis.append((p.split(\"/\")[-2], chk.syntax_problems(fm)[:1], loads))","+    if loads:","+        for k in (\"name\", \"description\"):","+            v = doc.get(k)","+            want = \"sequence\" if isinstance(v, list) else \"mapping\" if isinstance(v, dict) else \"scalar\"","+            if chk.value_kind(fm, k) != want:","+                kind_dis.append((p.split(\"/\")[-2], k, chk.value_kind(fm, k), want))","+print(\"REAL roster files:\", len(real), \"syntax disagreements:\", dis, \"kind disagreements:\", kind_dis)","+r = run()","+print(\"REAL checker exit\", r.returncode, \"|\", r.stdout.strip().splitlines()[-1])","+print(\"REAL failing:\", sorted(l[5:] for l in r.stdout.splitlines() if l.startswith(\"FAIL \")))","+","+# K2-03 fail-closed, fresh homes.","+def evidence_home(tag):","+    h = f\"{T}/t5f-ev-{tag}\"","+    skill(h, \"ok\", [\"name: ok\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"])","+    return h","+h = evidence_home(\"badjson\")","+open(f\"{h}/.claude/settings.json\", \"w\").write(\"{not json\")","+r = run(h); print(\"malformed settings.json -> exit\", r.returncode, \"(expect 2)\")","+h = evidence_home(\"nonobject\")","+open(f\"{h}/.claude/settings.json\", \"w\").write('{\"skillOverrides\": [\"x\"]}')","+r = run(h); print(\"skillOverrides not an object -> exit\", r.returncode, \"(expect 2)\")","+h = evidence_home(\"unreadable\")","+open(f\"{h}/.claude/settings.json\", \"w\").write(\"{}\")","+os.chmod(f\"{h}/.claude/settings.json\", 0)","+r = run(h); print(\"unreadable settings.json -> exit\", r.returncode, \"(expect 2)\")","+os.chmod(f\"{h}/.claude/settings.json\", stat.S_IRUSR | stat.S_IWUSR)","+h = evidence_home(\"brokengit\")","+open(f\"{h}/.claude/skills/.git\", \"w\").write(\"gitdir: /nonexistent/repo\\n\")","+r = run(h); print(\"git probe fails -> exit\", r.returncode, \"(expect 2)\")","+h = evidence_home(\"nosettings\")","+r = run(h); print(\"no settings, no git (control) -> exit\", r.returncode, \"(expect 0)\")","+for hh, exp in ((f\"{T}/t5-badcanon\", 1), (f\"{T}/t5-emptycanon\", 2), (f\"{T}/t5b-fx-yaml\", 1), (f\"{T}/t5b-fx-spell\", 1)):","+    r = run(hh)","+    print(os.path.basename(hh), \"exit\", r.returncode, \"(expect\", exp, \")\")","+print(\"FIXTURE FAILURES:\", bad or \"none\")"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/t7-failpaths.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":124,"lines":["+\"\"\"Task 7 Step 3: prove the cron wrapper's failure paths (plan R9 / R2-06).","+Same three probes as the plan's shell block, done with os calls because dcg","+blocks `mv`/`rm -rf` on variable paths.\"\"\"","+import os, subprocess, time","+","+K = \"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS\"","+CRON = f\"{K}/scripts/aios-audit-cron.sh\"","+MET = f\"{K}/scripts/aios-metrics.py\"","+BAK = \"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t7-aios-metrics.bak\"","+TREND = f\"{K}/docs/audits/aios-trend.md\"","+LOG = \"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/scripts/logs/aios-audit.log\"","+LOCK = \"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/scripts/.aios-audit.lock\"","+","+def rows():","+    return sum(1 for l in open(TREND) if l.startswith(\"| 20\"))","+","+def log_tail_from(offset):","+    with open(LOG) as f:","+        f.seek(offset)","+        return f.read()","+","+RECOVER = LOCK + \".recover\"","+","+def clear_dir(p):","+    if os.path.isdir(p):","+        for n in os.listdir(p):","+            os.remove(os.path.join(p, n))","+        os.rmdir(p)","+","+def clear_lock():","+    clear_dir(LOCK)","+    clear_dir(RECOVER)","+","+def run():","+    return subprocess.run([CRON], capture_output=True, text=True).returncode","+","+def stale_lock():","+    clear_lock()","+    os.mkdir(LOCK)","+    open(f\"{LOCK}/pid\", \"w\").write(\"999999\")               # a pid that cannot exist","+","+ok_all = True","+def report(label, good, detail):","+    global ok_all","+    ok_all &= good","+    print(f\"{'PASS' if good else 'FAIL'} {label}: {detail}\")","+","+# 1. Missing metrics script must fail the job and add no row.","+r0, off = rows(), os.path.getsize(LOG)","+os.rename(MET, BAK)","+try:","+    rc = run()","+finally:","+    os.rename(BAK, MET)","+t = log_tail_from(off)","+report(\"missing metrics script\", rc == 1 and \"FAIL metrics script errored\" in t and rows() == r0,","+       f\"exit={rc} rows {r0}->{rows()} log_has_FAIL={'FAIL metrics script errored' in t}\")","+","+# 2. A LIVE lock must make the job stand down, no row.","+clear_lock()","+os.mkdir(LOCK)","+open(f\"{LOCK}/pid\", \"w\").write(str(os.getpid()))          # this process is alive","+r0, off = rows(), os.path.getsize(LOG)","+rc = run()","+t = log_tail_from(off)","+report(\"live lock\", rc == 0 and \"ABORT live run\" in t and rows() == r0,","+       f\"exit={rc} rows {r0}->{rows()} log_has_ABORT={'ABORT live run' in t}\")","+","+# 3. A STALE lock must be RECLAIMED and one row added.","+clear_lock()","+os.mkdir(LOCK)","+open(f\"{LOCK}/pid\", \"w\").write(\"999999\")                   # a pid that cannot exist","+r0, off = rows(), os.path.getsize(LOG)","+rc = run()","+t = log_tail_from(off)","+report(\"stale lock reclaimed\", rc == 0 and \"RECLAIM stale lock\" in t and rows() == r0 + 1,","+       f\"exit={rc} rows {r0}->{rows()} log_has_RECLAIM={'RECLAIM stale lock' in t}\")","+report(\"lock released afterwards\", not os.path.exists(LOCK) and not os.path.exists(RECOVER),","+       f\"lock exists={os.path.exists(LOCK)} recover exists={os.path.exists(RECOVER)}\")","+","+# 4. Gate C C-02: TWO runs on the same stale lock -> exactly one row.","+# AIOS_LOCK_TEST_PAUSE holds the first reclaimer inside the recovery section,","+# so the second run is forced into the interleaving Codex described.","+for trial, pause in ((\"paused\", \"3\"), (\"unpaused\", \"\")):","+    stale_lock()","+    r0, off = rows(), os.path.getsize(LOG)","+    env = dict(os.environ, AIOS_LOCK_TEST_PAUSE=pause)","+    a = subprocess.Popen([CRON], env=env)","+    time.sleep(0.3 if pause else 0)","+    b = subprocess.Popen([CRON], env=env)","+    rca, rcb = a.wait(), b.wait()","+    t = log_tail_from(off)","+    n_reclaim = t.count(\"RECLAIM stale lock (owner\")","+    leftovers = os.path.exists(LOCK) or os.path.exists(RECOVER)","+    report(f\"concurrent stale lock ({trial})\",","+           rca == 0 and rcb == 0 and rows() == r0 + 1 and n_reclaim == 1 and not leftovers,","+           f\"exit={rca},{rcb} rows {r0}->{rows()} reclaims={n_reclaim} leftovers={leftovers}\")","+","+# 5. A recovery lock older than 10 min is reclaimed; the run proceeds.","+stale_lock()","+os.mkdir(RECOVER)","+old = time.time() - 11 * 60","+os.utime(RECOVER, (old, old))","+r0, off = rows(), os.path.getsize(LOG)","+rc = run()","+t = log_tail_from(off)","+report(\"stale recovery lock reclaimed\",","+       rc == 0 and \"RECLAIM stale recovery lock\" in t and rows() == r0 + 1","+       and not os.path.exists(LOCK) and not os.path.exists(RECOVER),","+       f\"exit={rc} rows {r0}->{rows()} log_has_RECLAIM_recovery={'RECLAIM stale recovery lock' in t}\")","+","+# 6. A FRESH recovery lock means another run is recovering: stand down, no row.","+stale_lock()","+os.mkdir(RECOVER)","+r0, off = rows(), os.path.getsize(LOG)","+rc = run()","+t = log_tail_from(off)","+report(\"fresh recovery lock respected\",","+       rc == 0 and \"ABORT another run is recovering\" in t and rows() == r0","+       and os.path.isdir(RECOVER),","+       f\"exit={rc} rows {r0}->{rows()} log_has_ABORT={'ABORT another run is recovering' in t}\")","+clear_lock()","+report(\"metrics script restored\", os.path.isfile(MET) and os.access(MET, os.X_OK), MET)","+print(\"ALL FAILURE PATHS PASS\" if ok_all else \"SOME FAILURE PATHS FAILED\")"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/c03-probe.py","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/gateC-dispositions.md","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/ir01-redgreen.py","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/t5f-checker-test.py","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/t7-failpaths.py"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1ab93f84-f778-4957-a1e9-734b142136e5","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
