{"parentUuid":"7d4d2c3e-e349-4227-ba36-101c1d53bdee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezxD6L6LaRW9EdoDbWuj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I finished the handoff as far as a background session can go. Everything is committed and pushed to KeystoneOS, and `main` matches GitHub.\n\n**What I fixed**\n- **C-01:** The 3 AIOS scripts are now marked executable in git, so a fresh copy of the repo can run them.\n- **C-02:** Two monthly runs can no longer both clear an old leftover lock. I tested two runs starting at the same time: exactly one trend row was written, and nothing was left behind. All 9 lock tests pass.\n- **C-03:** The \"never used\" count now says it covers Claude Code only. The audit skill no longer suggests deleting a skill based on that count alone. It must check Codex sessions first.\n- **IR-01:** Codex found this in its second review. The checker accepted a skill description written as a YAML list. It now rejects lists. The old checker missed all 4 bad test cases, and the new one catches all 4.\n\n**What else I did**\n- I logged Tasks 6–7 and both Gate C rounds in `docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md`.\n- I updated `docs/STATUS.md`.\n- I saved the test scripts in `docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/`, so the proof stays after this job is deleted.\n- I saved 2 traps to memory. One is a new `dcg` block on `>` redirects. The other: `claude -p --disallowedTools Bash` still runs shell commands through the context-mode tools.\n\n**Codex round 2:** both repos came back REVISE. The only new code defect was IR-01, now fixed but not re-checked by Codex. Every other REVISE line is the same roster item. That item is a choice, not a bug.\n\n**Gate D:** done for this session's work. Every claim above has command output behind it. The plan itself is not finished, because two items wait on you.\n\n**You decide: the roster.** 7 skills are switched off in Claude Code but still live in Codex and Pi: ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review, pp-espn, session-miner.\n- **Option A:** Retire them from canonical. You can undo it. It keeps your 9/12 skill cuts, and the checker drops to 0 failures.\n- **Option B:** Switch them back on in Claude Code. This adds their token cost back.\n- **My pick:** A, unless you use one of them in Codex.\n\n**You decide: Task 8 (Pi trial).** It is blocked because creating the `piuser` account needs `sudo`.\n- **Option A:** Run the 8 `sudo` lines in `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pi-trial.md` in your terminal.\n- **Option B:** Accept it as blocked.\n- **My pick:** B, unless the Pi trial still matters to you.\n\n**You run:** type `audit my AI OS` in a live session in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`. The test I ran earlier was headless and wrote no report, so the full audit flow is still unproven.\n\nresult: All Gate C fixes (C-01, C-02, C-03, IR-01) are committed, tested and pushed; the roster choice and the Pi trial are waiting on you."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_read_input_tokens":184917,"output_tokens":1090,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":41},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":404,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1090,"cache_read_input_tokens":184917,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":404},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CezxD4tWp4VhyEnKmM5AQ","attributionSkill":"memory-write","type":"assistant","uuid":"0dc13224-eddc-4ab7-8216-494c7f10695e","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:19:03.001Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high",