{"parentUuid":"91f6e9b2-bd7d-4a66-8ca2-368df615499a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- ArXiv: Search and retrieve arXiv academic papers by topic, category, or paper ID — with AlphaXiv-enriched AI-generated overviews. Uses arXiv Atom API across cs.AI/cs.LG/cs.CL/cs.CR/cs.MA/cs.SE/cs.IR. Three workflows: Latest, Search, Paper. USE WHEN arxiv, papers, latest papers, research papers, recent ML papers, paper lookup, summarize paper, latest LLM papers, AI safety papers, cs.AI latest. NOT FOR general research (Research), URL parsing (_PARSER), or annual reports (_ANNUALREPORTS).\n- capture-insight: Capture a story, win, or lesson the user just shared as a permanent atomic note in the SecondBrain vault. Use when the user tells a story or lesson and says \"capture this\", \"save this win/lesson\", \"that's worth a note\", or \"/capture-insight\". Do not use for end-of-day structured capture (use interview-me), whole-project distillation (use harvest), or plain facts (use memory-write).\n- ISA: Owns the Ideal State Artifact — universal primitive holding articulated ideal state of any project, task, application, library, or work session as a hard-to-vary explanation. Six workflows: Scaffold (fresh ISA at effort tier), Interview (adaptive Q&A), CheckCompleteness (score against tier gate), Reconcile (merge ephemeral feature-file excerpt back to master, keyed on stable ISC IDs), Seed (bootstrap from repo README/code/commits), Append (record Decisions/Changelog/Verification entries). Locked twelve-section order: Problem, Vision, Out of Scope, Principles, Constraints, Goal, Criteria, Test Strategy, Features, Decisions, Changelog, Verification. Auto-invoked by Algorithm at OBSERVE. USE WHEN ISA, ISC, ideal state, ideal state criteria, project specification, hill-climb, articulating done. NOT FOR creating new skills (use CreateSkill).\n- library-review: Review a book-library domain for gaps, contested entries, and missing coverage, and propose new entries. Manual loop — proposes, you approve. Use when the user says \"review my library\", \"/library-review <domain>\", \"what's missing from my <domain> advisor\", or after a batch of ingestion. Do not use to ask the library a question (use library-advisor) or to add a new book (use ingest-book).\n- pp-espn: ESPN sports CLI — live scores, standings, team stats, schedules, polls, rankings, and game summaries (box score, leaders, scoring plays, odds, win probability) across NFL / NBA / MLB / NHL / NCAA / MLS / EPL / WNBA. Use for 'what's the score of the Lakers game', 'Patriots schedule this week', 'NFL standings', 'box score', head-to-head comparisons, 'who's on top of the AP poll'. No API key required. Do not use to freeze the CFB model's weekly forecasts (use forecast-capture) or to fix game film JSON timestamps (use game-film-timestamps).\n- Science: The scientific method as a universal problem-solving algorithm — goal-first, hypothesis-plural, falsifiable experiments, honest measurement. Seven workflows: DefineGoal, GenerateHypotheses (min 3 — single-hypothesis is confirmation bias), DesignExperiment, MeasureResults, AnalyzeResults, Iterate, FullCycle. Diagnostic shortcuts: QuickDiagnosis (15-min rule), StructuredInvestigation (multi-factor). Scales across micro (TDD), meso (feature validation), macro (MVP launch). Integrates Council, Evals, Development, RedTeam. USE WHEN think about, figure out, experiment, iterate, optimize, hypothesis, science, full cycle, quick diagnosis, structured investigation, how do we test, analyze results. NOT FOR multi-angle lens passes (use IterativeDepth).\n- session-miner: Mine recent Claude Code sessions for learnings that never got captured — repeated corrections, decisions with rationale, gotchas, and workflows worth turning into skills — and route each to memory, the vault, or a skill edit. Use when the user says \"/session-miner\", \"what did we miss\", \"review recent sessions\", \"mine my history\", or \"anything from this week worth keeping?\". Do not use to audit vault notes (use improve-system) or to capture one story the user just told (use capture-insight).","skillCount":7,"isInitial":false,"names":["ArXiv","capture-insight","ISA","library-review","pp-espn","Science","session-miner"]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"83b27858-522e-4b39-b395-918a730dbbd4","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:26:37.617Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are available for use with the Skill tool:\n\n- ArXiv: Search and retrieve arXiv academic papers by topic, category, or paper ID — with AlphaXiv-enriched AI-generated overviews. Uses arXiv Atom API across cs.AI/cs.LG/cs.CL/cs.CR/cs.MA/cs.SE/cs.IR. Three workflows: Latest, Search, Paper. USE WHEN arxiv, papers, latest papers, research papers, recent ML papers, paper lookup, summarize paper, latest LLM papers, AI safety papers, cs.AI latest. NOT FOR general research (Research), URL parsing (_PARSER), or annual reports (_ANNUALREPORTS).\n- capture-insight: Capture a story, win, or lesson the user just shared as a permanent atomic note in the SecondBrain vault. Use when the user tells a story or lesson and says \"capture this\", \"save this win/lesson\", \"that's worth a note\", or \"/capture-insight\". Do not use for end-of-day structured capture (use interview-me), whole-project distillation (use harvest), or plain facts (use memory-write).\n- ISA: Owns the Ideal State Artifact — universal primitive holding articulated ideal state of any project, task, application, library, or work session as a hard-to-vary explanation. Six workflows: Scaffold (fresh ISA at effort tier), Interview (adaptive Q&A), CheckCompleteness (score against tier gate), Reconcile (merge ephemeral feature-file excerpt back to master, keyed on stable ISC IDs), Seed (bootstrap from repo README/code/commits), Append (record Decisions/Changelog/Verification entries). Locked twelve-section order: Problem, Vision, Out of Scope, Principles, Constraints, Goal, Criteria, Test Strategy, Features, Decisions, Changelog, Verification. Auto-invoked by Algorithm at OBSERVE. USE WHEN ISA, ISC, ideal state, ideal state criteria, project specification, hill-climb, articulating done. NOT FOR creating new skills (use CreateSkill).\n- library-review: Review a book-library domain for gaps, contested entries, and missing coverage, and propose new entries. Manual loop — proposes, you approve. Use when the user says \"review my library\", \"/library-review <domain>\", \"what's missing from my <domain> advisor\", or after a batch of ingestion. Do not use to ask the library a question (use library-advisor) or to add a new book (use ingest-book).\n- pp-espn: ESPN sports CLI — live scores, standings, team stats, schedules, polls, rankings, and game summaries (box score, leaders, scoring plays, odds, win probability) across NFL / NBA / MLB / NHL / NCAA / MLS / EPL / WNBA. Use for 'what's the score of the Lakers game', 'Patriots schedule this week', 'NFL standings', 'box score', head-to-head comparisons, 'who's on top of the AP poll'. No API key required. Do not use to freeze the CFB model's weekly forecasts (use forecast-capture) or to fix game film JSON timestamps (use game-film-timestamps).\n- Science: The scientific method as a universal problem-solving algorithm — goal-first, hypothesis-plural, falsifiable experiments, honest measurement. Seven workflows: DefineGoal, GenerateHypotheses (min 3 — single-hypothesis is confirmation bias), DesignExperiment, MeasureResults, AnalyzeResults, Iterate, FullCycle. Diagnostic shortcuts: QuickDiagnosis (15-min rule), StructuredInvestigation (multi-factor). Scales across micro (TDD), meso (feature validation), macro (MVP launch). Integrates Council, Evals, Development, RedTeam. USE WHEN think about, figure out, experiment, iterate, optimize, hypothesis, science, full cycle, quick diagnosis, structured investigation, how do we test, analyze results. NOT FOR multi-angle lens passes (use IterativeDepth).\n- session-miner: Mine recent Claude Code sessions for learnings that never got captured — repeated corrections, decisions with rationale, gotchas, and workflows worth turning into skills — and route each to memory, the vault, or a skill edit. Use when the user says \"/session-miner\", \"what did we miss\", \"review recent sessions\", \"mine my history\", or \"anything from this week worth keeping?\". Do not use to audit vault notes (use improve-system) or to capture one story the user just told (use capture-insight).\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
