{"parentUuid":"a7249e01-747d-48ea-909f-f783a4aea54c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezxpMmzv5kBRpdTJ26vk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AzNZiwLTFHuWuQXLca94Ps","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"os-audit: substrate and data feeds","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","prompt":"You are a READ-ONLY audit delegate for Eric's AI OS audit (2026-09-13, macOS, zsh).\n\nSkill to follow: read `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md` in full and follow it — but ONLY these two checks:\n- **Check 1 (routing integrity)** — layer \"Substrate\": `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `~/.claude/AGENTS.md`, and the `~/DEV/*.md` routers (CLAUDE.md, FOOTBALL.md, PERFORMANCE.md, RESEARCH.md, PLATFORM.md, PROGRAM.md, PERSONAL.md, COMMANDS.md). Does every path/pointer they name exist?\n- **Check 3 (freshness)** — layer \"Data feeds\": Fireflies, GPS, CFBD, Zotero. How stale is each feed's newest data?\n\nHARD RULES\n- Report findings only. Apply nothing. Do not create, edit, move or delete any file: no Write/Edit tools, no shell `>` redirects into files, no git commits, no ledger/report/trend files, no memory writes. If a skill step says to write something, skip it and say so.\n- Never open or read anything under a `DexaProject` path (identifiable health data).\n- No `timeout` command exists. A `dcg` guard may block some shell shapes; if blocked, skip that probe and note it. Do not try to bypass it.\n- Don't paste private file contents; cite paths and short evidence.\n\nRETURN (under ~700 words):\n1. Findings — each with severity RED / AMBER / GREEN, the evidence (path or command output), and a one-line fix suggestion.\n2. \"Checked\" — exactly what you ran or read, per check.\n3. \"Not checked\" — any part of Check 1 or Check 3 scope you did not cover, and why."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2360,"cache_read_input_tokens":563268,"output_tokens":8179,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2188},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":586,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":66,"cache_read_input_tokens":281341,"cache_creation_input_tokens":586,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":586},"type":"message"},{"input_tokens":263188,"output_tokens":8365,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"advisor_message","model":"claude-fable-5-1"},{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8113,"cache_read_input_tokens":281927,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1774,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":5,"requestId":"req_011CezxpLVbV5kYWSuR78X8P","attributionSkill":"update-config","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd6e4f91-d69b-43e3-ab92-523e59235973","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:29:27.527Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"dd6e4f91-d69b-43e3-ab92-523e59235973","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Agent","toolUseID":"toolu_01AzNZiwLTFHuWuQXLca94Ps","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"updatedInput\":{\"description\":\"os-audit: substrate and data feeds\",\"prompt\":\"You are a READ-ONLY audit delegate for Eric's AI OS audit (2026-09-13, macOS, zsh).\\n\\nSkill to follow: read `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/os-audit/SKILL.md` in full and follow it — but ONLY these two checks:\\n- **Check 1 (routing integrity)** — layer \\\"Substrate\\\": `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `~/.claude/AGENTS.md`, and the `~/DEV/*.md` routers (CLAUDE.md, FOOTBALL.md, PERFORMANCE.md, RESEARCH.md, PLATFORM.md, PROGRAM.md, PERSONAL.md, COMMANDS.md). Does every path/pointer they name exist?\\n- **Check 3 (freshness)** — layer \\\"Data feeds\\\": Fireflies, GPS, CFBD, Zotero. How stale is each feed's newest data?\\n\\nHARD RULES\\n- Report findings only. Apply nothing. Do not create, edit, move or delete any file: no Write/Edit tools, no shell `>` redirects into files, no git commits, no ledger/report/trend files, no memory writes. If a skill step says to write something, skip it and say so.\\n- Never open or read anything under a `DexaProject` path (identifiable health data).\\n- No `timeout` command exists. A `dcg` guard may block some shell shapes; if blocked, skip that probe and note it. Do not try to bypass it.\\n- Don't paste private file contents; cite paths and short evidence.\\n\\nRETURN (under ~700 words):\\n1. Findings — each with severity RED / AMBER / GREEN, the evidence (path or command output), and a one-line fix suggestion.\\n2. \\\"Checked\\\" — exactly what you ran or read, per check.\\n3. \\\"Not checked\\\" — any part of Check 1 or Check 3 scope you did not cover, and why.\\n<context_window_protection>\\n  <priority_instructions>\\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\\n  </priority_instructions>\\n\\n  <deferred_tool_bootstrap>\\n    The context-mode tools below may be DEFERRED in your harness — their schemas are not loaded yet, so calling them directly fails (e.g. \\\"tool not found\\\" / InputValidationError). Load them ONCE before your first ctx_* call:\\n    ToolSearch(query: \\\"select:mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute,mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search,mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute,mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file,mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index\\\")\\n    After that they are callable. If any ctx_* call fails as not-found, ToolSearch it and retry — do NOT fall back to Bash/Read just because the schema was not loaded yet.\\n  </deferred_tool_bootstrap>\\n\\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \\\"timeline\\\")\\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\\n       - Each command: {label: \\\"section header\\\", command: \\\"shell command\\\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\\\"q1\\\", \\\"q2\\\", ...])\\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n\\n  <when_not_to_use>\\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\\n  </when_not_to_use>\\n\\n  <file_writing_policy>\\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\\n  </file_writing_policy>\\n\\n  <output_constraints>\\n    <artifact_policy>\\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\\n    </artifact_policy>\\n  </output_constraints>\\n  <session_continuity>\\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\\n  </session_continuity>\\n\\n</context_window_protection>\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"model\":\"sonnet\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/pretooluse.mjs\"","durationMs":353},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f5aad244-0ab4-4fa8-80c3-9be69e0ef7a5","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:29:27.911Z","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
