{"parentUuid":"07f3be55-ba2f-411a-8b95-af1d7ff49878","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezxpMmzv5kBRpdTJ26vk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018rCAMQvf4M4REw7qe4m986","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Rules and identity drift check","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are a READ-ONLY audit delegate for Eric's AI OS audit (2026-09-13, macOS, zsh). Two layers.\n\n**Layer \"Rules\" (window: last 7 days).** Rule sources: `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `~/.claude/machine.md`, `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md`, and the ELI5 output style (plain words, short sentences, 2 options max per decision). Evidence: Claude Code transcripts `~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl` modified in the last 7 days (`find ~/.claude/projects -name '*.jsonl' -mtime -7`). Report:\n  a) rules contradicted by what actually happened (a rule the agent broke, or a rule that is now false — e.g. a path or tool that changed);\n  b) corrections the USER gave twice or more that are not yet a rule anywhere (look at user messages that correct, redirect, or complain; search for phrases like \"no,\", \"don't\", \"stop\", \"I said\", \"again\", \"wrong\").\n  Transcripts are large — use grep/python to extract user-message text rather than reading whole files. Use `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5` if helpful.\n\n**Layer \"Identity\" (window: last 90 days).** Read `~/.claude/global-memory/USER.md`. Flag any role, family, career or tooling fact that recent evidence contradicts. Full 90-day transcript review is too large: use memsearch queries and the most recent sessions, and state the scope you actually covered.\n\nHARD RULES\n- Report findings only. Apply nothing. Do not create, edit, move or delete any file: no Write/Edit, no shell `>` redirects into files (pipe to stdout only), no git commits, no memory writes.\n- Transcripts contain private material. Quote at most one short line per finding; never paste health data; never touch a `DexaProject` path.\n- No `timeout` command exists. A `dcg` guard may block some shell shapes; if blocked, skip and note it.\n\nRETURN (under ~800 words):\n1. Rules findings: (a) contradicted rules, (b) repeated corrections not yet rules — each with session file name, date and a one-line quote/paraphrase, plus a proposed rule wording.\n2. Identity findings with evidence.\n3. \"Checked\" — how many transcripts, date range, method, memsearch queries run.\n4. \"Not checked\" — scope you did not cover (be explicit about the 90-day Identity scope)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2360,"cache_read_input_tokens":563268,"output_tokens":8179,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2188},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":586,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":66,"cache_read_input_tokens":281341,"cache_creation_input_tokens":586,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":586},"type":"message"},{"input_tokens":263188,"output_tokens":8365,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"advisor_message","model":"claude-fable-5-1"},{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8113,"cache_read_input_tokens":281927,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1774,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":10,"requestId":"req_011CezxpLVbV5kYWSuR78X8P","attributionSkill":"update-config","type":"assistant","uuid":"d3291e9d-548e-49f0-9616-6e35aa0674cc","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:30:06.898Z","advisorModel"