{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:33:45.808Z","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>adcc66282c1dd04fe</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_012JBiU8eRXTZNc96PUMEbmd</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b/tasks/adcc66282c1dd04fe.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"brain-audit: vault four C's\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Brain audit, Vault layer: 79 / 100 on 2026-09-13 (read-only)\n\n**Score: 79 / 100.** The last score was 67 on 2026-09-07. That was only 6 days ago, not a month, so most of the 12-point gain is noise. It mostly shows the known pattern again, not real improvement.\n\n| C | Score | Prior |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Context | 19 | 17 |\n| Connections | 18 | 22 |\n| Capabilities | 17 | 15 |\n| Cadence | 25 | 13 |\n| **Total** | **79** | **67** |\n\nHeadline: one interview session on 09-09 made `Notes/` look fresh. `weekly-review` is 42 days overdue, harvest and the ledger are going stale, and there are still 0 grill sessions.\n\n### 1. Evidence per C\n\n**Context 19.** On the rubric alone this is 25:\n- `USER.md` is at 1263/1375 (91%).\n- `MEMORY.md` is at 2489/2500. Last run it was 2502, over the cap.\n- There are 48 Tier A memories, up from 40.\n- `Knowledge/` was last touched 3 days ago.\n\nThe 09-07 report said its 17 was really a penalty for the missing grill capture, and asked future runs to keep scoring it that way. That gap is unchanged. There are 0 grill sessions and `Inbox/grills/` does not exist. `~/.claude/skills/grilling/SKILL.md` is still 12 lines from Jul 8 and saves nothing to disk. I added +2 for fixing the cap and the Tier A growth. `MEMORY.md` is only 11 characters under its cap, so one more write puts it over again.\n\n**Connections 18.** Meeting sync ran 1 day ago and `portfolio.json` is 3 days old, both on time. The ledger is from 2026-08-11, which is 33 days: past its 30-day window but short of the 60 days that drops the score to 13. The last run gave 22 when the ledger was 27 days old and still on time. Harvest last ran 08-11, and `Projects/` was last touched 08-11, the same day as the ledger. So one manual step, harvest, is what is going stale.\n\n**Capabilities 17.** Of the two builds proposed on 09-07:\n- **Build 1 (`/grill-me`):** not shipped, no trace of it.\n- **Build 2 (brain-audit on a monthly timer):** only half shipped.\n  - `com.keystone.aiosaudit` was added 09-12 (commit \"feat: monthly AIOS metrics on launchd\"). It runs on day 1 of each month at 14:00.\n  - The `aios-audit` skill hands the Vault layer to brain-audit.\n  - But `aios-audit-cron.sh` deliberately does not run the audit itself. It only records metrics and reminds him.\n\nSeparately, the 09-12 skill-bloat audit did prune skills. Skills in use: `interview-me` (09-09), `forecast-capture` (09-10), meeting-sync (daily). `measure.sh` reports `skills_installed: 63`, but memory says 117 after the archive. I report the script's number, and the mismatch is unresolved.\n\n**Cadence 25.** Scored strictly on the rubric: all 10 `com.keystone.*` jobs show `exit=0` and `Notes/` is 4 days old. The caveat is what that freshness rests on:\n- Interview dates are 07-27, 07-28, 07-29, 07-31, 08-03, then 09-09. That is one session in 37 days, two days after the last audit.\n- `Notes/` went from 23 to 24 files. Only one note is new; `waiting-for-the-ask-kills-the-idea.md` was an existing note that got edited.\n- `rituals.log` shows interview-me DUE and weekly-review OVERDUE at 42 days.\n- `Drafts/` is 44 days stale.\n\nThis is the \"synthesis restarted after the audit\" pattern in its first week, so expect this 25 to fall. The one `.errors.log` line (a compile lock held for 1550 minutes) is plumbing and belongs to `claude-stack-doctor`.\n\n**Three tests** (these don't change the score):\n- **Teammate: WARN.** Kitman vs MyLink appears only in Inbox status and review files. Nothing in Notes, Knowledge, Projects or Drafts.\n- **Context-switch: PASS.** `localhost:7373` returned 200, and `portfolio.json` is 3 days old.\n- **Head-emptying: FAIL.** The OKR Q1 gate in `MEMORY.md` is still \"DUE (was 8/31)\", now 13 days overdue. Kitman vs MyLink is still undecided and has no note behind it.\n\n**Bug that would mislead the agent:** `measure.sh` reports `last_audit: os-audit-2026-07-24 | 51 days ago`. It sorts audit files by name in reverse, so `os-` lands above `brain-`. The real last audit is `brain-audit-2026-09-07`, 6 days ago. I did not fix it.\n\n### 2. Two next builds\n\n1. **`/grill-me &lt;topic&gt;`, saving each session to `Inbox/grills/`.** This is the same proposal as last time, and it was never built. It is the best match for the bottleneck memory: he needs a thinking partner, and what comes out of it should be captured. It targets Context and the failed head-emptying test. First topics: Kitman vs MyLink, then the OKR Q1 gate.\n2. **Add a brain-audit line to `ritual-check.ps1`.** The audit would then show as OVERDUE in the daily rituals check, the way weekly-review does, on a job that already runs green. The monthly timer only reminds, so the audit is still manual and will die like the others. This targets Capabilities. The alternative was automating harvest to stop the ledger going stale; I didn't propose it to keep this to two.\n\n### 3. Checked\n- Read `brain-audit/SKILL.md` and `measure.sh`, then ran `measure.sh`, which only reads.\n- Read `audits/_trend.md`, `brain-audit-2026-09-07.md` and `user_working-conditions-bottleneck.md`.\n- In `global-memory/MEMORY.md`, read the Pending Decisions section.\n- Listed recent `Notes/` file dates, the files changed since the 09-07 audit, and recent interview files in Inbox.\n- Grepped the vault for Kitman/MyLink and OKR.\n- Looked for grill skills and `Inbox/grills`; read the `grilling` skill.\n- Read `.errors.log`, the keystone LaunchAgents list, and the rituals and aiosaudit plists.\n- Read `aios-audit-cron.sh` (the first 60 lines) and the brain-audit mentions in the `aios-audit` skill; grepped `ritual-check.ps1` for any audit hook.\n- Ran git logs since 09-07 in KeystoneOS and `~/.claude`.\n- Read the tail of `rituals.log` and `rituals.err`.\n- Checked `localhost:7373` with curl.\n- Counted skill directories and read the skill-bloat memory.\n\n### 4. Not checked / Skipped\n- **Skipped as instructed:** the dated report to `~/SecondBrain/audits/`, the `_trend.md` row, and all note edits. Nothing was written.\n- Windows-side vault or skills state.\n- How well memsearch actually retrieves.\n- Whether aiosaudit has ever fired. Its `/tmp` logs are empty since 09-12, and its first scheduled run is 10-01.\n- Why the skill count is 63 in the script but 117 in memory.\n- The content of the new note; I only checked its file dates, per the privacy rule.\n- The compile-lock error, which is left to `claude-stack-doctor`. No shell commands were blocked.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>76661</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>13</tool_uses><duration_ms>239550</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
