{"parentUuid":"e09d3818-7149-4f7d-bd6f-4d85adc6ad5d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"17bd151a-9d10-466e-90aa-96977ec73761","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a9ba13cc638d671da</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_0162PUd4bYVyezb4Q1EFYkwn</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b/tasks/a9ba13cc638d671da.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"improve-system: vault note rot\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result># SecondBrain audit: stale notes, conflicts, duplicates (2026-09-13, read-only)\n\nI changed nothing: no files written, moved or deleted.\n\nThe biggest issue is that project status in the vault has drifted. Four project briefs still read as active or paused but haven't been touched in 89–103 days, and the newer project list leaves three of them out. The old hub and the OKR tracker both still describe the June plan. I found no true word-for-word duplicates.\n\n## 1. Findings (577 notes; 15 most important shown)\n\n**Totals:** 11 stale seed notes, 4 stale project briefs, 5 conflicts, 0 confirmed duplicates (1 pair to check).\n\n### Conflicts\n\n1. **Older seed notes that a later note overturns, with nothing on the older note saying so.** Each older note links to its update but is still `status: seed` and has no superseded marker.\n   - `Notes/process-is-the-invariant.md` (07-27) → `Notes/releasing-the-seat-creates-room.md` (07-28), which calls itself \"the update to\" it.\n   - `Notes/design-the-conditions-not-the-discipline.md` (07-28) → `Notes/company-generates-solitude-refines.md` (07-29), which says it \"got the sign wrong\".\n   - `Notes/waiting-for-the-ask-kills-the-idea.md` (07-29) → `Notes/the-ask-has-to-precede-the-dependency.md` (09-09), which calls itself its \"limit condition\".\n   - **Proposed:** add a `superseded_by:` / \"see update\" line to each older note, or merge each pair. Don't archive them.\n2. **`Projects/Applied-Performance-Hub.md` disagrees with `Projects/Applied-Performance-Active-Projects.md`.**\n   - The Hub (updated 06-01) points to the OKRs as \"v2\" with Objective 1 \"Analytics &amp; Planning\". The OKR doc is v3 (four objectives, Objective 1 is \"Data Systems &amp; Infrastructure\") and has its own \"Superseded (v2 → v3, 2026-07-17)\" section.\n   - The Hub lists FaceComps, AI Integration and Data Governance. Active-Projects (08-11) names none of them.\n   - Neither note links to the other.\n   - **Proposed:** update the Hub to point at v3 and Active-Projects, or mark the Hub superseded.\n3. **The OKR tracker is frozen before its own deadline.**\n   - `Projects/okr-tracker/okrs.yaml` was last changed 06-02; `SCOREBOARD.md` was generated 06-12 (\"80 days to gate\").\n   - The gate was 2026-08-31, and the scoreboard still shows the three v2 objectives.\n   - **Proposed:** mark the tracker archived-at-gate, or rebuild it against v3.\n4. **Four notes use the ingest date as `created`.** Every other faith note uses the sermon or event date. These four all say 2026-06-22:\n   - `Knowledge/faith/grace-and-redemption-at-christmas.md` (a Christmas sermon)\n   - `Knowledge/frameworks/church-community-building-acts-2-framework.md`\n   - `Knowledge/coaching-frameworks/nfl-player-workload-management-carolina-panthers.md`\n   - `Knowledge/coaching-frameworks/nfl-return-to-play-hamstring-injury-protocol-carolina-panthers.md`\n   - **Proposed:** set `created` to the real event date.\n5. **Church content filed under frameworks.** `Knowledge/frameworks/church-community-building-acts-2-framework.md` is church material. **Proposed:** move it to `Knowledge/faith/`.\n\n### Stale\n\n6. **`Projects/Project_FaceComps-Practice-Simulator.md`** (103 days untouched): \"Active work — PAUSED (2026-05-29)\". Its \"Phase 1 … August deadline\" has passed, and Active-Projects doesn't list it. **Proposed:** set status to paused/dormant with the date, or archive.\n7. **`Projects/Project_AI-Integration.md`** (103 days, updated 06-01): its next steps are still May actions, and Active-Projects doesn't list it. **Proposed:** update the status or archive.\n8. **`Projects/Project_Athlete-Data-Governance.md`** (103 days): \"Next step: Await Anthony's formal proposal\", and Active-Projects doesn't list it. **Proposed:** update the status.\n9. **`Projects/Project_BAIR-Research-Initiative.md`** (89 days): has no frontmatter, and still says \"Status: Active — initial meeting 2025-09-16\". Active-Projects tracks BAIR as a key result due Aug 31. **Proposed:** add frontmatter and refresh the status.\n10. **11 seed notes older than 60 days** (100–114 days old; ages in parentheses). **Proposed:** promote each to evergreen or archive it.\n    - `self-authored-direction` (114)\n    - `planning-windows-compound` (114)\n    - `answers-without-questions` (108)\n    - `adoption-is-the-bottleneck` (108)\n    - `the-daily-on-ramp` (103)\n    - `standards-without-enforcement` (102)\n    - `equipping-yourself-to-surface-the-issue` (102)\n    - `impatience-is-a-signal-to-protect-consistency` (101)\n    - `delivery-is-part-of-the-mechanism` (101)\n    - `the-question-comes-before-the-data` (100)\n    - `a-timeline-is-leverage` (100)\n\n    Another 12 seeds are 41–50 days old and will pass 60 days by mid-October.\n11. **Six `Projects/Graphify/*/GRAPHIFY_SYNC.md` notes are generated snapshots from 06-09 to 06-11** (about 95 days old), and all say \"Status: Active\". `Baylor_Active_Initiatives` has no matching repo under `~/DEV` and cites a OneDrive path with Windows backslashes. **Proposed:** regenerate them or archive them; that one is orphaned.\n12. **`Projects/Applied-Performance-Stakeholder-Briefing-Plan.md`:** its status still reads \"deck v1 due Fri 2026-08-14\" even though the body mentions sent/delivered. **Proposed:** update the status.\n\n### Hygiene\n\n13. **Three `status:` fields hold sentences instead of a value:**\n    - the OKRs doc (\"v3 — restructured…\")\n    - the Stakeholder Briefing Plan\n    - `Projects/Applied-Performance-JD-2026/JD-feedback-memo-2026-07-20.md` (\"draft…\")\n\n    Also, 127 of 577 notes (22%) have no `status`. `Knowledge/frameworks/risk-stratification-practitioner-evidence-gate.md` has no frontmatter at all. **Proposed:** normalize.\n14. **Windows-only paths in notes read on both machines.** `~/Desktop/DEV/Football/...` is the Windows layout; on this Mac the repos are at `~/DEV/Football/`. It appears in Project_FaceComps, Project_SpeedProfiling and Applied-Performance-Hub. **Proposed:** switch to the repo URL or a relative `DEV/Football/...` form.\n\n### Possible duplicate (unconfirmed)\n\n15. **Two baseball notes.** `Knowledge/sport-science/baseball-offseason-training-protocol.md` and `Knowledge/sport-science/baseball-training-program-design.md` share the same date (2026-04-30), source (\"Fireflies meeting transcript\") and topic, and link each other. Their text overlaps only about 4%, and neither records a meeting ID. **Proposed:** a human checks whether this was one meeting ingested twice (then merge) or two sessions (then no action).\n\n**Not a problem:**\n- The six GRAPHIFY_SYNC notes (0.40–0.49 text overlap) and several library research-paper pairs (0.40–0.42) only share template text.\n- The \"loneliness\" faith notes (61% vs 60% statistic) are separate sermons.\n- No action on any of these.\n\n## 2. Checked\n\n- **Folders:** `~/SecondBrain/Notes` (24), `Knowledge` (421, of which 358 are in `library/`), `Projects` (133). That is 578 files, 577 excluding `Knowledge/library/README.md`.\n- **Stale:** read every note's frontmatter; checked seed `created` dates against 60 days, and modified dates for the `Project_*` files against 30 days. For the old project briefs, I read their opening lines.\n- **Duplicates:** looked for identical titles and filenames, similar titles (85% or closer), and text overlap between notes. Also checked the library for repeated DOIs (219 DOIs, none repeated).\n- **Conflicts:** compared opening claims and tags of the 24 Notes and 62 non-library Knowledge notes. I read further only for suspected pairs, checked whether the older note in each update chain links forward, and compared status wording in the Hub, Active-Projects and the OKR doc.\n- **Also checked:** whether the repo paths cited in notes exist on disk, and the last changed dates in `okrs.yaml`.\n\n## 3. Not checked / Skipped\n\n- **Step 0 (apply approved proposals): not run, as instructed.** The ledger `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/reports/proposals-pending.md` has no items (\"_None yet_\"): 0 approved, 0 open.\n- **Nothing written:** no proposals, no ledger entries, no files.\n- **Excluded by the skill:** `Archive/`, `Inbox/`, `morning-briefings/`, and non-markdown files (apart from a date check on `okrs.yaml`).\n- **Not compared claim by claim:** library entries against each other (only the duplicate checks above ran), and Knowledge notes outside the named pairs.\n- **Out of scope:** `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/` and `~/.claude/global-memory/`. No DexaProject paths were touched. No commands were blocked by the shell guard.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>105600</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>13</tool_uses><duration_ms>298877</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"4b5df634-21fe-4540-9c16-93542660c876","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:34:52.253Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
