n- Read the doctor-plus skill.\n- Measured sizes of: global CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, machine.md, TOOLPATHS.md, `global-memory/{USER,MEMORY}.md`, the `~/DEV` router `.md` files, and the project memory index.\n- Parsed `settings.json` for hooks, skill overrides and output style. Read the ELI5 style and `skills/CLAUDE.md`.\n- Read the injection logic in `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` and the compiler's `session-start.py`, and sized the KeystoneOS snapshot and knowledge index.\n- Parsed the frontmatter of all 61 `~/.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` for description length, code-block count and absolute-rule count.\n- Checked `CreateSkill` Workflows for the Examples requirement.\n- Listed every project CLAUDE.md to depth 4 by size and date count, and pulled the cited lines from Ath_Medicine and FaceComps.\n- Compared the two hook directories with `cmp` and diffed the ones that differ.\n- Compared caps and Windows wording between memory-write and AGENTS.md. Caps match; the Windows status does not.\n- Read the `skill-bloat-and-promotion` and `hook-two-copies-trap` memory files.\n- Checked tests, spreadsheets and specs in 6 active builds, and counted STATUS.md files.\n- Every command was read-only. Two used `&gt; /dev/null`, and one glob gave a harmless \"no matches\" error. No file was touched.\n\n## 3. Not checked\n- **`/doctor` and `claude doctor`:** interactive, and skipped as instructed. Run `/doctor` in your own session for that half.\n- **Plugin skill description size:** 564 plugin SKILL.md files are cached, but most are disabled plugins or old versions. The per-session count of about 40 comes from the session skill list, not a measurement.\n- **`~/.agents/skills`** (213 entries vs 61): outside scope. I spot-checked 4 and they were identical.\n- **Not scanned:** project CLAUDE.md files deeper than depth 4, `_ARCHIVE`, and nested per-directory CLAUDE.md files other than `skills/`.\n- **Not scanned:** the content of the 50 project memory files, beyond the index and the two memos.