{"parentUuid":"05f6c881-75af-4a7f-822c-0500300a5eea","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7ff1caa4-64c9-42b2-9fcc-ba8ec9754423","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a6fbd873c46e9ca1e</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01AzNZiwLTFHuWuQXLca94Ps</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b/tasks/a6fbd873c46e9ca1e.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"os-audit: substrate and data feeds\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## OS Audit — Checks 1 &amp; 3 (Routing Integrity + Freshness)\n\n### Findings\n\n**GREEN — Substrate routing resolves.** Verified every path/pointer named in `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `~/.claude/AGENTS.md`, `~/.claude/machine.md`, and all 8 `~/DEV/*.md` routers (CLAUDE, FOOTBALL, PERFORMANCE, RESEARCH, PLATFORM, PROGRAM, PERSONAL, COMMANDS) — roughly 150 referenced folders/files, including all COMMANDS.md script paths (`keystone.ps1`, `daily-backup.ps1`, `weekly_run.sh`, `skill-button.sh`, etc.) and all 8 `~/go/bin/` CLIs. All exist. No dead paths, no misroutes found.\n\n**AMBER — FOOTBALL.md archive section is location-ambiguous** [confusion]. The \"Archive / dormant\" entries `_obsidian_extracted_from_FaceComps/` and `Football_Data_DEV/` sit directly under the \"Inside `Football/`\" table with no path prefix, implying they're inside `Football/`. Both actually live at `~/DEV/` root (confirmed: missing under `Football/`, present at `DEV/`). Fix: prefix each with `../` or move the note out of the Football/ subsection.\n\n**GREEN — Memory index integrity.** All 45 files (`project_*`, `user_*`, `feedback_*`, `reference_*`) listed in `MEMORY.md` resolve to real files in `~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/`. One extra file on disk (`project_headless-claude-tool-deny-gap.md`) postdates the frozen session snapshot — expected drift, not a bug. `_archive/` subfolder is self-documented (own README), not an orphan.\n\n**GREEN — DexaProject move claim verified** (existence check only, no content read): new Google Drive path exists; `~/DEV/DexaProject` correctly absent, matching PERFORMANCE.md's claim.\n\n**GREEN — CFBD feed is FRESH.** `CFB_Victory_Model/data/weekly_snapshots/` newest files are the `2026-09-10_*.csv` set (mtime 2026-09-11) — matches the declared Wednesday-capture cadence, one day behind today (2026-09-13, a Sunday). No gap.\n\n**GREEN — Fireflies feed is FRESH, raw and ingested layers match.** `fireflies-pp-cli transcripts status` shows the newest raw transcript at 2026-09-11. `SecondBrain/Inbox/meetings/` (the ingested layer) has same-week notes through 2026-09-11/12. No raw-vs-ingested gap. (Note: per-project meeting folders like `Applied-Performance-Hub/meetings/` are dormant since July — that's a triage/organization question, out of this check's scope.)\n\n**AMBER/RED — GPS feed looks FROZEN** [poisoning risk]. `DataBase_GPS_Reporting/gps_report/data/gps_history.duckdb` (the actual GPS session database) was last modified 2026-08-01 — **before** the 2026-08-24 season start. `gps_report/Reports/` newest dated output folder is `2026-03-06`. Football season is ~3 weeks in with presumably weekly GPS loads, and nothing in `PERFORMANCE.md` flags this pipeline as paused. Separately, `Catapult_API/` (a different GPS-adjacent project) has raw JSON dumps dated 2026-09-06 — one week old — but filenames like `_auburn_g1_dataset.json` look like sample/test data, not a labeled recurring pull. Can't tell from files alone whether GPS ingestion quietly migrated from `DataBase_GPS_Reporting` to `Catapult_API`, or simply stalled. **Question for Eric**, not an assumption.\n\n**AMBER — Zotero is mildly DRIFTING.** `zotero-research-library-pp-cli cache status` reports last sync ~268h ago (~11 days, ≈2026-09-02). RESEARCH.md declares no fixed cadence for this feed, so not clearly broken, but worth a manual re-sync before trusting library-advisor results as current.\n\n### Checked\n- Read all 8 `~/DEV/*.md` routers, `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `~/.claude/AGENTS.md`, `~/.claude/machine.md`, and `~/.claude/projects/.../MEMORY.md`.\n- Ran `test -e` existence checks (no content reads) against every path/pointer extracted from those files, plus a reverse check on `~/DEV` top-level dirs vs. the routers.\n- Freshness: `fireflies-pp-cli transcripts status`, `zotero-research-library-pp-cli cache status`, file-date surveys of `CFB_Victory_Model/data/`, `CFB_Forecast_Archive/`, `DataBase_GPS_Reporting/`, `Catapult_API/`, and `SecondBrain/*/meetings/`, plus `git log -1` on the GPS and Catapult repos.\n- DexaProject: existence-only check (`[ -e ]`), no directory listing or content read, per hard rule.\n\n### Not checked\n- Contents of the 23 project-level `CLAUDE.md` files (Check 1 step 5's \"spot-check hardcoded paths in skills/agents\") — only sampled ~7 skill files for existence, didn't open each to verify internal path claims; time/scope-bounded.\n- Windows-side paths (`~/Desktop/DEV`) — unreachable from this Mac session.\n- Whether GPS ingestion actually moved to `Catapult_API/` — inferred from file dates only; needs Eric's confirmation, not assumed either way.\n- Raw Zotero.app library (`~/Zotero/storage`) freshness directly — an early `find` over that tree produced runaway output (500+ storage-folder names) and was abandoned mid-command to avoid context bloat; freshness was instead read from the `pp-cli` cache-sync layer only.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>137574</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>19</tool_uses><duration_ms>349764</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"257eea44-db43-43a7-80a7-6810c8ca2f3c","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:35:23.086Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipAttachme