{"parentUuid":"69c41a8e-5bf9-40f7-a0e0-b300b433cc8d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezybdgDEXzzQK5fDtqCh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 6 helpers are done. The audit has everything it needs.\n\nNow I write these, all at once:\n- The audit report.\n- The Pi-paused and roster updates in `STATUS.md` and the execution log.\n- The fix to the stale memory line.\n\nI also read `rot.md` with the Read tool. The edit tool needs that read before it will change the file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3834,"cache_read_input_tokens":317327,"output_tokens":8071,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1827},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3834,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":8071,"cache_read_input_tokens":317327,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3834,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3834},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CezybcaUqTeHddJeZvkua","type":"assistant","uuid":"0713c1b6-89b5-476f-813e-f1d5b70a7575","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:37:27.686Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"0713c1b6-89b5-476f-813e-f1d5b70a7575","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezybdgDEXzzQK5fDtqCh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C6UbFxFGFxxbsDSfVWSVeQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md","content":"# AIOS audit — 2026-09-13\n\nFirst full run of `aios-audit`. The skill's trigger was verified headlessly on 2026-09-12.\nThis run followed its body by hand, from a background Claude Code session rooted at `~/DEV`:\nthe project skill is not listed there. The five delegate layers ran as parallel **read-only**\nsubagents under the `rot.md` delegation contract. Every delegate returned a \"checked\" and a\n\"not checked\" list, and each receipt below is scoped to that list.\n\nNothing was deleted, archived, disabled or edited as part of the audit. Every fix below is a\nproposal.\n\nDone just before the audit, by Eric's decision: **roster Option B**. The 7 owned skills that\nwere `\"off\"` in Claude Code are on again (`~/.claude` commit `21c686d`). **Pi trial paused** by Eric.\n\n## Step 0 — what was due\n\nEvery layer was `unknown` except Skills (audited 2026-09-12, inside its 1-month window).\nSkills is green and skipped. The other 10 layers ran.\n\n## Step 1–2 — metrics and invariants\n\n`python3 scripts/aios-metrics.py`, 2026-09-13, exit 0, no errors:\n\n| Key | Value | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tracked_symlinks_in_canonical` | 0 | GREEN |\n| `pool_view_drift` / `codex_view_drift` | 0 / 0 | GREEN |\n| `pool_dangling` / `codex_dangling` | 0 / 0 | GREEN |\n| `portability_failures` | **0** (was 7) | GREEN — roster decision resolved it |\n| `canonical_skills` / `third_party_links_in_canonical` | 42 / 19 | info |\n| `pool_third_party` / `codex_third_party` | 168 / 10 | info |\n| `never_used` | 20 | info — `usage_scope=claude_code_transcripts_only`, `usage_unreadable_transcripts=0`. Includes the 7 skills that were off until today, so they could not have been used in Claude. Not DELETE evidence. |\n| `agents` | 0 | no agents defined |\n| `hooks_claude` / `hooks_codex` | 61 / 59 | see Hooks |\n| `roster_tokens_est` | 6671 | info |\n\n## Skills — GREEN, skipped\n\nAudited 2026-09-12. Parity re-checked today: `skill-portability-check.py` → 42 checked, 0 failing.\n\n## Agents — GREEN\n\n`~/.claude/agents/*.md`: 0. No agents defined.\n\n## Hooks — RED (delegate: claude-stack-doctor)\n\n- **RED — Codex snapshot hook is an old copy.** `~/.codex/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js`\n  is 31 lines; `~/.claude/hooks/` has the 98-line version. The Codex copy injects only the\n  KeystoneOS pointer — no `USER.md`, no `MEMORY.md`, no `.errors.log` surfacing, no loud failure\n  on a missing source. Codex sessions start without the profile and memory. This is the\n  two-copies trap again.\n- Only in `~/.claude/hooks`: `herdr-agent-state.sh`, `memsearch-sync.js.bak-20260814` — look intentional/inert.\n- In both but different: `transcript-capture.js` (comments only), `memsearch-sync.js.bak-2026-09-02` (dead backup).\n- **AMBER — `dcg` registered twice** under PreToolUse in `~/.claude/settings.json` (absolute path and\n  guarded exec), so it runs twice per Bash call (found by doctor-plus).\n- GREEN: all `com.keystone.*` launchd jobs exit 0; compiler venv and memsearch 0.4.17 resolve;\n  flush pipeline normal through 2026-09-12; backup 2026-09-12 OK with an SSD receipt; global-memory in sync.\n- AMBER: `compile.py --auto` held its lock ~26 h before reclaim (2026-09-13 04:30 UTC); later compiles succeeded.\n\nNot checked: `stack-check.ps1` / `handoff-check.ps1` not run; Windows side.\n\n## Rules — AMBER (audited directly, 7 days)\n\nNo correction repeated twice in the last 7 days. Rules now false or in conflict:\n\n- `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md`: \"23 projects carry their own CLAUDE.md\" — about 130 now (the 2026-09-09 GitHub move added one per repo). \"~155 skills\" — about 65 after the 2026-09-12 cut.\n- **`memory-write` SKILL.md (lines ~80, ~101) says the Windows box was \"retired 2026-08-14\"** and forbids writing its slugs. `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md` and `USER.md` say Windows is active again. `AGENTS.md` lets memory-write win a conflict, so the stale rule wins. `project_backup-sync-system.md` repeats \"Windows retired\" in 3 places; only the Windows scheduled tasks were retired.\n- `USER.md` says \"Tool paths: see CLAUDE.md\"; `machine.md` says their one home is `TOOLPATHS.md`.\n- `status-report` skill asks 4–5 numbered questions per turn (`SKILL.md:225`); the ELI5 style says 2 options max.\n- `project_dcg-guard-blocks.md` lacks one blocked shape: `cat > \"$DIR/file\" <<'EOF'`.\n- `.errors.log` is tracked in the synced global-memory repo and caused a merge conflict on 2026-09-11. No rule says it is per-machine.\n\nNot checked: Codex sessions; subagent transcripts.\n\n## Identity — AMBER (partial scope)\n\n- A child's age in `USER.md` carries an \"as of 2026-09-01\" date but matches June-era sources. One of the two is stale. Eric to confirm.\n- \"No cloud/servers/schedulers without Baylor IT approval\" is broader than practice (8 launchd jobs, private GitHub, Drive backup). It probably means Baylor data and systems. Eric to reword.\n- \"OneDrive project folders — beware DuckDB locks\" looks outdated; projects live in `~/DEV` on GitHub.\n\n**Scope:** last 7 days of Claude transcripts plus 11 memsearch queries — not the 90-day window.\n\n## Memory (agent) — AMBER (audited directly)\n\n- Index ↔ file resolution: every Mac-slug `MEMORY.md` resolves both ways. The retired\n  `C--Users-eric-rash` slug has 4 files missing from its index. Report only — memory-write says never write there.\n- **Stale fact:** `project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md:153–157` says the 7 skills are off. Now false (fixed right after this report, as a consequence of Eric's decision, not as an audit action).\n- `~/.claude/global-memory/MEMORY.md`: 2,441 of 2,500 chars. 11 time-dimensioned phrases, including \"DUE (was 8/31)\" (OKR Q1 gate, now 13 days overdue) and the 9/7 status report \"UNSENT\".\n- The DEV-slug `MEMORY.md` index carries facts in some lines (\"morning-cadence dies on…\", \"reminder sent 9/8\"), against its own header.\n- `project_backup-sync-system.md` has the most dated phrases (10).\n\n## Memory (vault notes) — AMBER (delegate: improve-system)\n\nScanned 577 notes in `~/SecondBrain/` Notes, Knowledge, Projects. Step 0 suppressed; 0 approved proposals were pending.\n\n- 11 seed notes older than 60 days; 12 more pass 60 days by mid-October.\n- 4 project briefs read active/paused but are 89–103 days old and absent from `Applied-Performance-Active-Projects.md`: FaceComps simulator, AI Integration, Athlete Data Governance, BAIR.\n- `Applied-Performance-Hub.md` still points at OKRs v2; the OKR doc is v3. `okr-tracker/` froze on 06-12, before its own 08-31 gate.\n- 3 older notes are overturned by newer notes but carry no superseded marker.\n- 6 `Graphify/*/GRAPHIFY_SYNC.md` snapshots from June say \"Active\"; one names no existing repo.\n- Hygiene: sentence-valued `status:` fields; 22% of notes without `status`; Windows-only `~/Desktop/DEV` paths in 3 notes.\n- 0 confirmed duplicates; one baseball pair to check by hand.\n\n## Vault — AMBER, 79/100 (delegate: brain-audit)\n\nContext 19, Connections 18, Capabilities 17, Cadence 25 (was 67 on 2026-09-07). Report and trend row suppressed.\nThe rise is mostly one interview session on 09-09. Weekly review is 42 days overdue; the ledger is 33 days old;\n0 grill sessions; the 09-07 build \"`/grill-me`\" is unbuilt. Head-emptying test FAIL (OKR gate, Kitman vs MyLink).\nBug: `measure.sh` reports `last_audit` as an os-audit from 07-24 because it sorts by name.\n\n## Substrate — GREEN with one AMBER (delegate: os-audit Check 1)\n\nAbout 150 paths named in `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `machine.md` and the 8 `~/DEV` routers all exist.\nAMBER: `FOOTBALL.md` lists `_obsidian_extracted_from_FaceComps/` and `Football_Data_DEV/` under \"Inside `Football/`\";\nboth are at `~/DEV/` root.\n\nNot checked: internal path claims inside the ~130 project `CLAUDE.md` files.\n\n## Data feeds — RED (delegate: os-audit Check 3)\n\n| Feed | Newest data | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| CFBD | `weekly_snapshots/2026-09-10_*` | GREEN |\n| Fireflies | raw 2026-09-11; vault 2026-09-11/12 | GREEN |\n| Zotero | cache sync ~11 days ago | AMBER |\n| **GPS** | `gps_history.duckdb` modified **2026-08-01**, before the 08-24 season start; newest report folder 2026-03-06 | **RED or moved** — `Catapult_API/` has JSON from 2026-09-06 that looks like sample data. Eric to say where GPS sessions land now. |\n\n## Context posture — AMBER (delegate: doctor-plus; `/doctor` not run)\n\n- Shift 1: `~/.claude/skills/CLAUDE.md` spends ~3× the rule on enforcement, and cites a memory file that does not exist.\n- Shift 2: the CreateSkill scaffold and validator make `## Examples` mandatory.\n- Shift 3: skill descriptions of 800–1,200 chars (`scroll-craft`, `impeccable`, `ISA`, `CreateSkill`); project `CLAUDE.md` files of 21–27k chars load in full.\n- Shift 4: the memory-write Windows conflict and the double `dcg` registration (above).\n- Shift 5: status and findings sections inside project `CLAUDE.md` files (Ath_Medicine, FaceComps, PlayerProfiles_FB, cmj-traffic-light) belong in `docs/STATUS.md`.\n- Shift 6: GREEN — active builds use real references (xlsx prototypes, tests).\n\n## Proposed next builds (exactly two, ranked)\n\n1. **Fix the cross-harness drift that every session pays for.** Copy the 98-line\n   `~/.claude/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js` over the Codex copy, and correct the\n   \"Windows retired\" rule in `memory-write` SKILL.md and `project_backup-sync-system.md`.\n   Starts with: *\"Sync the Codex snapshot hook and fix the Windows-retired rule.\"*\n2. **Confirm the GPS feed in season.** Find where Catapult sessions land since 08-24 and\n   whether `gps_history.duckdb` stalled. Starts with Eric answering: *\"GPS sessions now land in ___.\"*\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3834,"cache_read_input_tokens":317327,"output_tokens":8071,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1827},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3834,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":8071,"cache_read_input_tokens":317327,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3834,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3834},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CezybcaUqTeHddJeZvkua","type":"assistant","uuid":"d9c40566-0549-4fd2-a9d3-a9a56921809c","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:38:15.944Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
