{"parentUuid":"5e64697e-e58d-4589-8697-bac3a1157bb0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezyiNenPfoUahUVgJebS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WkU98tSiXi9kZsETsZSH2w","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/rot.md","old_string":"| Identity | `global-memory/USER.md` | very slow | 3 months | unknown | memory-write |","new_string":"| Identity | `global-memory/USER.md` | very slow | 3 months | 2026-09-13 (partial: 7 days of sessions + memsearch, not 90 days) | memory-write |"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9745,"cache_read_input_tokens":321161,"output_tokens":2496,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":295},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9745,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":2496,"cache_read_input_tokens":321161,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9745,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9745},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CezyiMFgt4cwMZs5ZCqpu","type":"assistant","uuid":"6805a4f2-b5f4-4a9a-b306-88670fc612cb","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:38:40.128Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"6805a4f2-b5f4-4a9a-b306-88670fc612cb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d7908bed-a694-4873-b058-61f2cd834cd8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WkU98tSiXi9kZsETsZSH2w","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/.claude/rot.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"496c4a69-5d18-4782-93b6-1f0b22db75ae","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:38:42.595Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/rot.md","oldString":"| Identity | `global-memory/USER.md` | very slow | 3 months | unknown | memory-write |","newString":"| Identity | `global-memory/USER.md` | very slow | 3 months | 2026-09-13 (partial: 7 days of sessions + memsearch, not 90 days) | memory-write |","originalFile":"# rot.md — how fast each AIOS layer goes stale\n\nAudit each layer on its own clock, not all at once. `aios-audit` reads this\nfile: any layer past due, or marked `unknown`, is a finding.\n\n**A date here is a receipt, not an intention.** Write one only after that\nlayer's check in the last column has actually run and produced output.\n\n| Layer | Where it lives | Rots | Audit every | Last audited | Owner | Concrete check |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Identity | `global-memory/USER.md` | very slow | 3 months | unknown | memory-write | Read USER.md; flag any role, family, or career fact contradicted by the last 90 days of sessions. |\n| Substrate | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `~/DEV/*.md` routers | slow | 3 months | unknown | os-audit | Delegate to `os-audit` Check 1 (routing integrity). |\n| Skills | `~/.claude/skills/` | fast | 1 month | 2026-09-12 | aios-audit | `skill-portability-check.py` + never-used list + the crutch test below. |\n| Agents | `~/.claude/agents/` | fast | 1 month | unknown | aios-audit | Count `*.md`. Currently **0 exist** — report \"no agents defined\" and skip until one does. |\n| Rules | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` behaviour rules, output styles | fastest | 1 week | unknown | aios-audit | Diff CLAUDE.md against the last 7 days of sessions: any rule contradicted by what actually happened, and any correction the user repeated twice that is not yet a rule. |\n| Hooks | `~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/` | slow | 6 months | unknown | claude-stack-doctor | Delegate. Also diff the two copies — they must match (`hook-two-copies-trap`). |\n| Memory (agent) | `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/`, `global-memory/` | medium | 1 month | unknown | **aios-audit itself** | Audited directly — see the delegation contract below. `improve-system` does NOT cover these stores. Check: every `MEMORY.md` index line resolves to a file; every memory file appears in its index; `global-memory/MEMORY.md` is under its 2,500-char cap; flag time-dimensioned facts (counters, \"still open\", past-tense futures). |\n| Memory (vault notes) | `~/SecondBrain/` notes | medium | 1 month | unknown | improve-system | Delegate — but read-only, per the contract below. |\n| Data feeds | Fireflies, GPS, CFBD, Zotero | varies | 1 week | unknown | os-audit | Delegate to `os-audit` Check 3 (freshness). |\n| Vault | `~/SecondBrain/` | medium | 1 month | unknown | brain-audit | Delegate to `brain-audit` (four C's score). |\n| Context posture | workspace-wide | medium | 3 months | unknown | doctor-plus | Delegate to `doctor-plus`. |\n\n## The question that governs a skill's fate\n\nNot \"how often did I run it?\" but **\"would the current model do this fine\nwithout the skill?\"** If yes, the skill is a crutch that now limits the model.\nDelete it. Keep only skills carrying tacit knowledge the model cannot know:\nforce-plate thresholds, GPS conventions, Baylor reporting norms, Eric's own\nroutines.\n\nSeasonal skills (`forecast-capture`, `ingest-book`) are exempt from low-use\npressure. Judge them in season.\n\n## Delegation contract (R2-09)\n\nA delegate is invoked **read-only**, for a **named scope**, and its receipt is\nwritten **only** for the scope it actually covered.\n\n1. **Read-only.** Before invoking a delegate, instruct it explicitly: report\n   findings, apply nothing, write no ledger, create no files. Several delegates\n   (`improve-system` among them) begin by applying previously approved proposals\n   — that must be suppressed. `aios-audit` writes only its own report and the\n   `Last audited` column.\n2. **Scope must be verified, not assumed.** A delegate's actual coverage is what\n   its body scans, not what this table wishes it scanned. `improve-system` scans\n   `~/SecondBrain/` — Notes, Knowledge, Projects. It does **not** touch\n   `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/` or `global-memory/`. Those are audited by\n   `aios-audit` directly.\n3. **A receipt covers only what was checked.** If a delegate returns findings for\n   a narrower scope than its row claims, write the date **and** a scope note, or\n   leave the row `unknown`. Never stamp a date because a delegate exited cleanly.\n\n## Layout invariants the audit must assert\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/` is canonical, is a git repo, and contains **no TRACKED symlinks**\n  (`git ls-files -s` shows no mode 120000). On-disk links to third-party skills are\n  expected; they are listed in the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` (never the tracked\n  `.gitignore`), and a pre-commit hook refuses to commit one. What must never happen is\n  committing a link, because Windows pulls this repo and a Mac link is dead there.\n- `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are **generated views**. Each carries\n  a `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` manifest. Every entry **in the manifest** must be\n  a symlink on Mac (a copy on Windows); wrong representation is drift.\n- Entries **not** in the manifest are third-party installs (`npx skills add`).\n  They are counted and reported, **never** flagged as errors and never pruned.\n- Support directories (`_shared/`) have no SKILL.md and must never be pruned.\n\n## Direction of travel\n\n**Fewer skills, stricter rules.** Skills get deleted; rules get sharpened.\n\n## Cadence\n\nMonthly metrics: launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit`, day 1 at 14:00.\nIt writes a trend row and a nudge. It does not commit and does not push.\nThe agentic audit is run by hand: \"audit my AI OS\" in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":8,"oldLines":7,"newStart":8,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," | Layer | Where it lives | Rots | Audit every | Last audited | Owner | Concrete check |"," |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","-| Identity | `global-memory/USER.md` | very slow | 3 months | unknown | memory-write | Read USER.md; flag any role, family, or career fact contradicted by the last 90 days of sessions. |","+| Identity | `global-memory/USER.md` | very slow | 3 months | 2026-09-13 (partial: 7 days of sessions + memsearch, not 90 days) | memory-write | Read USER.md; flag any role, family, or career fact contradicted by the last 90 days of sessions. |"," | Substrate | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `~/DEV/*.md` routers | slow | 3 months | unknown | os-audit | Delegate to `os-audit` Check 1 (routing integrity). |"," | Skills | `~/.claude/skills/` | fast | 1 month | 2026-09-12 | aios-audit | `skill-portability-check.py` + never-used list + the crutch test below. |"," | Agents | `~/.claude/agents/` | fast | 1 month | unknown | aios-audit | Count `*.md`. Currently **0 exist** — report \"no agents defined\" and skip until one does. |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6805a4f2-b5f4-4a9a-b306-88670fc612cb","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"496c4a69-5d18-4782-93b6-1f0b22db75ae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezyiNenPfoUahUVgJebS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013muuUsKe22dKLpL2re33db","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md","old_string":"## Next\n- **Eric decides the roster** (see Open questions). Then re-run\n  `python3 scripts/skill-portability-check.py` — it should reach 0 failing.\n- **Eric runs \"audit my AI OS\"** interactively in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`. The Task 6 smoke\n  test was headless and wrote no report, so the full audit flow is unverified.\n- **Task 8:** run plan Task 8 Step 1 in a terminal (commands in the Pi trial report),\n  then a sudo-capable session runs Steps 2–8. Or accept BLOCKED.\n- Gate D (verification before completion) after those.\n\n## Open questions\n- **Roster:** 7 owned skills are `\"off\"` in `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides` but\n  published to Codex and Pi: ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review,\n  pp-espn, session-miner. Re-enable them in Claude Code, or retire them from canonical.\n  Flagged by Codex in every review round since Gate B.","new_string":"## Next\n- **Audit build 1:** sync the Codex snapshot hook (`~/.codex/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js`\n  is a stale 31-line copy) and fix the \"Windows retired\" rule in `memory-write` and\n  `project_backup-sync-system.md`.\n- **Audit build 2:** Eric confirms where GPS sessions land since 2026-08-24.\n- Other audit proposals (vault note rot, double `dcg` registration, stale router counts,\n  `measure.sh` sort bug): see `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`.\n- **Task 8 (Pi trial):** paused by Eric.\n\n## Open questions\n- Where do GPS sessions land now: `DataBase_GPS_Reporting` or `Catapult_API`?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9745,"cache_read_input_tokens":321161,"output_tokens":2496,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":295},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9745,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":2496,"cache_read_input_tokens":321161,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9745,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9745},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CezyiMFgt4cwMZs5ZCqpu","type":"assistant","uuid":"3c844251-17a0-46d2-8879-67232d6b7ac4","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:38:47.648Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"3c844251-17a0-46d2-8879-67232d6b7ac4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d7908bed-a694-4873-b058-61f2cd834cd8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013muuUsKe22dKLpL2re33db","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"72cdf012-2cea-4f22-9f69-8cdfb3eb8d53","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:38:47.752Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md","oldString":"## Next\n- **Eric decides the roster** (see Open questions). Then re-run\n  `python3 scripts/skill-portability-check.py` — it should reach 0 failing.\n- **Eric runs \"audit my AI OS\"** interactively in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`. The Task 6 smoke\n  test was headless and wrote no report, so the full audit flow is unverified.\n- **Task 8:** run plan Task 8 Step 1 in a terminal (commands in the Pi trial report),\n  then a sudo-capable session runs Steps 2–8. Or accept BLOCKED.\n- Gate D (verification before completion) after those.\n\n## Open questions\n- **Roster:** 7 owned skills are `\"off\"` in `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides` but\n  published to Codex and Pi: ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review,\n  pp-espn, session-miner. Re-enable them in Claude Code, or retire them from canonical.\n  Flagged by Codex in every review round since Gate B.","newString":"## Next\n- **Audit build 1:** sync the Codex snapshot hook (`~/.codex/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js`\n  is a stale 31-line copy) and fix the \"Windows retired\" rule in `memory-write` and\n  `project_backup-sync-system.md`.\n- **Audit build 2:** Eric confirms where GPS sessions land since 2026-08-24.\n- Other audit proposals (vault note rot, double `dcg` registration, stale router counts,\n  `measure.sh` sort bug): see `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`.\n- **Task 8 (Pi trial):** paused by Eric.\n\n## Open questions\n- Where do GPS sessions land now: `DataBase_GPS_Reporting` or `Catapult_API`?","originalFile":"# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\nLast updated 2026-09-13 (Mac, background session). Evidence for every claim below is in\n`docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md`.\n\n## Current state\n- The dominant thread is the **harness-agnostic AIOS plan**:\n  `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md` (approved; do not edit —\n  its SHA-256 `71b5242e…` binds the approval). Goal: every skill Eric owns loads\n  identically in Claude Code, Codex and Pi from one versioned canonical folder, plus a\n  recurring audit that keeps the AIOS from rotting.\n- Architecture: `~/.claude/skills/` (repo `erash11/claude-skills`) is canonical and holds\n  real directories only. `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are generated views\n  rebuilt per machine by `sync-to-codex.sh` / `.ps1` — symlinks on Mac, copies on Windows.\n- **Tasks 1–7 done.** Task 8 (Pi trial) **PAUSED by Eric** (2026-09-13). It also needs\n  `sudo` to create `piuser`. Report and unblock commands: `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pi-trial.md`.\n- **Roster resolved 2026-09-13 (Option B):** the 7 owned skills are on again in Claude Code\n  (`~/.claude` commit `21c686d`). Checker: 42/42 portable.\n- **First `aios-audit` ran 2026-09-13:** `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`. Two RED:\n  the Codex snapshot hook is a stale copy, and the GPS feed looks frozen since 2026-08-01.\n- **Gate B** (2 rounds) and **Gate C** (2 rounds) run. Every code finding is fixed:\n  C-01 exec bits, C-02 atomic stale-lock reclaim, C-03 usage metrics scoped to Claude\n  transcripts, IR-01 checker rejects list/map descriptions. IR-01 is host-tested but\n  not re-inspected by Codex.\n- Monthly metrics run on launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit` (day 1, 14:00). It writes a row\n  to `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` and a nudge; it never commits.\n- `portability_failures=7`: the open roster decision below. Every other invariant is 0.\n\n## Next\n- **Eric decides the roster** (see Open questions). Then re-run\n  `python3 scripts/skill-portability-check.py` — it should reach 0 failing.\n- **Eric runs \"audit my AI OS\"** interactively in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`. The Task 6 smoke\n  test was headless and wrote no report, so the full audit flow is unverified.\n- **Task 8:** run plan Task 8 Step 1 in a terminal (commands in the Pi trial report),\n  then a sudo-capable session runs Steps 2–8. Or accept BLOCKED.\n- Gate D (verification before completion) after those.\n\n## Open questions\n- **Roster:** 7 owned skills are `\"off\"` in `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides` but\n  published to Codex and Pi: ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review,\n  pp-espn, session-miner. Re-enable them in Claude Code, or retire them from canonical.\n  Flagged by Codex in every review round since Gate B.\n\n## Gotchas\n- Never commit a symlink into `~/.claude/skills/`. Windows pulls that repo and an absolute\n  Mac symlink arrives unusable. A pre-commit hook refuses it.\n- Hooks and sync scripts exist in two copies (`~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/`; `.sh`\n  and `.ps1`). Any change patches both.\n- Never run `graphify install --platform agents`: the views link into canonical, so it\n  overwrites the Claude variant. Use `--platform claude` only.\n- `never_used` in the metrics is **Claude Code evidence only**. Check `~/.codex/sessions`\n  before recommending any deletion.\n- `claude -p --disallowedTools Bash` does not block the context-mode MCP shell tools.\n- A concurrent `closeout` commits whatever is uncommitted. Commit at each verified step.\n- `dcg` blocks: `rm -rf` in heredocs, `mv` and `>` redirects on home paths, `git` inside\n  command substitution. Use the Write tool plus a Python file that does the I/O.\n- Never point Pi at `~/DEV` — it ships no sandbox and no approval prompts, by design.\n- Never let any harness near `DexaProject` (identifiable athlete health data, on Google\n  Drive, not in `~/DEV`).\n- Plugin skills (`superpowers`, `mattpocock-skills`) are vendored and out of scope.\n- On the Mac: `timeout` is not installed and Python is PEP 668-managed (stdlib `python3`\n  or `uv`, never global `pip install`).\n- No success claim without pasted command output.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":29,"oldLines":19,"newStart":29,"newLines":16,"lines":[" - `portability_failures=7`: the open roster decision below. Every other invariant is 0."," "," ## Next","-- **Eric decides the roster** (see Open questions). Then re-run","-  `python3 scripts/skill-portability-check.py` — it should reach 0 failing.","-- **Eric runs \"audit my AI OS\"** interactively in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`. The Task 6 smoke","-  test was headless and wrote no report, so the full audit flow is unverified.","-- **Task 8:** run plan Task 8 Step 1 in a terminal (commands in the Pi trial report),","-  then a sudo-capable session runs Steps 2–8. Or accept BLOCKED.","-- Gate D (verification before completion) after those.","+- **Audit build 1:** sync the Codex snapshot hook (`~/.codex/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js`","+  is a stale 31-line copy) and fix the \"Windows retired\" rule in `memory-write` and","+  `project_backup-sync-system.md`.","+- **Audit build 2:** Eric confirms where GPS sessions land since 2026-08-24.","+- Other audit proposals (vault note rot, double `dcg` registration, stale router counts,","+  `measure.sh` sort bug): see `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`.","+- **Task 8 (Pi trial):** paused by Eric."," "," ## Open questions","-- **Roster:** 7 owned skills are `\"off\"` in `~/.claude/settings.json` `skillOverrides` but","-  published to Codex and Pi: ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review,","-  pp-espn, session-miner. Re-enable them in Claude Code, or retire them from canonical.","-  Flagged by Codex in every review round since Gate B.","+- Where do GPS sessions land now: `DataBase_GPS_Reporting` or `Catapult_API`?"," "," ## Gotchas"," - Never commit a symlink into `~/.claude/skills/`. Windows pulls that repo and an absolute"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3c844251-17a0-46d2-8879-67232d6b7ac4","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"72cdf012-2cea-4f22-9f69-8cdfb3eb8d53","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezyiNenPfoUahUVgJebS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KdHjcPdhWpnaiATHx9tzqb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/9823c1f0/tmp/gateC3-feedback.md","content":"# Final verification — scope and host dispositions (2026-09-13)\n\nEric asked for Codex to verify all of this session's work. Earlier rounds already covered\n`767b3de..dae7aeb` (Gate C rounds 1 and 2). **Do not re-review C-01, C-02 or C-03** — round 2\nfound no defect in them. This inspection covers `dae7aeb..HEAD` in KeystoneOS plus one commit\noutside this repo.\n\n## In scope\n\n1. **`2bcdda2` — IR-01 fix** (`scripts/skill-portability-check.py`). `value_kind()` reads the YAML node\n   kind of `name` and `description` before content checks; a sequence or mapping (flow or block,\n   any indent) is reported once and not content-checked. Host evidence: 24/24 fixtures; value kinds\n   and syntax verdicts agree with PyYAML on all 42 real skills; red-green: the pre-fix checker passes\n   4 wrong-type fixtures, the fixed one flags all 4, a plain-string control passes both. Evidence\n   scripts: `docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/`. **Not yet independently inspected.**\n2. **Docs and evidence** — `f58187c`, `6c9faf1`, `41c3a79` and the audit commit: execution log\n   (`docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md`), `docs/STATUS.md`, `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pi-trial.md`,\n   the evidence folder. Check that claims match the code and git history.\n3. **`~/.claude` commit `21c686d` (outside this repo; read `~/.claude/settings.json` directly).**\n   Roster Option B, chosen by Eric: the 7 lines `\"ArXiv\"`, `\"ISA\"`, `\"Science\"`, `\"capture-insight\"`,\n   `\"library-review\"`, `\"pp-espn\"`, `\"session-miner\"`: `\"off\"` were removed from `skillOverrides`\n   (absent = on). Host evidence: 99 → 92 overrides, all other settings compared identical after\n   JSON parse; `settings.local.json` has no `skillOverrides`; checker `42 checked, 0 failing`, exit 0.\n4. **First `aios-audit` run** — `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`, `docs/rot.md` (copy of\n   `~/.claude/rot.md`, `Last audited` column stamped). Check against the `aios-audit` SKILL.md contract\n   and the `rot.md` receipt rule: were only allowed files written, is every stamped date backed by a\n   check that ran, are partial scopes labelled, are there exactly two proposed builds, and does the\n   report avoid claiming more than the delegates checked. The audit's findings about other systems\n   (hooks, GPS, vault) are reported, not fixed, by design.\n\n## Known, not defects\n\n- Task 8 (Pi trial) is paused by Eric.\n- The C-02 recovery-lock residual risk was accepted in round 2.\n- `aios-audit` was executed by hand from a `~/DEV`-rooted session because the project skill is not\n  listed there; its trigger was verified headlessly on 2026-09-12.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9745,"cache_read_input_tokens":321161,"output_tokens":2496,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":295},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9745,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":2496,"cache_read_input_tokens":321161,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9745,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9745},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CezyiMFgt4cwMZs5ZCqpu","type":"assistant","uuid":"af610238-735d-4210-b883-5c9d46ba90e1","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:39:01.811Z","advisorModel":"claude-fabl