e exempt from low-use\npressure. Judge them in season.\n\n## Delegation contract (R2-09)\n\nA delegate is invoked **read-only**, for a **named scope**, and its receipt is\nwritten **only** for the scope it actually covered.\n\n1. **Read-only.** Before invoking a delegate, instruct it explicitly: report\n   findings, apply nothing, write no ledger, create no files. Several delegates\n   (`improve-system` among them) begin by applying previously approved proposals\n   — that must be suppressed. `aios-audit` writes only its own report and the\n   `Last audited` column.\n2. **Scope must be verified, not assumed.** A delegate's actual coverage is what\n   its body scans, not what this table wishes it scanned. `improve-system` scans\n   `~/SecondBrain/` — Notes, Knowledge, Projects. It does **not** touch\n   `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/` or `global-memory/`. Those are audited by\n   `aios-audit` directly.\n3. **A receipt covers only what was checked.** If a delegate returns findings for\n   a narrower scope than its row claims, write the date **and** a scope note, or\n   leave the row `unknown`. Never stamp a date because a delegate exited cleanly.\n\n## Layout invariants the audit must assert\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/` is canonical, is a git repo, and contains **no TRACKED symlinks**\n  (`git ls-files -s` shows no mode 120000). On-disk links to third-party skills are\n  expected; they are listed in the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` (never the tracked\n  `.gitignore`), and a pre-commit hook refuses to commit one. What must never happen is\n  committing a link, because Windows pulls this repo and a Mac link is dead there.\n- `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are **generated views**. Each carries\n  a `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` manifest. Every entry **in the manifest** must be\n  a symlink on Mac (a copy on Windows); wrong representation is drift.\n- Entries **not** in the manifest are third-party installs (`npx skills add`).\n  They are counted and reported, **never** flagged as errors and never pruned.\n- Support directories (`_shared/`) have no SKILL.md and must never be pruned.\n\n## Direction of travel\n\n**Fewer skills, stricter rules.** Skills get deleted; rules get sharpened.\n\n## Cadence\n\nMonthly metrics: launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit`, day 1 at 14:00.\nIt writes a trend row and a nudge. It does not commit and does not push.\nThe agentic audit is run by hand: \"audit my AI OS\" in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":7,"newStart":13,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Skills | `~/.claude/skills/` | fast | 1 month | 2026-09-12 | aios-audit | `skill-portability-check.py` + never-used list + the crutch test below. |"," | Agents | `~/.claude/agents/` | fast | 1 month | 2026-09-13 | aios-audit | Count `*.md`. Currently **0 exist** — report \"no agents defined\" and skip until one does. |"," | Rules | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` behaviour rules, output styles | fastest | 1 week | 2026-09-13 (Claude transcripts only; Codex sessions not checked) | aios-audit | Diff CLAUDE.md against the last 7 days of sessions: any rule contradicted by what actually happened, and any correction the user repeated twice that is not yet a rule. |","-| Hooks | `~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/` | slow | 6 months | unknown | claude-stack-doctor | Delegate. Also diff the two copies — they must match (`hook-two-copies-trap`). |","+| Hooks | `~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/` | slow | 6 months | 2026-09-13 (Mac only; stack-check.ps1 not run) | claude-stack-doctor | Delegate. Also diff the two copies — they must match (`hook-two-copies-trap`). |"," | Memory (agent) | `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/`, `global-memory/` | medium | 1 month | unknown | **aios-audit itself** | Audited directly — see the delegation contract below. `improve-system` does NOT cover these stores. Check: every `MEMORY.md` index line resolves to a file; every memory file appears in its index; `global-memory/MEMORY.md` is under its 2,500-char cap; flag time-dimensioned facts (counters, \"still open\", past-tense futures). |"," | Memory (vault notes) | `~/SecondBrain/` notes | medium | 1 month | unknown | improve-system | Delegate — but read-only, per the contract below. |"," | Data feeds | Fireflies, GPS, CFBD, Zotero | varies | 1 week | unknown | os-audit | Delegate to `os-audit` Check 3 (freshness). |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"858858c7-34a9-483c-8dbe-e7567edfc9f7","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"fcaa304a-0d54-4a2b-a61d-53a3c735e16e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezykYtVEPUWXB3sKdDSv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01957bzgf4cu6DLc1QmcsK7h","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/rot.md","old_string":"| Memory (agent) | `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/`, `global-memory/` | medium | 1 month | unknown |","new_string":"| Memory (agent) | `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/`, `global-memory/` | medium | 1 month | 2026-09-13 (time-dimensioned scan: DEV slug + global only) |"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2794,"cache_read_input_tokens":330906,"output_tokens":2533,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":366},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2794,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":2533,"cache_read_input_tokens":330906,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2794},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":6,"requestId":"req_011CezykXV9gsYhKC7QRYtBG","type":"assistant","uuid":"8f774073-5b52-4664-98b0-eb9cc006ae79","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:39:19.564Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8f774073-5b52-4664-98b0-eb9cc006ae79","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d7908bed-a694-4873-b058-61f2cd834cd8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01957bzgf4cu6DLc1QmcsK7h","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/.claude/rot.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"59c6b7b8-c566-4523-bd1a-6ddf3ed6b5d8","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:39:21.170Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/rot.md","oldString":"| Memory (agent) | `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/`, `global-memory/` | medium | 1 month | unknown |","newString":"| Memory (agent) | `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/`, `global-memory/` | medium | 1 month | 2026-09-13 (time-dimensioned scan: DEV slug + global only) |","originalFile":"# rot.md — how fast each AIOS layer goes stale\n\nAudit each layer on its own clock, not all at once. `aios-audit` reads this\nfile: any layer past due, or marked `unknown`, is a finding.\n\n**A date here is a receipt, not an intention.** Write one only after that\nlayer's check in the last column has actually run and produced output.\n\n| Layer | Where it lives | Rots | Audit every | Last audited | Owner | Concrete check |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Identity | `global-memory/USER.md` | very slow | 3 months | 2026-09-13 (partial: 7 days of sessions + memsearch, not 90 days) | memory-write | Read USER.md; flag any role, family, or career fact contradicted by the last 90 days of sessions. |\n| Substrate | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `~/DEV/*.md` routers | slow | 3 months | 2026-09-13 (router paths only; project CLAUDE.md internals not checked) | os-audit | Delegate to `os-audit` Check 1 (routing integrity). |\n| Skills | `~/.claude/skills/` | fast | 1 month | 2026-09-12 | aios-audit | `skill-portability-check.py` + never-used list + the crutch test below. |\n| Agents | `~/.claude/agents/` | fast | 1 month | 2026-09-13 | aios-audit | Count `*.md`. Currently **0 exist** — report \"no agents defined\" and skip until one does. |\n| Rules | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` behaviour rules, output styles | fastest | 1 week | 2026-09-13 (Claude transcripts only; Codex sessions not checked) | aios-audit | Diff CLAUDE.md against the last 7 days of sessions: any rule contradicted by what actually happened, and any correction the user repeated twice that is not yet a rule. |\n| Hooks | `~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/` | slow | 6 months | 2026-09-13 (Mac only; stack-check.ps1 not run) | claude-stack-doctor | Delegate. Also diff the two copies — they must match (`hook-two-copies-trap`). |\n| Memory (agent) | `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/`, `global-memory/` | medium | 1 month | unknown | **aios-audit itself** | Audited directly — see the delegation contract below. `improve-system` does NOT cover these stores. Check: every `MEMORY.md` index line resolves to a file; every memory file appears in its index; `global-memory/MEMORY.md` is under its 2,500-char cap; flag time-dimensioned facts (counters, \"still open\", past-tense futures). |\n| Memory (vault notes) | `~/SecondBrain/` notes | medium | 1 month | unknown | improve-system | Delegate — but read-only, per the contract below. |\n| Data feeds | Fireflies, GPS, CFBD, Zotero | varies | 1 week | unknown | os-audit | Delegate to `os-audit` Check 3 (freshness). |\n| Vault | `~/SecondBrain/` | medium | 1 month | unknown | brain-audit | Delegate to `brain-audit` (four C's score). |\n| Context posture | workspace-wide | medium | 3 months | unknown | doctor-plus | Delegate to `doctor-plus`. |\n\n## The question that governs a skill's fate\n\nNot \"how often did I run it?\" but **\"would the current model do this fine\nwithout the skill?\"** If yes, the skill is a crutch that now limits the model.\nDelete it. Keep only skills carrying tacit knowledge the model cannot know:\nforce-plate thresholds, GPS conventions, Baylor reporting norms, Eric's own\nroutines.\n\nSeasonal skills (`forecast-capture`, `ingest-book`) are exempt from low-use\npressure. Judge them in season.\n\n## Delegation contract (R2-09)\n\nA delegate is invoked **read-only**, for a **named scope**, and its receipt is\nwritten **only** for the scope it actually covered.\n\n1. **Read-only.** Before invoking a delegate, instruct it explicitly: report\n   findings, apply nothing, write no ledger, create no files. Several delegates\n   (`improve-system` among them) begin by applying previously approved proposals\n   — that must be suppressed. `aios-audit` writes only its own report and the\n   `Last audited` column.\n2. **Scope must be verified, not assumed.** A delegate's actual coverage is what\n   its body scans, not what this table wishes it scanned. `improve-system` scans\n   `~/SecondBrain/` — Notes, Knowledge, Projects. It does **not** touch\n   `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/` or `global-memory/`. Those are audited by\n   `aios-audit` directly.\n3. **A receipt covers only what was checked.** If a delegate returns findings for\n   a narrower scope than its row claims, write the date **and** a scope note, or\n   leave the row `unknown`. Never stamp a date because a delegate exited cleanly.\n\n## Layout invariants the audit must assert\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/` is canonical, is a git repo, and contains **no TRACKED symlinks**\n  (`git ls-files -s` shows no mode 120000). On-disk links to third-party skills are\n  expected; they are listed in the per-machine `.git/info/exclude` (never the tracked\n  `.gitignore`), and a pre-commit hook refuses to commit one. What must never happen is\n  committing a link, because Windows pulls this repo and a Mac link is dead there.\n- `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are **generated views**. Each carries\n  a `.generated-by-sync-to-codex` manifest. Every entry **in the manifest** must be\n  a symlink on Mac (a copy on Windows); wrong representation is drift.\n- Entries **not** in the manifest are third-party installs (`npx skills add`).\n  They are counted and reported, **never** flagged as errors and never pruned.\n- Support directories (`_shared/`) have no SKILL.md and must never be pruned.\n\n## Direction of travel\n\n**Fewer skills, stricter rules.** Skills get deleted; rules get sharpened.\n\n## Cadence\n\nMonthly metrics: launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit`, day 1 at 14:00.\nIt writes a trend row and a nudge. It does not commit and does not push.\nThe agentic audit is run by hand: \"audit my AI OS\" in `~/DEV/KeystoneOS`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":7,"newStart":14,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Agents | `~/.claude/agents/` | fast | 1 month | 2026-09-13 | aios-audit | Count `*.md`. Currently **0 exist** — report \"no agents defined\" and skip until one does. |"," | Rules | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` behaviour rules, output styles | fastest | 1 week | 2026-09-13 (Claude transcripts only; Codex sessions not checked) | aios-audit | Diff CLAUDE.md against the last 7 days of sessions: any rule contradicted by what actually happened, and any correction the user repeated twice that is not yet a rule. |"," | Hooks | `~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/` | slow | 6 months | 2026-09-13 (Mac only; stack-check.ps1 not run) | claude-stack-doctor | Delegate. Also diff the two copies — they must match (`hook-two-copies-trap`). |","-| Memory (agent) | `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/`, `global-memory/` | medium | 1 month | unknown | **aios-audit itself** | Audited directly — see the delegation contract below. `improve-system` does NOT cover these stores. Check: every `MEMORY.md` index line resolves to a file; every memory file appears in its index; `global-memory/MEMORY.md` is under its 2,500-char cap; flag time-dimensioned facts (counters, \"still open\", past-tense futures). |","+| Memory (agent) | `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/`, `global-memory/` | medium | 1 month | 2026-09-13 (time-dimensioned scan: DEV slug + global only) | **aios-audit itself** | Audited directly — see the delegation contract below. `improve-system` does NOT cover these stores. Check: every `MEMORY.md` index line resolves to a file; every memory file appears in its index; `global-memory/MEMORY.md` is under its 2,500-char cap; flag time-dimensioned facts (counters, \"still open\", past-tense futures). |"," | Memory (vault notes) | `~/SecondBrain/` notes | medium | 1 month | unknown | improve-system | Delegate — but read-only, per the contract below. |"," | Data feeds | Fireflies, GPS, CFBD, Zotero | varies | 1 week | unknown | os-audit | Delegate to `os-audit` Check 3 (freshness). |"," | Vault | `~/SecondBrain/` | medium | 1 month | unknown | brain-audit | Delegate to `brain-audit` (four C's score). |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8f774073-5b52-4664-98b0-eb9cc006ae79","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
