{"parentUuid":"05fa5c76-1c2e-4014-8cbf-8b594a48157f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezywW1A5XK4a1PeHNuU5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UfSBJ1oGm9y43AG8RogYqL","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md","old_string":"- `portability_failures=7`: the open roster decision below. Every other invariant is 0.","new_string":"- `portability_failures=0` since the roster decision (2026-09-13). Every layout invariant is 0."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1477,"cache_read_input_tokens":339083,"output_tokens":9909,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2832},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1477,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":9909,"cache_read_input_tokens":339083,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1477,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1477},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CezywUrwhHwswCuYx5Mcv","type":"assistant","uuid":"e4362b95-5ed5-4671-9599-cd9de39315e0","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:42:29.415Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"e4362b95-5ed5-4671-9599-cd9de39315e0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"44efd2f3-3273-4dc9-8348-229d2b07e4a6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UfSBJ1oGm9y43AG8RogYqL","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"abba5c79-3258-4137-92d9-470e2d2a1de5","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:42:29.561Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md","oldString":"- `portability_failures=7`: the open roster decision below. Every other invariant is 0.","newString":"- `portability_failures=0` since the roster decision (2026-09-13). Every layout invariant is 0.","originalFile":"# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\nLast updated 2026-09-13 (Mac, background session). Evidence for every claim below is in\n`docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md`.\n\n## Current state\n- The dominant thread is the **harness-agnostic AIOS plan**:\n  `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md` (approved; do not edit —\n  its SHA-256 `71b5242e…` binds the approval). Goal: every skill Eric owns loads\n  identically in Claude Code, Codex and Pi from one versioned canonical folder, plus a\n  recurring audit that keeps the AIOS from rotting.\n- Architecture: `~/.claude/skills/` (repo `erash11/claude-skills`) is canonical and holds\n  real directories only. `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are generated views\n  rebuilt per machine by `sync-to-codex.sh` / `.ps1` — symlinks on Mac, copies on Windows.\n- **Tasks 1–7 done.** Task 8 (Pi trial) **PAUSED by Eric** (2026-09-13). It also needs\n  `sudo` to create `piuser`. Report and unblock commands: `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pi-trial.md`.\n- **Roster resolved 2026-09-13 (Option B):** the 7 owned skills are on again in Claude Code\n  (`~/.claude` commit `21c686d`). Checker: 42/42 portable.\n- **First `aios-audit` ran 2026-09-13:** `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`. Two RED:\n  the Codex snapshot hook is a stale copy, and the GPS feed looks frozen since 2026-08-01.\n- **Gate B** (2 rounds) and **Gate C** (2 rounds) run. Every code finding is fixed:\n  C-01 exec bits, C-02 atomic stale-lock reclaim, C-03 usage metrics scoped to Claude\n  transcripts, IR-01 checker rejects list/map descriptions. IR-01 is host-tested but\n  not re-inspected by Codex.\n- Monthly metrics run on launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit` (day 1, 14:00). It writes a row\n  to `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` and a nudge; it never commits.\n- `portability_failures=7`: the open roster decision below. Every other invariant is 0.\n\n## Next\n- **Audit build 1:** sync the Codex snapshot hook (`~/.codex/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js`\n  is a stale 31-line copy) and fix the \"Windows retired\" rule in `memory-write` and\n  `project_backup-sync-system.md`.\n- **Audit build 2:** Eric confirms where GPS sessions land since 2026-08-24.\n- Other audit proposals (vault note rot, double `dcg` registration, stale router counts,\n  `measure.sh` sort bug): see `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`.\n- **Task 8 (Pi trial):** paused by Eric.\n\n## Open questions\n- Where do GPS sessions land now: `DataBase_GPS_Reporting` or `Catapult_API`?\n\n## Gotchas\n- Never commit a symlink into `~/.claude/skills/`. Windows pulls that repo and an absolute\n  Mac symlink arrives unusable. A pre-commit hook refuses it.\n- Hooks and sync scripts exist in two copies (`~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/`; `.sh`\n  and `.ps1`). Any change patches both.\n- Never run `graphify install --platform agents`: the views link into canonical, so it\n  overwrites the Claude variant. Use `--platform claude` only.\n- `never_used` in the metrics is **Claude Code evidence only**. Check `~/.codex/sessions`\n  before recommending any deletion.\n- `claude -p --disallowedTools Bash` does not block the context-mode MCP shell tools.\n- A concurrent `closeout` commits whatever is uncommitted. Commit at each verified step.\n- `dcg` blocks: `rm -rf` in heredocs, `mv` and `>` redirects on home paths, `git` inside\n  command substitution. Use the Write tool plus a Python file that does the I/O.\n- Never point Pi at `~/DEV` — it ships no sandbox and no approval prompts, by design.\n- Never let any harness near `DexaProject` (identifiable athlete health data, on Google\n  Drive, not in `~/DEV`).\n- Plugin skills (`superpowers`, `mattpocock-skills`) are vendored and out of scope.\n- On the Mac: `timeout` is not installed and Python is PEP 668-managed (stdlib `python3`\n  or `uv`, never global `pip install`).\n- No success claim without pasted command output.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":26,"oldLines":7,"newStart":26,"newLines":7,"lines":["   not re-inspected by Codex."," - Monthly metrics run on launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit` (day 1, 14:00). It writes a row","   to `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` and a nudge; it never commits.","-- `portability_failures=7`: the open roster decision below. Every other invariant is 0.","+- `portability_failures=0` since the roster decision (2026-09-13). Every layout invariant is 0."," "," ## Next"," - **Audit build 1:** sync the Codex snapshot hook (`~/.codex/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js`"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e4362b95-5ed5-4671-9599-cd9de39315e0","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"abba5c79-3258-4137-92d9-470e2d2a1de5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezywW1A5XK4a1PeHNuU5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rv45RbWuak2EEK7brwMy1T","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t5g-checker-test.py","content":"\"\"\"IR-03 checker tests: name/description must be YAML STRINGS - not lists/maps (IR-01)\nand not implicit null/boolean/number/timestamp scalars (IR-03). Re-runs every t5f\nfixture in fresh folders (old fixture dirs cannot be deleted), cross-checks value_kind\nagainst PyYAML, and red-greens against the pre-IR-03 checker (2bcdda2).\nRun with: uv run --no-project --with pyyaml python t5g-checker-test.py\"\"\"\nimport os, subprocess, glob, importlib.util, yaml, stat, types, datetime\n\nT = \"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp\"\nK = \"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS\"\nCHK = f\"{K}/scripts/skill-portability-check.py\"\nGOOD_DESC = \"Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\"\n\ndef run(home=None):\n    env = dict(os.environ)\n    if home:\n        env[\"HOME\"] = home\n    return subprocess.run([\"python3\", CHK], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env)\n\ndef skill(root, name, fm_lines):\n    os.makedirs(f\"{root}/.claude/skills/{name}\")\n    open(f\"{root}/.claude/skills/{name}/SKILL.md\", \"w\").write(\"---\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(fm_lines) + \"\\n---\\nbody\\n\")\n\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"chk\", CHK)\nchk = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nspec.loader.exec_module(chk)\nold = types.ModuleType(\"old\")\nexec(compile(subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", K, \"show\", \"2bcdda2:scripts/skill-portability-check.py\"],\n                            capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout, \"old\", \"exec\"), old.__dict__)\n\n# dir name -> (frontmatter lines, expect_flagged, loader_should_accept)\nFX = {\n    # --- carried from t5e/t5f ---\n    \"dq-bad-escape\":    ([\"name: dq-bad-escape\", 'description: \"Use when testing. Do not use otherwise. \\\\q\"'], True, False),\n    \"dq-good-escapes\":  ([\"name: dq-good-escapes\", 'description: \"Use when \\\\\"x\\\\\" \\\\x41 \\\\u00e9. Do not use otherwise.\"'], False, True),\n    \"dq-unclosed\":      ([\"name: dq-unclosed\", 'description: \"Use when testing.', '  Do not use otherwise.\"'], True, None),\n    \"dq-trailing-text\": ([\"name: dq-trailing-text\", 'description: \"Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\" extra'], True, False),\n    \"sq-good-doubled\":  ([\"name: sq-good-doubled\", \"description: 'Use when it''s testing. Do not use otherwise.'\"], False, True),\n    \"sq-unclosed\":      ([\"name: sq-unclosed\", \"description: 'Use when testing. Do not use otherwise.\"], True, False),\n    \"flow-map\":         ([\"name: flow-map\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\", \"metadata: {a: b}\"], True, None),\n    \"flow-seq-good\":    ([\"name: flow-seq-good\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\", \"metadata:\", \"  bins: [one, two-cli]\"], False, True),\n    \"flow-seq-nested\":  ([\"name: flow-seq-nested\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\", \"metadata:\", \"  bins: [[one], two]\"], True, None),\n    \"tag\":              ([\"name: tag\", f\"description: !!str {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, None),\n    \"anchor\":           ([\"name: anchor\", f\"description: &d {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, None),\n    \"tab-indent\":       ([\"name: tab-indent\", \"description: >-\", f\"\\t{GOOD_DESC}\"], True, False),\n    \"nested-colon\":     ([\"name: nested-colon\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\", \"metadata:\", \"  short-description: bad: value\"], True, False),\n    \"block-good\":       ([\"name: block-good\", \"description: >-\", \"  Use when testing: a # b. Do not use otherwise.\"], False, True),\n    \"list-items-good\":  ([\"name: list-items-good\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\", \"metadata:\", \"  install:\", \"    - kind: go\", \"      module: github.com/x/y\"], False, True),\n    \"top-junk\":         ([\"name: top-junk\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\", \"just words\"], True, False),\n    \"desc-flow-seq\":    ([\"name: desc-flow-seq\", f\"description: [{GOOD_DESC}]\"], True, True),\n    \"desc-block-seq\":   ([\"name: desc-block-seq\", \"description:\", f\"  - {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),\n    \"desc-block-seq0\":  ([\"name: desc-block-seq0\", \"description:\", f\"- {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),\n    \"desc-block-map\":   ([\"name: desc-block-map\", \"description:\", f\"  when: {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),\n    \"desc-flow-map\":    ([\"name: desc-flow-map\", \"description: {when: yes}\"], True, True),\n    \"name-flow-seq\":    ([\"name: [name-flow-seq]\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),\n    \"desc-plain-multi\": ([\"name: desc-plain-multi\", \"description:\", \"  Use when testing.\", \"  Do not use otherwise.\"], False, True),\n    \"desc-folded-then-key\": ([\"name: desc-folded-then-key\", \"description: >-\", f\"  {GOOD_DESC}\", \"metadata:\", \"  a: b\"], False, True),\n    # --- new for IR-03: implicit non-string scalars (dir name == value, so only the TYPE is wrong) ---\n    \"true\":             ([\"name: true\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),\n    \"null\":             ([\"name: null\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),\n    \"123\":              ([\"name: 123\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),\n    \"1.5\":              ([\"name: 1.5\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),\n    \"2026-09-13\":       ([\"name: 2026-09-13\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),\n    \"Off\":              ([\"name: Off\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"], True, True),\n    \"desc-bool\":        ([\"name: desc-bool\", \"description: yes\"], True, True),\n    \"desc-number\":      ([\"name: desc-number\", \"description: 42\"], True, True),\n    \"desc-null-multi\":  ([\"name: desc-null-multi\", \"description:\", \"  ~\"], True, True),\n    # --- controls: quoted forms and look-alike strings are strings ---\n    \"yes\":              (['name: \"yes\"', f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"], False, True),\n    \"404\":              ([\"name: '404'\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"], False, True),\n    \"true-thing\":       ([\"name: true-thing\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"], False, True),\n    \"v1.2.3\":           ([\"name: v1.2.3\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"], False, True),\n}\nIR03 = [\"true\", \"null\", \"123\", \"1.5\", \"2026-09-13\", \"Off\", \"desc-bool\", \"desc-number\", \"desc-null-multi\"]\n\ndef loader_kind(v):\n    if isinstance(v, list): return \"sequence\"\n    if isinstance(v, dict): return \"mapping\"\n    if v is None: return \"null\"\n    if isinstance(v, bool): return \"boolean\"\n    if isinstance(v, (int, float)): return \"number\"\n    if isinstance(v, (datetime.date, datetime.datetime)): return \"timestamp\"\n    return \"scalar\"\n\nH = f\"{T}/t5g-fx\"\nfor n, (lines, _, _) in FX.items():\n    skill(H, n, lines)\nr = run(H)\nprint(\"FIXTURES exit\", r.returncode, \"|\", r.stdout.strip().splitlines()[-1])\nfailing, reasons, cur = set(), {}, None\nfor l in r.stdout.splitlines():\n    if l.startswith(\"FAIL \"):\n        cur = l[5:]; failing.add(cur); reasons[cur] = []\n    elif cur and l.strip().startswith(\"- \"):\n        reasons[cur].append(l.strip()[2:])\nbad = []\nfor n, (lines, expect_flag, loader_ok) in FX.items():\n    flagged = n in failing\n    try:\n        doc = yaml.safe_load(\"\\n\".join(lines)); loads = True\n    except yaml.YAMLError:\n        doc, loads = None, False\n    note = \"\"\n    if loader_ok is not None and loads != loader_ok:\n        note = f\" (loader assumption wrong: loads={loads})\"\n    if loads and isinstance(doc, dict):\n        fm = \"\\n\".join(lines)\n        for k in (\"name\", \"description\"):\n            want, got = loader_kind(doc.get(k)), chk.value_kind(fm, k)\n            if got != want and not (want == \"null\" and got == \"empty\"):\n                note += f\" (value_kind {k}={got}, loader says {want})\"\n    status = \"PASS\" if flagged == expect_flag and not note else \"FAIL\"\n    if status == \"FAIL\":\n        bad.append(n)\n    first = (reasons.get(n) or [\"\"])[0][:70]\n    print(f\"  {status} {n}: flagged={flagged} expect={expect_flag} loads={loads}{note} | {first}\")\n\nprint(\"RED-GREEN (pre-IR-03 checker 2bcdda2 vs current) on the IR-03 fixtures:\")\nrg_ok = True\nfor n in IR03:\n    p = f\"{H}/.claude/skills/{n}/SKILL.md\"\n    o, c = bool(old.check(p)[1]), bool(chk.check(p)[1])\n    # desc-bool/desc-number were already flagged by the old checker (no clauses); the\n    # red-green claim is about the TYPE message, so check that too.\n    typed = any(\"not a string\" in x for x in chk.check(p)[1])\n    print(f\"  {n:16} old_flagged={o!s:5} new_flagged={c!s:5} type_reported={typed}\")\n    rg_ok &= c and typed\nprint(\"  red-green:\", \"PASS\" if rg_ok else \"FAIL\")\n\ndis, kind_dis = [], []\nreal = [p for p in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.expanduser(\"~/.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md\")))\n        if not os.path.islink(os.path.dirname(p))]\nfor p in real:\n    fm = chk.frontmatter(open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\").read())\n    flagged = bool(chk.syntax_problems(fm))\n    try:\n        doc = yaml.safe_load(fm); loads = True\n    except yaml.YAMLError:\n        doc, loads = None, False\n    if flagged == loads:\n        dis.append((p.split(\"/\")[-2], chk.syntax_problems(fm)[:1], loads))\n    if loads:\n        for k in (\"name\", \"description\"):\n            want, got = loader_kind(doc.get(k)), chk.value_kind(fm, k)\n            if got != want:\n                kind_dis.append((p.split(\"/\")[-2], k, got, want))\nprint(\"REAL roster files:\", len(real), \"syntax disagreements:\", dis, \"kind disagreements:\", kind_dis)\nr = run()\nprint(\"REAL checker exit\", r.returncode, \"|\", r.stdout.strip().splitlines()[-1])\n\ndef evidence_home(tag):\n    h = f\"{T}/t5g-ev-{tag}\"\n    skill(h, \"ok\", [\"name: ok\", f\"description: {GOOD_DESC}\"])\n    return h\nh = evidence_home(\"badjson\"); open(f\"{h}/.claude/settings.json\", \"w\").write(\"{not json\")\nprint(\"malformed settings.json -> exit\", run(h).returncode, \"(expect 2)\")\nh = evidence_home(\"nonobject\"); open(f\"{h}/.claude/settings.json\", \"w\").write('{\"skillOverrides\": [\"x\"]}')\nprint(\"skillOverrides not an object -> exit\", run(h).returncode, \"(expect 2)\")\nh = evidence_home(\"unreadable\"); open(f\"{h}/.claude/settings.json\", \"w\").write(\"{}\")\nos.chmod(f\"{h}/.claude/settings.json\", 0)\nprint(\"unreadable settings.json -> exit\", run(h).returncode, \"(expect 2)\")\nos.chmod(f\"{h}/.claude/settings.json\", stat.S_IRUSR | stat.S_IWUSR)\nh = evidence_home(\"brokengit\"); open(f\"{h}/.claude/skills/.git\", \"w\").write(\"gitdir: /nonexistent/repo\\n\")\nprint(\"git probe fails -> exit\", run(h).returncode, \"(expect 2)\")\nh = evidence_home(\"nosettings\")\nprint(\"no settings, no git (control) -> exit\", run(h).returncode, \"(expect 0)\")\nfor hh, exp in ((f\"{T}/t5-badcanon\", 1), (f\"{T}/t5-emptycanon\", 2), (f\"{T}/t5b-fx-yaml\", 1), (f\"{T}/t5b-fx-spell\", 1)):\n    print(os.path.basename(hh), \"exit\", run(hh).returncode, \"(expect\", exp, \")\")\nprint(\"FIXTURE FAILURES:\", bad or \"none\")\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1477,"cache_read_input_tokens":339083,"output_tokens":9909,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2832},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1477,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":9909,"cache_read_input_tokens":339083,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1477,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1477},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":nu