{"parentUuid":"c0b7dac2-eaab-4998-92e5-68b9bdf3d221","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"44efd2f3-3273-4dc9-8348-229d2b07e4a6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C5jE8kh6KvfF9DCANwGvfx","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"3df664a3-36c4-4433-971f-8703563fe18f","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:43:38.863Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/README.md","oldString":"| `ir01-redgreen.py` |","newString":"| `t5g-checker-test.py` | IR-03: implicit null/boolean/number/timestamp `name`/`description` rejected; all t5f fixtures; PyYAML agreement; red-green vs `2bcdda2` | Same as `t5f` (fresh `t5g-` prefix needed on a re-run) |\n| `gateC3-feedback.md` | What was sent to Codex for the final verification (round 3) | none |\n| `ir01-redgreen.py` |","originalFile":"# Gate C evidence — 2026-09-13\n\nCopies of the scripts behind the Gate C claims in\n`docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md`. The originals lived in job temp\nfolders that are deleted with the job. Kept so the evidence can be re-read and\nre-run.\n\n**These are records, not a test suite. Read before running.**\n\n| File | Proves | Side effects |\n|---|---|---|\n| `t7-failpaths.py` | Cron wrapper failure paths and C-02 lock race (9 probes) | Runs the REAL wrapper: appends rows to `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` and nudges to `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. Back both up first and restore after. |\n| `c03-probe.py` | C-03 unreadable-transcript count | Creates and removes one probe file under `~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/` |\n| `t5f-checker-test.py` | IR-01 and all earlier checker fixtures; PyYAML agreement | Needs `uv run --no-project --with pyyaml`. Builds fixtures under a hard-coded job temp path; fails if those folders already exist, so change `t5f-` to a fresh prefix first. Also expects the older fixture homes `t5-badcanon`, `t5-emptycanon`, `t5b-fx-*`. |\n| `ir01-redgreen.py` | Checker before `2bcdda2` passes list descriptions; after, flags them | Reads the `t5f-fx` fixtures; read-only |\n| `gateC-dispositions.md` | What was sent to Codex for Gate C round 2 | none |\n\nPaths inside the scripts are absolute and Mac-specific.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":6,"newStart":12,"newLines":8,"lines":[" | `t7-failpaths.py` | Cron wrapper failure paths and C-02 lock race (9 probes) | Runs the REAL wrapper: appends rows to `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` and nudges to `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. Back both up first and restore after. |"," | `c03-probe.py` | C-03 unreadable-transcript count | Creates and removes one probe file under `~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/` |"," | `t5f-checker-test.py` | IR-01 and all earlier checker fixtures; PyYAML agreement | Needs `uv run --no-project --with pyyaml`. Builds fixtures under a hard-coded job temp path; fails if those folders already exist, so change `t5f-` to a fresh prefix first. Also expects the older fixture homes `t5-badcanon`, `t5-emptycanon`, `t5b-fx-*`. |","+| `t5g-checker-test.py` | IR-03: implicit null/boolean/number/timestamp `name`/`description` rejected; all t5f fixtures; PyYAML agreement; red-green vs `2bcdda2` | Same as `t5f` (fresh `t5g-` prefix needed on a re-run) |","+| `gateC3-feedback.md` | What was sent to Codex for the final verification (round 3) | none |"," | `ir01-redgreen.py` | Checker before `2bcdda2` passes list descriptions; after, flags them | Reads the `t5f-fx` fixtures; read-only |"," | `gateC-dispositions.md` | What was sent to Codex for Gate C round 2 | none |"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c0b7dac2-eaab-4998-92e5-68b9bdf3d221","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userTyp