{"parentUuid":"3df664a3-36c4-4433-971f-8703563fe18f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cezz5swV5aUNJec9mEAxj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016CzjbevvBH6Z6SdWNfwvTP","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md","old_string":"## First `aios-audit` run (2026-09-13)","new_string":"## Final Codex verification — round 3 (2026-09-13)\n\n`gpt-5.6-terra`, effort high, base `dae7aeb` (IR-01 fix, docs, evidence, audit report, and\n`~/.claude` commit `21c686d`). Verdict **REVISE**. It confirmed `21c686d` removes exactly the 7\noverrides.\n\n| ID | Sev | Finding | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| IR-03 | medium | `value_kind()` called every plain value a string, so `name: true`, `null`, `123`, dates passed though a loader returns a non-string | Plain scalars resolved against the YAML 1.1 (PyYAML) and 1.2 core implicit types; null/boolean/number/timestamp reported as \"not a string\". Quoted and block scalars stay strings. |\n| DOC-01 | low | `STATUS.md` still said `portability_failures=7` and called the roster open | Line corrected to `0` |\n\nHost verification (`t5g-checker-test.py`): 37/37 fixtures; red-green vs `2bcdda2` — the old checker\npassed all 6 wrong-type `name` fixtures, the new one flags all 9 IR-03 fixtures with a type message;\nquoted `\"yes\"`, `'404'`, `true-thing`, `v1.2.3` still pass; value kinds agree with PyYAML on all 42\nreal skills; real roster 42/42; fail-closed 4/4 exit 2, control exit 0.\n\n## First `aios-audit` run (2026-09-13)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3040,"cache_read_input_tokens":350783,"output_tokens":3259,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":470},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"stand