{"parentUuid":"6f58ec7b-05f6-4298-8f1b-785d0c84ffb2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b4c0f99f-d416-4b0a-819d-31601dd3681d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MTeUAn29fyX1tCta25vNgZ","type":"tool_result","content":"copied","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b95e54b2-edd4-455f-8f26-2637acac5113","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:52:57.095Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"copied","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/gateC4-feedback.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":20,"lines":["+# Narrow re-check of the round-3 fixes (2026-09-13)","+","+Round 3 (`gpt-5.6-terra`, base `dae7aeb`) returned REVISE with IR-03 and DOC-01. This inspection","+covers **only the fix commit** on top of `5c98b06`. Everything before `5c98b06` was reviewed in","+rounds 1–3; do not re-review it.","+","+| ID | Disposition | What changed |","+|---|---|---|","+| IR-03 | ACCEPTED | `scripts/skill-portability-check.py`: `IMPLICIT` patterns (null, boolean, number, timestamp — union of the YAML 1.1 resolver PyYAML uses and the 1.2 core schema) and `_plain_kind()`. `value_kind()` resolves plain inline and multi-line plain scalars against them; quoted and `|`/`>` block scalars stay strings. `NOT_STRING` covers the new kinds, so a wrong-type `name`/`description` is reported once and not content-checked. `y`/`n` are deliberately not treated as booleans (PyYAML and the 1.2 core schema both read them as strings). |","+| DOC-01 | ACCEPTED | `docs/STATUS.md`: `portability_failures=0` since the roster decision. |","+","+Host verification (`docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/t5g-checker-test.py`): 37/37 fixtures;","+red-green vs `2bcdda2` — the old checker passed `name: true`, `null`, `123`, `1.5`, `2026-09-13`, `Off`,","+the new one flags them and `description: yes`, `42`, multi-line `~` with a type message; controls","+`\"yes\"`, `'404'`, `true-thing`, `v1.2.3` pass; value kinds agree with PyYAML on all 42 real skills;","+real roster 42/42; fail-closed 4/4 exit 2.","+","+Please look for: a string the new patterns wrongly call non-string (false positive on a real skill","+name/description shape), a non-string form still called a string, and any regression in the","+multi-line plain-scalar path."]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/gateC4-feedback.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6f58ec7b-05f6-4298-8f1b-785d0c84ffb2","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b95e54b2-edd4-455f-8f26-2637acac5113","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezzeY6K3nfnvj9fS6dZn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MdT3XpxW3jjMDecssCpNqu","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/9823c1f0/tmp/gateC5-feedback.md","content":"# Round 5 — narrow re-check of `62fbb72` only (2026-09-13)\n\nRound 4 (`gpt-5.6-terra`, base `5c98b06`) returned IR-04 and IR-05. This inspection covers **only\ncommit `62fbb72`** on top of `14b4a8f`. **Do not re-review anything before `14b4a8f`.** This is the\nlast round this session.\n\n## Dispositions\n\n| ID | Disposition | Detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| IR-04 | **SPLIT** | `0:1` — ACCEPTED and fixed: PyYAML's sexagesimal int needs a `1-9` lead, and YAML 1.2 core has no sexagesimal. `0008` / `0129` — **REJECTED**. Round 4 said \"YAML 1.2 core also does not resolve it as a number\". That is incorrect: YAML 1.2.2 §10.3.2 core schema int is `[-+]? [0-9]+`, leading zeros allowed. The checker's rule is \"non-string if EITHER family (PyYAML 1.1 or 1.2 core) resolves it to a non-string\", so `0008` is correctly flagged. |\n| IR-05 | ACCEPTED | Date-only timestamp now needs two-digit month and day; the one-digit form resolves only inside a date-time. `2026-9-3` is a string. |\n| host-found | fixed | `._1`-style values were flagged as floats. PyYAML's `.`-leading float is `\\.[0-9][0-9_]*…` (digit right after the dot). |\n\nThe number and timestamp patterns are now transcribed branch by branch from PyYAML's resolver and\nthe YAML 1.2.2 core schema.\n\n## Evidence (in `docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/`)\n\nReal YAML 1.2 loader — the `yaml` npm package bundled with Pi, loaded as a library (`t5h-jsyaml.cjs`):\n\n```\n0008               yaml-1.2-core=number    yaml-1.1=number\n0129               yaml-1.2-core=number    yaml-1.1=number\n0:1                yaml-1.2-core=scalar    yaml-1.1=number\n2026-9-3           yaml-1.2-core=scalar    yaml-1.1=timestamp\n1e3                yaml-1.2-core=number    yaml-1.1=number\n0o17               yaml-1.2-core=number    yaml-1.1=scalar\nv1.2.3             yaml-1.2-core=scalar    yaml-1.1=scalar\n```\n\nCorpus (`t5h-kind-corpus.py`): 38,454 plain scalars PyYAML accepts. 0 that PyYAML's resolver tags as a\nnon-string are called strings by the checker. 628 are called non-string beyond PyYAML; all 628 match\nan independently transcribed YAML 1.2 core regex (0 unjustified). Named: `0:1` and `2026-9-3` are now\nstrings. Regression: `t5g` fixtures unchanged (37 checked, 26 failing); real roster 42/42.\n\n## Please look for\n\nA plain scalar that NEITHER PyYAML nor YAML 1.2 core resolves to a non-string but the checker flags,\nor one that either resolves to a non-string but the checker calls a string.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2232,"cache_read_input_tokens":763787,"output_tokens":3491,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":691},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":103,"cache_read_input_tokens":381540,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707},"type":"message"},{"input_tokens":343857,"output_tokens":7858,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"advisor_message","model":"claude-fable-5-1"},{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3388,"cache_read_input_tokens":382247,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1525,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1525,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},