{"parentUuid":"82c1c902-961a-4af9-bb87-523709b3cba6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf112HijdNGck2gj7eCwS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Neither IR-06 nor IR-07 are actual defects—PyYAML correctly treats those values as text, and the \"timestamp/number\" readings came from the npm yaml library's 1.1 mode, which none of the harnesses use by default. Round 5 was marked \"failed\" only because I accidentally committed docs during review; I'll log this honestly, save the round-5 notes, and add a STATUS.md warning against committing during review before finishing up.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4011,"cache_read_input_tokens":392812,"output_tokens":2980,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1445},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4011,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":2980,"cache_read_input_tokens":392812,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4011},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cf112FdijdvrsduN5bvra","type":"assistant","uuid":"d87d2ee4-b7b7-4a20-82a9-c049b286a751","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:56:04.859Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d87d2ee4-b7b7-4a20-82a9-c049b286a751","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf112HijdNGck2gj7eCwS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QpaPZwt7bkE462X6uNp5uW","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md","old_string":"**Not re-inspected by Codex.** Four inspection rounds ran this session; a fifth waits on Eric.","new_string":"## Final Codex verification — round 5, narrow, last (2026-09-13)\n\n`gpt-5.6-terra`, effort high, base `14b4a8f` (commit `62fbb72` only). Verdict **REVISE**. The runner\nmarked the run `failed` — \"Code changed during inspection\" — because the host committed `34ab774`\n(docs only: `STATUS.md`, round-4 notes) while it ran. `scripts/skill-portability-check.py` did not\nchange, so the findings address the final checker. Host error, recorded here.\n\n| ID | Claim | Host check (PyYAML 6.0.3 resolver and Pi's `yaml` npm library, this Mac) | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| IR-06 | PyYAML resolves `2026-9-3` as a timestamp; the checker calls it a string | PyYAML → `str`; checker → string. Only the `yaml` npm library in its **1.1 mode** returns a timestamp. The round-5 notes' \"yaml-1.1=timestamp\" line came from that library, not PyYAML. | Not a defect under the stated contract (PyYAML + YAML 1.2 core). **Open for Eric** if the contract should also cover npm `yaml` 1.1 mode. |\n| IR-07 | PyYAML resolves `1_0e+3` as a float; the checker calls it a string | PyYAML → `str` (its exponent form needs a decimal point); checker → string. npm `yaml` 1.1 mode → number; 1.2 core → string. | Same as IR-06. |\n\nNo harness loads skills in YAML 1.1 mode by default (Claude Code and Pi use JS 1.2-core loaders;\nCodex a Rust 1.2 loader). Round 5 was the declared stop: no further fixes or rounds this session."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_seq