13 (Option B):** the 7 owned skills are on again in Claude Code\n  (`~/.claude` commit `21c686d`). Checker: 42/42 portable.\n- **First `aios-audit` ran 2026-09-13:** `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`. Two RED:\n  the Codex snapshot hook is a stale copy, and the GPS feed looks frozen since 2026-08-01.\n- **Gate B** (2 rounds), **Gate C** (2 rounds) and two final Codex verification rounds\n  (3 and 4, `gpt-5.6-terra`) ran on 2026-09-12/13. Every code finding is fixed: C-01 exec\n  bits, C-02 atomic stale-lock reclaim, C-03 usage metrics scoped to Claude transcripts,\n  IR-01 list/map names rejected, IR-03 implicit null/boolean/number/timestamp rejected,\n  IR-04/IR-05 exact YAML grammars (`0008` kept as a number on purpose: YAML 1.2 core).\n  Round 5 checks the last fix, `62fbb72`; see the audit log for its verdict.\n- Monthly metrics run on launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit` (day 1, 14:00). It writes a row\n  to `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` and a nudge; it never commits.\n- `portability_failures=0` since the roster decision (2026-09-13). Every layout invariant is 0.\n\n## Next\n- **Audit build 1:** sync the Codex snapshot hook (`~/.codex/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js`\n  is a stale 31-line copy) and fix the \"Windows retired\" rule in `memory-write` and\n  `project_backup-sync-system.md`.\n- **Audit build 2:** Eric confirms where GPS sessions land since 2026-08-24.\n- Other audit proposals (vault note rot, double `dcg` registration, stale router counts,\n  `measure.sh` sort bug): see `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`.\n- **Task 8 (Pi trial):** paused by Eric.\n\n## Open questions\n- Where do GPS sessions land now: `DataBase_GPS_Reporting` or `Catapult_API`?\n\n## Gotchas\n- Never commit a symlink into `~/.claude/skills/`. Windows pulls that repo and an absolute\n  Mac symlink arrives unusable. A pre-commit hook refuses it.\n- Hooks and sync scripts exist in two copies (`~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/`; `.sh`\n  and `.ps1`). Any change patches both.\n- Never run `graphify install --platform agents`: the views link into canonical, so it\n  overwrites the Claude variant. Use `--platform claude` only.\n- `never_used` in the metrics is **Claude Code evidence only**. Check `~/.codex/sessions`\n  before recommending any deletion.\n- `claude -p --disallowedTools Bash` does not block the context-mode MCP shell tools.\n- A concurrent `closeout` commits whatever is uncommitted. Commit at each verified step.\n- **Never commit to a repo while a `claudex-loop` inspection of it is running.** The runner\n  snapshots the tree and marks the run `failed` (\"Code changed during inspection\").\n  Happened in round 5 on 2026-09-13.\n- `dcg` blocks: `rm -rf` in heredocs, `mv` and `>` redirects on home paths, `git` inside\n  command substitution. Use the Write tool plus a Python file that does the I/O.\n- Never point Pi at `~/DEV` — it ships no sandbox and no approval prompts, by design.\n- Never let any harness near `DexaProject` (identifiable athlete health data, on Google\n  Drive, not in `~/DEV`).\n- Plugin skills (`superpowers`, `mattpocock-skills`) are vendored and out of scope.\n- On the Mac: `timeout` is not installed and Python is PEP 668-managed (stdlib `python3`\n  or `uv`, never global `pip install`).\n- No success claim without pasted command output.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":25,"oldLines":7,"newStart":25,"newLines":9,"lines":["   bits, C-02 atomic stale-lock reclaim, C-03 usage metrics scoped to Claude transcripts,","   IR-01 list/map names rejected, IR-03 implicit null/boolean/number/timestamp rejected,","   IR-04/IR-05 exact YAML grammars (`0008` kept as a number on purpose: YAML 1.2 core).","-  Round 5 checks the last fix, `62fbb72`; see the audit log for its verdict.","+  Round 5 (last) returned REVISE on `62fbb72` with IR-06/IR-07; host checks show both hold only","+  for the npm `yaml` library's 1.1 mode, not PyYAML or YAML 1.2 core. Open for Eric: widen the","+  contract, or accept."," - Monthly metrics run on launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit` (day 1, 14:00). It writes a row","   to `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` and a nudge; it never commits."," - `portability_failures=0` since the roster decision (2026-09-13). Every layout invariant is 0."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e3e2ae97-80b0-4af5-b101-6c9c946917dc","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
