{"parentUuid":"d0ceafd8-ae12-4530-a793-21243be6bf1e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf115zqbSMWvcvBtFmsDJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I did all 4 things you asked. Everything is committed and pushed, and both repos match GitHub.\n\n**1. Roster (Option B): done.**\n- I removed the 7 `\"off\"` lines from `~/.claude/settings.json`, commit `21c686d`.\n- The 7 skills showed up in this session's skill list right away.\n- The checker now reports 42 skills, 0 failing, and `portability_failures=0`.\n\n**2. Pi trial: paused.** I recorded this in `docs/STATUS.md` and the execution log.\n\n**3. Audit: run.** The report is `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`.\n- 10 layers were checked by read-only helpers, and nothing was changed. The Skills layer was audited on 9/12, so it counted as green.\n- Every row in `rot.md` now has a date, with a scope note where the check was partial.\n- **2 RED findings:**\n  - The Codex copy of the session-start hook (`keystone-unified-snapshot.js`) is an old 31-line version. Codex sessions start without your profile or memory.\n  - The GPS database hasn't changed since 8/1, before the season started.\n- **Other findings:**\n  - The `memory-write` skill still says Windows is retired.\n  - `dcg` runs twice on every shell command.\n  - The vault scored 79/100 and has stale project notes.\n- I fixed one stale memory line: the note that said the 7 skills were off.\n\n**4. Codex review: 5 rounds**, on `gpt-5.6-terra` at `high` effort for the last three.\n- Rounds 1–4 found real bugs: C-01 to C-03, IR-01, IR-03, IR-05, part of IR-04, and one stale `STATUS.md` line. All are fixed and tested on this Mac.\n- Your real skills still pass, 42 of 42.\n- Round 5 came back REVISE. Its two claims (IR-06, IR-07) are wrong for PyYAML. I tested them: PyYAML and the checker agree on both values. The claims only hold for an npm YAML library's 1.1 mode, and none of your 3 harnesses use that mode.\n- The runner also marked round 5 `failed`, because I committed docs while it ran. Only docs changed, so the verdict still applies to the final checker. I stopped there, as agreed.\n\n**You decide: 3 things.**\n\n1. **Audit build 1: copy the current hook over the Codex copy, and fix the \"Windows retired\" text.** It is one file copy and two text edits, and you can undo it. The audit rules don't let me do it without asking.\n   - **Option A:** Yes, do it.\n   - **Option B:** Not now.\n   - **My pick:** A.\n2. **GPS:** where do GPS sessions land since 8/24? In `DataBase_GPS_Reporting`, `Catapult_API`, or somewhere else?\n3. **Round 5 findings:**\n   - **Option A:** Accept the checker as it is. It follows PyYAML and YAML 1.2, which is how your harnesses actually load skills.\n   - **Option B:** Make it also follow the npm library's 1.1 mode. It gets stricter, but some valid names would be rejected.\n   - **My pick:** A.\n\nresult: The 7 skills are back on in Claude Code, the Pi trial is paused, and the first AI OS audit is done (2 RED: stale Codex hook, GPS feed) — all committed and pushed; 5 Codex rounds ran, bugs from rounds 1–4 are fixed, and 3 decisions wait on you."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1049,"cache_read_input_tokens":400150,"output_tokens":1295,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":109},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1049,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1295,"cache_read_input_tokens":400150,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1049,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1049},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"re