{"parentUuid":"4423b230-04aa-4d21-be25-80474266ca91","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0fe7818e-8df1-47a7-8f51-80020aa241f5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ArWvpMtjSUU4iVMW6HSa6k","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/handoff-2026-09-13-aios-audit-decisions.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"197202df-f716-4ad0-a3d4-0aec7b2a1a25","timestamp":"2026-09-13T14:30:54.604Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/handoff-2026-09-13-aios-audit-decisions.md","content":"# Handoff — AIOS plan after the first audit and Codex rounds 3–5 (2026-09-13)\n\nPicked up from: `/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/handoff-2026-09-13-aios-gate-c.md`\n\n## Read these first (they hold the detail — do not duplicate)\n\n- Current state and next steps: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md`\n- Execution log, every gate and Codex round with evidence: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md` (sections from \"Gate C — round 1\" to the end)\n- First audit report: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`\n- Layer receipts: `~/.claude/rot.md` (copy: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/rot.md`)\n- Test scripts and Codex notes kept as evidence: `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/evidence/2026-09-13-gate-c/README.md` (read its side-effects column before running anything)\n- Plan (approved, **do not edit**, SHA-256 `71b5242e…`): `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`\n- Pi trial report (paused): `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-12-pi-trial.md`\n- Git: `git -C ~/DEV/KeystoneOS log --oneline 08bf6e8..a5f19b3`; `~/.claude` commits `21c686d` (roster), `fe3c6aa` (memory)\n\n## State\n\n- Everything is committed and pushed. KeystoneOS HEAD `a5f19b3`; `~/.claude` clean for `settings.json` and the DEV memory folder.\n- Roster Option B is done (7 skills re-enabled in Claude Code). Checker 42/42; all metrics invariants 0.\n- Task 8 (Pi trial) is **paused by Eric**. Do not start it.\n- Codex: 5 rounds. The last (round 5) returned REVISE with IR-06/IR-07; host checks show both hold only for the npm `yaml` library's 1.1 mode, not PyYAML or YAML 1.2 core. Runner marked it `failed` because docs were committed mid-inspection. **Eric declared round 5 the stop** (via the session plan) — no more rounds without asking.\n\n## Waiting on Eric (asked at the end of the session, no answer yet)\n\n1. **Audit build 1** — copy `~/.claude/hooks/keystone-unified-snapshot.js` (98 lines) over the stale 31-line `~/.codex/hooks/` copy, and fix the \"Windows retired 2026-08-14\" text in `~/.claude/skills/memory-write/SKILL.md` (~lines 80, 101) and `~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_backup-sync-system.md`. Recommended: yes. The audit skill forbids doing it unasked.\n2. **GPS feed** — where do sessions land since 2026-08-24? `DataBase_GPS_Reporting/gps_report/data/gps_history.duckdb` was last modified 2026-08-01; `Catapult_API/` has JSON from 09-06 that looks like sample data.\n3. **IR-06/IR-07** — accept the checker (PyYAML + YAML 1.2 core; recommended) or widen it to also match npm `yaml` 1.1 mode.\n\nOther audit proposals (double `dcg` registration in `~/.claude/settings.json`, stale counts in `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md`, `brain-audit` `measure.sh` sort bug, vault note rot, `status-report` asking >2 questions under ELI5, USER.md stale pointers) are listed in the audit report. None applied.\n\n## Traps met this session\n\n- `dcg` blocks shell `>` redirects into home paths, even with absolute paths. Use a Python file that opens the output itself (see `~/.claude/jobs/9823c1f0/tmp/launch-inspect-r5.py` pattern). Saved to memory `project_dcg-guard-blocks.md`.\n- **Never commit to KeystoneOS while a `claudex-loop` inspection runs** — the runner fails the round. Now a gotcha in `STATUS.md`.\n- `aios-audit` is a KeystoneOS project skill. From a `~/DEV`-rooted session it is not listed; read its `SKILL.md` and follow it by hand.\n- Codex models on this Mac (`~/.codex/models_cache.json`): `gpt-5.6-terra` at `--effort high` worked well for narrow reviews (~90–165 s). Rounds share one quota.\n- `claude -p --disallowedTools Bash` does not block context-mode MCP shell tools (memory `project_headless-claude-tool-deny-gap.md`).\n- Job tmp folders (`~/.claude/jobs/9823c1f0/tmp`, `…/c59d1788/tmp`) are deleted with their jobs; durable copies of the evidence are in the repo.\n\n## Suggested skills\n\n- `memory-write` — if build 1 is approved, the Windows-retired correction touches its own SKILL.md and a memory file; follow its tier and dedup rules.\n- `CreateSkill` — required before editing any `~/.claude/skills/*` file (the `memory-write` fix, or the `status-report` question count).\n- `update-config` — before removing the duplicate `dcg` hook entry in `~/.claude/settings.json`.\n- `claude-stack-doctor` — to re-verify the hooks after syncing the Codex copy.\n- `superpowers:verification-before-completion` — before claiming any of the above done.\n- `claudex-loop` — only if Eric asks for another Codex round.\n- `closeout` — at session end (STATUS update, commit, push).\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4423b230-04aa-4d21-be25-80474266ca91","session_id":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
