{"parentUuid":"244f5d9a-3b6c-4956-ac95-814fc0c8f757","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:resume","toolUseID":"8910e9ac-859b-4d2d-a569-817741a9d91b","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\\n# User Profile\\n\\n## About\\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\\n\\n## Preferences\\n- Python/R. Two machines: Windows by day, Mac by evening (split 9/24). Tool paths: machine.md.\\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\\n\\n## Working Style\\n- Direct; says \\\"stop\\\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \\\"sharpened, not soothed.\\\"\\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\\n# Working Memory\\n\\n## Active Threads (max 5; park one to add one)\\n- **Status report**: biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\\n- **SW/Tech Review (10/1)**: Erin asked; NEXT Teams 10/2, ET by 11/30. →`SoftwareTech_Review/docs/`\\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: q2wk to a named user: RI5 #002 wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23. →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- **PP Recruiting (9/30)**: 017 sent-ready; 018 SHIP. NEXT send 018, walkthrough. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 built. NEXT Tim/Jacob export; Joe → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\\n\\n## Parked (NEXT lives in each STATUS.md; `where-was-i.py` lists them)\\n- Prioritization slate LIVE 5/5 →Tier A prioritization-slate\\n- Personal site: scroll-craft LOCAL, Artifact live →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\\n- FB matchups: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py` →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026`\\n- Flint: NEXT Eric: OneDrive keep/drop, 2 verify →`Flint`\\n- 42Analytics: NEXT captions (429s) on Mac →`42Analytics`\\n- VB GRID: fix merged 10/2 (#2); await Mike's reply →`Volleyball_GRID`\\n- Sleep sched: NEXT night/early-kickoff →`sleep-scheduler`\\n- TypeSafe: MAINTENANCE; PR #31 merged as record →`TypeSafe_Sandbox`\\n\\n## Environment Notes\\n- Machine split (9/24): Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD.\\n- Hooks: patch both copies for shared events. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\\n- Win: Drive sync, junction and renv traps →machine.md. PFF: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB; `PFF_DB`.\\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches unasked (verify) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\\n- Sessions: start `where-was-i.py`, prune with `session-sweep.py` →Tier A session-hygiene.\\n\\n## Pending Decisions\\n- None open. (OKR gate + OKRs_2026-27 CLOSED 10/2: Eric not developing further.)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\\n\\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4310 chars, updated 2026-10-02 11:26)\"}}","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading unified cross-harness snapshot...","durationMs":603},"type":"attachment","uuid":"42b926b7-489f-4f1f-907e-195e1d1e94be","timestamp":"2026-10-02T21:52:58.275Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"42b926b7-489f-4f1f-907e-195e1d1e94be","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:resume","toolUseID":"8910e9ac-859b-4d2d-a569-817741a9d91b","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\", \"additionalContext\": \"## Today\\nFriday, October 02, 2026\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Knowledge Base\\n\\n319 compiled articles (237 concepts, 81 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here \\u2014 read it only when a question actually needs it:\\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \\\"<query>\\\" --top-k 5`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recent Daily Log\\n\\n- Still-open hook failures in `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`: `perch-pull` exit 1 (10/1, log at `~/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json`), `daily-backup` `manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics`, and the KeystoneOS AI OS audit is due.\\n\\n**Artifacts:**\\n- Handoff: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/CFB_Victory_Model/docs/handoffs/2026-10-02-week4-capture.md`\\n- STATUS: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/CFB_Victory_Model/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- Pushed: `CFB_Victory_Model` (16 snapshots + log), `CFB_Forecast_Archive` (snapshot copies + comparison), `~/.claude/global-memory`, `~/.claude`\\n\\n### Session (16:50)\\n\\n**Context:** Mac evening session \\u2014 checked whether the 5 Claude Code mods synced from Windows were active on the Mac, then enabled them.\\n\\n**Key Exchanges:**\\n- Asked if \\\"the Claude mods we made earlier\\\" were visible. Answer: the files were present at `~/.claude/mods/` (`repo-band`, `next-steps`, `job-watch`, `merge-cleanup`, `where`), synced over via the `~/.claude` repo, but not loaded \\u2014 `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` was unset on the Mac.\\n- Clarified a boundary: mods render UI (bands, buttons, status line, toasts) to the user's screen only. Their output does not enter the agent's context, so the user sees them and Claude does not.\\n\\n**Decisions Made:**\\n- User approved enabling the mods on the Mac. Added the `export CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS=...` line (all 5 mod paths, colon-separated) to `~/.zshrc`, with a backup of the prior file at `~/.claude/jobs/a70d9b79/tmp/zshrc.bak`.\\n\\n**Lessons Learned:**\\n- `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` is per-machine by design (per the mods README) \\u2014 it was only ever set on Windows, so repo-synced mods arrive dormant on a new machine. Expect this on any future machine.\\n- `job-watch` is cross-platform: it reads Mac jobs via `launchctl`, so no Mac-specific fix was needed despite Mac/Windows storing scheduled jobs differently.\\n- All 5 mods passed `claude plugin validate` on the Mac.\\n- An already-open terminal will not pick up the new env var \\u2014 a fresh terminal window is required.\\n\\n**Action Items:**\\n- User must quit Claude Code, open a **new** terminal window, and start `claude` to load the mods. Expected: `repo-band` dirty/unpushed band, `next-steps` buttons, `job-watch` status line, and the `/repos`, `/jobs`, `/where` commands.\\n- If nothing appears, check the Claude Code \\\"rollout switch\\\" that can block mods (README notes it was only observed blocking headless runs, not normal sessions).\\n- Startup hook failures still open: `perch-pull` exit 1 (log at `~/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json`), `daily-backup` errors `repo-behind-blocked:global-memory` and `manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics`.\\n- `~/.zshrc` change is machine-local and not covered by the `~/.claude` repo sync \\u2014 the Windows laptop needs no action, but a future machine will.\\n\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading knowledge base...","durationMs":608},"type":"attachment","uuid":"687991f5-d648-4e1b-91f5-fcfad0ee35b2","timestamp":"2026-10-02T21:52:58.278Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"687991f5-d648-4e1b-91f5-fcfad0ee35b2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:resume","toolUseID":"8910e9ac-859b-4d2d-a569-817741a9d91b","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"\\n<context_window_protection>\\n  <priority_instructions>\\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\\n  </priority_instructions>\\n\\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \\\"timeline\\\")\\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\\n       - Each command: {label: \\\"section header\\\", command: \\\"shell command\\\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\\\"q1\\\", \\\"q2\\\", ...])\\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n\\n  <when_not_to_use>\\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\\n  </when_not_to_use>\\n\\n  <file_writing_policy>\\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\\n  </file_writing_policy>\\n\\n  <output_constraints>\\n    <artifact_policy>\\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\\n    </artifact_policy>\\n  </output_constraints>\\n  <session_continuity>\\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\\n  </session_continuity>\\n\\n  <ctx_commands>\\n    \\\"ctx stats\\\" | \\\"ctx-stats\\\" | \\\"/ctx-stats\\\" | context savings question\\n    → Call stats MCP tool, display full output verbatim.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx doctor\\\" | \\\"ctx-doctor\\\" | \\\"/ctx-doctor\\\" | diagnose context-mode\\n    → Call doctor MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx upgrade\\\" | \\\"ctx-upgrade\\\" | \\\"/ctx-upgrade\\\" | update context-mode\\n    → Call upgrade MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx purge\\\" | \\\"ctx-purge\\\" | \\\"/ctx-purge\\\" | wipe/reset knowledge base\\n    → Call purge MCP tool with confirm: true. Warn: irreversible.\\n\\n    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: \\\"context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use `ctx purge` to start fresh.\\\"\\n  </ctx_commands>\\n\\n</context_window_protection>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/sessionstart.mjs\"","durationMs":608},"type":"attachment","uuid":"37dbd1ef-38c3-40eb-baa4-c41cb28534c5","timestamp":"2026-10-02T21:52:58.279Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
