f the prior file at `~/.claude/jobs/a70d9b79/tmp/zshrc.bak`.\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` is per-machine by design (per the mods README) — it was only ever set on Windows, so repo-synced mods arrive dormant on a new machine. Expect this on any future machine.\n- `job-watch` is cross-platform: it reads Mac jobs via `launchctl`, so no Mac-specific fix was needed despite Mac/Windows storing scheduled jobs differently.\n- All 5 mods passed `claude plugin validate` on the Mac.\n- An already-open terminal will not pick up the new env var — a fresh terminal window is required.\n\n**Action Items:**\n- User must quit Claude Code, open a **new** terminal window, and start `claude` to load the mods. Expected: `repo-band` dirty/unpushed band, `next-steps` buttons, `job-watch` status line, and the `/repos`, `/jobs`, `/where` commands.\n- If nothing appears, check the Claude Code \"rollout switch\" that can block mods (README notes it was only observed blocking headless runs, not normal sessions).\n- Startup hook failures still open: `perch-pull` exit 1 (log at `~/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json`), `daily-backup` errors `repo-behind-blocked:global-memory` and `manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics`.\n- `~/.zshrc` change is machine-local and not covered by the `~/.claude` repo sync — the Windows laptop needs no action, but a future machine will.\n"],"hookName":"SessionStart","toolUseID":"SessionStart","hookEvent":"SessionStart"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5c9a49be-31c0-4ab1-8654-552791c10a89","timestamp":"2026-10-02T21:52:58.354Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nSessionStart hook additional context: ## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\n# User Profile\n\n## About\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\n\n## Preferences\n- Python/R. Two machines: Windows by day, Mac by evening (split 9/24). Tool paths: machine.md.\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\n\n## Working Style\n- Direct; says \"stop\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \"sharpened, not soothed.\"\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\n\n---\n\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\n# Working Memory\n\n## Active Threads (max 5; park one to add one)\n- **Status report**: biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\n- **SW/Tech Review (10/1)**: Erin asked; NEXT Teams 10/2, ET by 11/30. →`SoftwareTech_Review/docs/`\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: q2wk to a named user: RI5 #002 wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23. →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **PP Recruiting (9/30)**: 017 sent-ready; 018 SHIP. NEXT send 018, walkthrough. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 built. NEXT Tim/Jacob export; Joe → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\n\n## Parked (NEXT lives in each STATUS.md; `where-was-i.py` lists them)\n- Prioritization slate LIVE 5/5 →Tier A prioritization-slate\n- Personal site: scroll-craft LOCAL, Artifact live →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\n- FB matchups: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py` →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026`\n- Flint: NEXT Eric: OneDrive keep/drop, 2 verify →`Flint`\n- 42Analytics: NEXT captions (429s) on Mac →`42Analytics`\n- VB GRID: fix merged 10/2 (#2); await Mike's reply →`Volleyball_GRID`\n- Sleep sched: NEXT night/early-kickoff →`sleep-scheduler`\n- TypeSafe: MAINTENANCE; PR #31 merged as record →`TypeSafe_Sandbox`\n\n## Environment Notes\n- Machine split (9/24): Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD.\n- Hooks: patch both copies for shared events. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\n- Win: Drive sync, junction and renv traps →machine.md. PFF: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB; `PFF_DB`.\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches unasked (verify) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\n- Sessions: start `where-was-i.py`, prune with `session-sweep.py` →Tier A session-hygiene.\n\n## Pending Decisions\n- None open. (OKR gate + OKRs_2026-27 CLOSED 10/2: Eric not developing further.)\n\n---\n\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\n\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4310 chars, updated 2026-10-02 11:26)\n## Today\nFriday, October 02, 2026\n\n---\n\n## Knowledge Base\n\n319 compiled articles (237 concepts, 81 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here — read it only when a question actually needs it:\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5`\n\n---\n\n## Recent Daily Log\n\n- Still-open hook failures in `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`: `perch-pull` exit 1 (10/1, log at `~/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json`), `daily-backup` `manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics`, and the KeystoneOS AI OS audit is due.\n\n**Artifacts:**\n- Handoff: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/CFB_Victory_Model/docs/handoffs/2026-10-02-week4-capture.md`\n- STATUS: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/CFB_Victory_Model/docs/STATUS.md`\n- Pushed: `CFB_Victory_Model` (16 snapshots + log), `CFB_Forecast_Archive` (snapshot copies + comparison), `~/.claude/global-memory`, `~/.claude`\n\n### Session (16:50)\n\n**Context:** Mac evening session — checked whether the 5 Claude Code mods synced from Windows were active on the Mac, then enabled them.\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- Asked if \"the Claude mods we made earlier\" were visible. Answer: the files were present at `~/.claude/mods/` (`repo-band`, `next-steps`, `job-watch`, `merge-cleanup`, `where`), synced over via the `~/.claude` repo, but not loaded — `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` was unset on the Mac.\n- Clarified a boundary: mods render UI (bands, buttons, status line, toasts) to the user's screen only. Their output does not enter the agent's context, so the user sees them and Claude does not.\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- User approved enabling the mods on the Mac. Added the `export CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS=...` line (all 5 mod paths, colon-separated) to `~/.zshrc`, with a backup of the prior file at `~/.claude/jobs/a70d9b79/tmp/zshrc.bak`.\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` is per-machine by design (per the mods README) — it was only ever set on Windows, so repo-synced mods arrive dormant on a new machine. Expect this on any future machine.\n- `job-watch` is cross-platform: it reads Mac jobs via `launchctl`, so no Mac-specific fix was needed despite Mac/Windows storing scheduled jobs differently.\n- All 5 mods passed `claude plugin validate` on the Mac.\n- An already-open terminal will not pick up the new env var — a fresh terminal window is required.\n\n**Action Items:**\n- User must quit Claude Code, open a **new** terminal window, and start `claude` to load the mods. Expected: `repo-band` dirty/unpushed band, `next-steps` buttons, `job-watch` status line, and the `/repos`, `/jobs`, `/where` commands.\n- If nothing appears, check the Claude Code \"rollout switch\" that can block mods (README notes it was only observed blocking headless runs, not normal sessions).\n- Startup hook failures still open: `perch-pull` exit 1 (log at `~/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json`), `daily-backup` errors `repo-behind-blocked:global-memory` and `manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics`.\n- `~/.zshrc` change is machine-local and not covered by the `~/.claude` repo sync — the Windows laptop needs no action, but a future machine will.\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
